PVD("sri_lanka_vision_2019-2030",{"docs":["","1940_Sri_Lanka_Sustainable_Sri_Lanka_2030_Vision_and_Strategic_Path_2019_PEC"],"s":{"1":[[1,"115","5","Innovation Education Experimentation and Adaptation Space","What is needed is space for experimentation and adaptation in innovation education.",""],[1,"115","5","Secondary-Level Magnet Schools","Sri Lanka could create space for a few \"magnet schools\" with various specializations and different admission criteria that can exist as islands of diversity within the school systems at the secondary level.",""],[1,"115","5","Industry-Collaborative Magnet School Operation","Ideally, they will be operated in close collaboration with industry associations who will provide the linkages to companies and possibly provide some of the financing.",""],[1,"115","5","Tertiary Innovation Initiatives","At the tertiary level, a variety of initiatives could be launched, that learn from, and build upon the experience gained over several years at the University of Moratuwa",""],[1,"116","8","Technical, Professional and Vocational Education Pathways at Upper Secondary Level","promote technical, professional and vocational education opportunities, as an alternative pathway at upper secondary stage of school education.",""],[1,"116","9","Curriculum Diversification and Modernization","Diversify and modernize the curriculum in order to address present and future demands in the local and international labour markets.",""],[1,"116","9","Technology-Enhanced Learning Promotion","The use of modern technologies should be encouraged to enhance learning.",""],[1,"116","10","Outcome-Based Curriculum Reform","Establish a better-articulated outcome based curriculum integrating and embedding skills (cognitive and well as socio-emotional) focusing on the underlying objective that all children should be successful learners, confident individuals, responsible citizens and effective contributors (Singapore and Scotland share this focus).",""],[1,"116","11","Curriculum Reform for Civic and Social Harmony","Promote a school system that, through the curriculum, lays a strong social and cultural foundation that promotes multi-ethnic and multi-religious harmony and encourages strong civic values, ethics and patterns of behavior consistent with a strong democracy and social justice system.",""],[1,"116","12","Promotion of International Languages, STEM, and Professional Subjects","Promote international languages (e.g. English), STEM subjects (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) and professional subjects (e.g. medicine, engineering, para- medicine etc.) that will help employability.",""],[1,"116","12","Integration of Arts with STEM Education","Knowledge of the arts must be encouraged and linked to the STEM subjects.",""],[1,"116","13","School-to-Tertiary Education Linkage Strengthening","Strengthen vertical and horizontal linkages between school education and tertiary/higher education sectors.",""],[1,"117","11","Curriculum-Integrated Assessment Reform","Improve attainment of learning outcomes in the classroom and make assessment an essential part of the curriculum not separated from learning and teaching.",""],[1,"117","12","International Benchmarking of GCE Qualifications","Benchmark GCE OL and AL qualifications with international examinations.",""],[1,"117","14","English Language Curriculum and Textbook Review and Improvement","Review and improve the primary and secondary English language curriculum and textbooks.",""],[1,"118","11","Young Professionals Development Programme","Promote development of young professionals at different levels (i.e. school, zonal, provincial and, national).",""]],"2":[[1,"35","8","Independent and Non-Aligned Foreign Policy","Sri Lanka continues to conduct its foreign relations in an independent and non-aligned manner, and pursues its foreign policy with the aim to make Sri Lanka safer and more prosperous through beneficial bilateral and multi-stakeholder partnerships.",""],[1,"36","4","Economic Diplomacy Initiative","Vigorously pursue economic diplomacy initiatives to bolster the economy, enhance development activities and attract foreign investors and traders to the country, taking advantage of the positive international focus on Sri Lanka.",""],[1,"36","7","Public Diplomacy and Media Image Promotion","Further focus on facilitating negotiations related to the fishermen issue while countering misinformation propagated by certain diaspora elements through think-tank intervention by promoting Sri Lanka's image through media and practice of public diplomacy.",""],[1,"36","9","Proactive International Engagement and UN Leadership","Take a more pro-active role on the international stage and at the United Nations in keeping with independent Sri Lanka's traditional leadership role in the G-77, transitioning from a country under scrutiny by the international community to a global role model on human rights and reconciliation.",""],[1,"45","5","Economic Diplomacy and International Partnership Support","Work with international organisations and bilateral donor countries will strengthen & expand relationship to secure financial and technical support, for development.",""],[1,"45","5","Economic Diplomacy Initiative to Attract Investment and Trade","By pursuing economic diplomacy initiatives to bolster the economy, development activities will be enhanced while attracting foreign investors and traders to the country, taking advantage of the positive international focus on Sri Lanka.",""],[1,"82","10","Regional Cooperation Expansion with Asian Neighbours","Expand relations with growing Asian neighbours to take advantage of regional initiatives such as China's One-Belt-One-Road (OBOR) programme",""],[1,"82","11","Engagement with New Development Finance Institutions","Engage with new agencies such as the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) to access new forms of development finance",""],[1,"239","7","Indian Ocean Regional Cooperation through IORA","Sri Lanka's active role in IORA is aimed to ensure maritime safety and security, protection of ocean",""],[1,"241","6","Multi-Sectoral Cross-Border Cooperation","Strengthen multi-sectoral cooperation with close neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"241","7","Far-East Asian Partnership Strengthening and Maritime Security Dialogue","Strengthen relations with traditionally friendly Far-East Asian partners with comprehensive partnership and the inaugural bilateral dialogue on maritime security, safety and oceanic Issues.",""],[1,"241","8","North America Cooperation Engagement","Interact and engage with friendly nations in North America to further consolidate cooperation.",""],[1,"241","9","Regular United Nations Engagement","Engage with the United Nations, including high level exchanges on a regular basis.",""],[1,"241","10","Expansion of International Ties","Strengthen and expand ties with countries in Australasia, South East Asia and Africa.",""],[1,"241","11","SAARC Regional Cooperation Deepening","Deepen ties with counterparts in the SAARC region.",""],[1,"241","12","Bilateral Relations Development with European Countries","Continue efforts to develop bilateral relations with countries in the European Region.",""],[1,"241","14","Fishermen Negotiation Facilitation and Public Diplomacy Initiative","The Government of Sri Lanka should further focus on facilitating negotiations related to the issues of fishermen while countering misinformation propagated by certain diaspora elements through think-tank intervention by promoting Sri Lanka's image through media and the practice of public diplomacy.",""],[1,"241","16","International Development Cooperation and Resource Mobilization","Assist in the realization of SDG 17 (means of implementation) by working with international organizations, such as UNCTAD, UNDP, FAO, WFP, UNDO & financial institutions, and most importantly with the bilateral donor countries from the West, using our recently strengthened and expanded relationship to secure financial and technical support, for development.",""],[1,"242","2","Donor Coordination for Inclusive Sustainable Industrial Development","Help bridge bilateral and multilateral donors in intensifying efforts towards inclusive sustainable industrial development (SDG-09) as Sri Lanka's industrial base expands with increasing economic activity and investment.",""],[1,"242","2","North-South Technical Cooperation Facilitation","North-South Cooperation remains an important mode of facilitation of technical knowledge.",""],[1,"242","2","South-South Cooperation for Economic Advancement","Sri Lanka's leadership, as a robust and resilient trade and maritime hub providing connectivity between East and West, could help leverage South-South cooperation for economic advancement.",""],[1,"304","10","Indian Ocean Regional Cooperation Promotion","C. Promote Indian Ocean based regional cooperation as a priority in the Sri Lankan Foreign Policy.",""],[1,"304","10","Active Participation in the Indian Ocean Rim Association","The country's active role in the Indian Ocean Rim Association (ORA) is aimed to ensure maritime safety and security, protection of ocean related resources and freedom of navigation, and to reap the benefits of a Blue Economy.",""],[1,"305","2","Public Diplomacy and Media Image Promotion Initiative","Further focus on facilitating negotiations related to the fishermen issue while countering misinformation propagated by certain diaspora elements through think-tank intervention, by promoting Sri Lanka's image through the media and through the practice of public diplomacy.",""],[1,"305","4","International Development Cooperation for SDG 17 Support","Assist in the realization of SDG 17 (means of implementation) by working with international organizations such as the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO), WFP, United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) & financial institutions, most importantly with the bilateral donor countries from the West, using our recently strengthened and expanded relationship to secure financial and technical support for development.",""],[1,"305","6","Donor Bridging for Inclusive Sustainable Industrial Development","Help bridge bilateral and multilateral donors in intensifying efforts towards inclusive, sustainable industrial development (SDG 9),",""],[1,"305","6","North-South Technical Cooperation Facilitation","While North-South cooperation remains an important mode of facilitation of technical knowledge, Sri Lanka's leadership as a robust and resilient trade and maritime hub providing connectivity between East and West, could help leverage South-South cooperation for economic advancement.",""]],"3":[[1,"7","4","Public Consensus Building for Sustainable Sri Lanka 2030 Vision","The Sustainable Development Council will build on the public consensus on the Sustainable Sri Lanka 2030 Vision document, in order to inform our way forward to make Sri Lanka a truly sustainable country by 2030.",""],[1,"8","3","National Economic Council Support for Vision Implementation","The National Economic Council, as the highest policy institution of the Government of Sri Lanka, welcomes the Sustainable Sri Lanka 2030 Vision and will support its successful implementation once adopted by Cabinet.",""],[1,"12","6","Inclusive Stakeholder Consultation Process for Vision Development","PEC team members who are fully conversant with the range of sustainable development topics, will continue to follow an inclusive process by systematically consulting all relevant stakeholders, thereby ensuring wide ownership of the emerging path towards the vision of Sri Lanka in 2030.",""],[1,"17","2","Educational, Language, and Decentralization Programmes for Social Cohesion","Persisting ethnic tensions that threaten national unity and peace need to be defused through effective educational, language and decentralization policies and programmes.",""],[1,"17","2","School and Community Social Cohesion Programmes","Social cohesion should be promoted through school and community level programmes.",""],[1,"17","5","National and Community Reconciliation Programme","Formulate and implement a comprehensive, multi-level program of reconciliation at national and community levels.",""],[1,"38","6","National Reconciliation Process","To launch, entrench and then solidify a national reconciliation process a generation or more of effort, extending across successive Government mandates, will be required.",""],[1,"39","3","Reconciliation Agenda Implementation Package","Rapidly fulfil key outstanding commitments related to the reconciliation agenda, including the establishment of an effective Office of Missing Persons (OMP), an enhanced reparations system, a Truth and Reconciliation Commission (TRC), and a credible judicial mechanism to prosecute allegations of the most serious crimes committed during the conflict.",""],[1,"39","5","National Communications Strategy for Reforms and Reconciliation","Launch a comprehensive Communications Strategy to explain and sell proposed reforms and reconciliation efforts nationally, with full engagement of the President, Prime Minister and all members of Cabinet.",""],[1,"39","5","Conflict Reduction and Reconciliation Programmes","Launch programmes to diminish conflict and foster reconciliation in focus areas.",""],[1,"46","1","Support for Transitional Justice Mechanisms","Secretariat for the Coordination of Reconciliation Mechanisms will have supported the establishment of key transitional justice mechanisms.",""],[1,"46","1","National Reconciliation Policy and Action Plans","Policies and Action Plans, in addition to the National Reconciliation Policy will address issues such as violence against women, empowering female headed households, women's entrepreneurship development, and institutionalizing gender mainstreaming.",""],[1,"94","2","National Reconciliation Program","A coordinated national program of reconciliation is critically important to reduce ethno-religious tensions in the country in order to create a peaceful environment that is critically important to facilitate sustainable economic and social development.",""],[1,"94","2","Trilingual Policy Implementation","The government's trilingual policy needs to be implemented effectively through education, state institutions and state employment.",""],[1,"94","2","Reconciliation Mechanisms under UN HRC 30/1","The reconciliation mechanisms to be created pursuant to UN HRC 30/1 are a critical part of the reconciliation process.",""],[1,"96","7","National Unity and Reconciliation Support","Strengthening state and non-state agencies working in the areas of national unity and reconciliation among communities can also facilitate peace and harmony, a key prerequisite for protection and well - being of all citizens.",""],[1,"212","1","Interfaith Harmony Promotion Mechanisms","Interfaith mechanisms that promote common values and harmony, need to be encouraged.",""],[1,"212","2","Active Citizenship and National Identity Promotion","The State shall reinforce all patriotic forces by law, policy and spirit to explore the notion of active citizenship in Sri Lanka and what it means to be Sri Lankan, strengthen the notion of Sri Lankan identity identifying the values enriched by the nation's diverse cultural pluralism and heritage and thereby recognizing the existence of more than one religion, language and ethnicity in this country as the natural prerequisite for national coexistence.",""],[1,"212","9","Inter-religious and Inter-ethnic Appreciation Incentive Measures","the State must make every possible effort to incentivize inter- religious and inter-ethnic appreciation.",""],[1,"212","11","Intercultural Education and Language Learning Initiative","Social and historical education should strive towards promoting the understanding of the contributions of all communities towards the greatness of the country.",""],[1,"212","11","Cross-Community Cultural Exchange Programme","Sri Lankans should be able to understand and enjoy the traditions of other communities: learning each other's language; getting to know each other's festivities; exchanging cultural, musical, literary, culinary knowledge, etc.",""],[1,"214","5","Promoting Active Citizenship Project","\"Promoting Active Citizenship\" (PAC) project, the pilot program of SFCG Sri Lanka aims at a transformed Hill Country culture in which young people are equipped and inspired to face their community's challenges through dialogue and building relationships with decision makers, actively engaging in the community, and advocating for their rights and the rights of their people42.",""],[1,"214","8","Open Dialogue Platforms for Social Engagement","the open dialogue platforms will provide an arena for active social engagement",""],[1,"216","2","Transitional Justice and National Healing Mechanisms","The transitional justice mechanisms planned by the current Government will contribute to defining this shared history and national healing, allowing all communities to feel understood and be proudly Sri Lankan.",""],[1,"216","4","Youth and Religious Leader Civic Communication Campaign","New communication technology will be used to challenge all identified negative features of our society and institutions especially through the activism of youth groups, and the leadership of enlightened religious leaders.",""],[1,"226","4","Implementation of Missing Persons Tracing Legislation","Already, legislation has been enacted on the tracing of missing persons, and this must be implemented without delay with adequate and effective - state and people support for implementation.",""],[1,"226","4","Strengthening or Establishing Justice Institutions","The current challenge is to strengthen existing institutions or create new ones that will restore the confidence of alleged victims of such violence their families and the general public in the administration of justice by local domestic institutions.",""],[1,"226","4","Credible Environment for Investigation, Prosecution, and Law Enforcement","The focus should be on creating a credible environment for effective investigation, prosecution, judicial decision making and law enforcement according to core norms of good governance and the rule of law.",""],[1,"257","1","National Reconciliation Policy Framework","The National Reconciliation Policy adopted by the Council of Ministers in May 2017 will serve as the guidepost of principles and the framework for reconciliation work going forward.",""],[1,"257","11","Multi-pronged Reconciliation and Community Engagement Strategy","A multi-pronged strategy (starting with reconciliation, as discussed in the main text) that covers ethnic, linguistic and religious elements needs to be implemented.",""],[1,"257","11","Community Engagement Projects","Major community engagement projects are required.",""],[1,"261","1","Reconciliation and Long-Term Stability Institutions and Programmes","Creation of effective institutions and programmes to foster reconciliation and long-term stability, e.g. Office of Missing Persons (OMP), a comprehensive reparations programme and a credible Truth and Reconciliation Commission.",""],[1,"261","6","Truth and Reconciliation Commission","A well-run Truth and Reconciliation Commission would make broad recommendations for institutional reform to ensure greater inclusiveness, accountability and fairness of institutions thus ensuring the non-recurrence of violence, while simultaneously fostering greater confidence in long-term stability and a better environment for investment and growth.",""],[1,"262","10","Women’s Engagement in Transitional Justice Mechanisms","Reconciliation efforts should consider the role of women and their engagement seriously and provide unique platforms for engagement, including in the transitional justice mechanisms envisioned, namely the Truth and Reconciliation Commission, a reparations scheme, the Office of Missing Persons and an accountability mechanism.",""],[1,"265","14","National Reconciliation Policy Implementation","The National Reconciliation Policy adopted by the Cabinet of Ministers in May 2017 will guide the overall direction and emphasis of the reconciliation agenda.",""],[1,"265","14","Secretariat Support for Transitional Justice Mechanisms","By 2020 the Secretariat for the Coordination of Reconciliation Mechanisms will have supported the establishment of key transitional justice mechanisms: The Office of Missing Persons (OMP); a truth and reconciliation commission (TRC); and an office of reparations will be fully operational by 2020, providing critical assistance to victims.",""],[1,"287","3","National and Community Reconciliation Program","Formulate and implement a comprehensive, multi-level program of reconciliation at national and community levels.",""],[1,"307","1","Reconciliation Agenda Implementation Package","Rapidly fulfil key outstanding commitments related to the reconciliation agenda, including the establishment of an effective Office of Missing Persons (OMP), an enhanced reparations system, a Truth and Reconciliation Commission (TRC), and a credible judicial mechanism to prosecute allegations of the most serious crimes committed during the conflict.",""],[1,"307","3","National Communications Strategy for Reforms and Reconciliation","Launch a comprehensive Communications Strategy to explain and sell proposed reforms and reconciliation efforts nationally, with full engagement of the President, Prime Minister and all members of Cabinet.",""],[1,"307","3","Conflict Reduction and Reconciliation Programmes","Launch programmes to diminish conflict and foster reconciliation in focus areas.",""],[1,"307","4","Military Occupied Land Handover and Restitution","Carry out the complete hand-over/restitution of military occupied lands in the North and East.",""],[1,"308","2","National Reconciliation Policy Implementation","The National Reconciliation Policy adopted by the Cabinet of Ministers in May 2017 will guide the overall direction and emphasis of the reconciliation agenda.",""],[1,"308","2","Secretariat for the Coordination of Reconciliation Mechanisms Support","By 2020, the Secretariat for the Coordination of Reconciliation Mechanisms will have supported the establishment of key transitional justice mechanisms: the OMP, a TRC, and an office of reparations will be fully operational by then, providing critical assistance to victims.",""],[1,"308","2","Domestic Judicial Mechanism for Past Atrocities","The legal framework for a domestic judicial mechanism to deal with the most serious crimes and atrocities of the past will be ready to be presented to the Parliament.",""],[1,"308","5","Military Land Restitution to Civilians","The restitution of lands held by the military to civilians ... will be close to completion by 2020.",""],[1,"308","5","Withdrawal of Military from Business Activities","the withdrawal of the military from business activities, will be close to completion by 2020.",""],[1,"308","6","Tamil Language Equality and Accessibility Measures","The government has taken important steps to give equal representation to the Tamil language in national life.",""]],"4":[[1,"34","3","Independent and Professional Public Institutions Strengthening","Strengthen the rule of law by supporting the creation and establishment of independent and professional institutions that can effectively serve the public, and by creating an understanding among politicians of the importance of such institutions for good governance.",""],[1,"34","4","Cross-Level Good Governance Strengthening Reform","Strengthen good governance strategy and structure that cuts across all levels (e.g. central, provincial and local) of public bodies/agencies, re-defining their scope, re-assigning specific roles, responsibilities and accountabilities, and empowering them with delegated authority independent of political intervention or influence.",""],[1,"34","5","Public Sector Ethics and Integrity Framework","Maintain a workplace culture with strong ethics and integrity as part of the governance framework and for good public sector performance.",""],[1,"34","6","Strengthen Government-Bureaucracy Accountability and Policy Implementation","Ensure clear and transparent relationships between the elected government and the bureaucracy to prevent any undue influence in the administration of public functions and to ensure swift and efficient implementation of government policies and strategies.",""],[1,"34","7","Public Sector Performance Monitoring and Evaluation System","Drive performance of the public sector with optimum effectiveness and efficiency, through performance monitoring and evaluation systems and process, both at an individual and organizational level and performance reporting.",""],[1,"34","8","Integrity and Trust Values Promotion Initiative","Promote and inculcate values such as integrity, trust,",""],[1,"45","3","Public Sector Governance and Performance Management Framework","A consistent policy framework for good governance by the public sector will help overcome the fundamental problems and ensure effective implementation.",""],[1,"78","8","Public Sector Reform for Improved Service Delivery","Include public sector (other than SOEs) reform for improved service delivery and reduced transaction costs, including corruption",""],[1,"78","11","Service Delivery Efficiency Improvement Measures","Promote adoption of innovative measures that increase the efficiency of service delivery.",""],[1,"229","4","Public Sector Performance Monitoring and Evaluation System","Drive performance of the public sector with optimum effectiveness and efficiency, through performance monitoring and evaluation systems, and process both at an individual and organizational level; and performance reporting.",""],[1,"230","1","Public Sector Performance Monitoring and Evaluation System","The public sector will be run with optimum effectiveness and efficiency, through performance monitoring and evaluation systems and process, both at an individual and organizational level and performance reporting.",""],[1,"235","1","Adapt Market Testing Infrastructure for Public Service Innovation Pilots","The infrastructure for market testing products and services can easily be adapted to piloting and evaluating innovations in delivery of government services to citizens, businesses and external actors.",""],[1,"235","2","Government Procedure Reengineering Initiatives","Reengineering of government procedures is an essential precondition and will require government-specific initiatives.",""],[1,"302","4","Support for Independent and Professional Public Institutions","Establish rule of law by supporting the creation of independent and professional institutions that can effectively serve the public, forming an understanding among politicians of the importance of such institutions for good governance.",""],[1,"303","1","Cross-Level Good Governance Reform","Establish a good governance strategy and structure that cuts across all levels (e.g. central, provincial and local) of public bodies/agencies, thereby re-defining their scope, re-assigning specific roles, responsibilities and accountabilities, and empowering them with delegated authority independent of political intervention or influence.",""],[1,"303","2","Public Sector Ethics and Integrity Framework","Maintain a workplace culture with strong ethics and integrity as part of the governance framework and for good public sector performance.",""],[1,"303","3","Government-Bureaucracy Coordination and Administrative Integrity Reform","Ensure clear and transparent relationships between the elected Government and the bureaucracy to prevent any undue influence in the administration of public functions and to ensure swift and efficient implementation of Government policies and strategies.",""],[1,"303","4","Public Sector Performance Monitoring and Evaluation System","Drive the performance of the public sector with optimum effectiveness and efficiency through performance monitoring and evaluation systems and processes, both at an individual and organizational level, and through performance reporting.",""],[1,"303","5","Public Service Values and Integrity Promotion","Promote and inculcate values such as integrity, trust, respect, directness, speed and transparency, and direct leadership across all levels of public servants.",""],[1,"303","6","Public Sector Governance and Decentralized Planning Reform","Decentralization of planning and plan implementation, adoption of the subsidiarity principle in the devolution of power, people's participation in governance at national, provincial and local levels and the empowerment of local councils, will change the highly centralized decision making structure that is presently in place.",""],[1,"303","7","Public Sector Performance Monitoring and Evaluation System","The public sector will be run with optimum effectiveness and efficiency through performance monitoring and evaluation systems and processes, both at an individual and organizational level, and performance reporting.",""]],"5":[[1,"36","2","International Counter-Terrorism Information and Intelligence Sharing","The Government continues to support related internal stakeholders to connect with other nations on these critical issues in order to find solutions for mutual benefit.",""],[1,"36","2","Draft Counter-Terrorism Legal Framework","A Draft Legal Framework for Counter Terrorism Act consistent with international human rights Norms and Standards is already under consideration.",""],[1,"39","8","National Security Policy Development","Establish a National Security Policy through a participatory mechanism that reflects the multiple security domains that the country is engaged in and the roles of different actors that safeguard our security (i.e. the state, the tri-forces and the new dimension of the citizenry guaranteeing its own security).",""],[1,"39","9","Maritime Domain Monitoring Enhancement","Comprehensively implement effective monitoring of Sri Lanka's maritime domain.",""],[1,"40","1","Defense Command, Control, Communications and Intelligence Capacity Enhancement","(Command, Control, Communications and Intelligence) capacities, naval and aviation capabilities and operational capacities need to be evaluated and enhanced.",""],[1,"40","2","Stricter Immigration and Border Security Policy","Implement a more stringent immigration policy and a more robust border security policy in order to combat Transnational Organized Crime.",""],[1,"40","3","Security Review Provision for Large-Scale Foreign Projects","Establish a Security Review Provision on Large Scale Foreign Projects under Sri Lankan law.",""],[1,"46","1","Dynamic National Security Model","A dynamic security model will be developed for Sri Lanka that can evolve with the trajectory of the threats facing our nation.",""],[1,"239","5","International Information and Intelligence Sharing on Counterterrorism","The Foreign Ministry continues to support related internal stakeholders to connect with other nations on these critical issues in order to find solutions for mutual benefit.","Foreign Ministry"],[1,"239","5","Draft Counterterrorism Legal Framework","A draft Legal Framework for Counter Terrorism Act consistent with international human rights norms and standards is already under consideration.",""],[1,"257","13","Maritime Domain Monitoring and ISR Upgrade","Effective monitoring of Sri Lanka's maritime domain must be comprehensively implemented.",""],[1,"258","1","Intelligence and Operational Capacity Enhancement","Intelligence) capacities, naval and aviation capabilities, and operational capacities need to be evaluated and enhanced.",""],[1,"258","3","Security Review Provision for Large-Scale Foreign Projects","A Security Review Provision should be established under Sri Lankan law, to assess the impact of Large Scale Foreign Projects on national security which includes impact on domestic manufacturing and service capacity, the stable operation of the national economy, basic societal order, impact on living conditions, etc.",""],[1,"258","11","Stricter Immigration Policy and Border Control Strengthening","Sri Lanka must implement a more stringent immigration policy and more effective border controls, supplemented by comprehensive training of border security officers and the police force.",""],[1,"258","11","Regional Security Cooperation and Maritime Surveillance Enhancement","Collaboration with countries in the region must be improved to ensure regional security, including better monitoring and surveillance of Sri Lanka's maritime borders and coastal areas to stop the flow of illicit drugs, weapons etc.",""],[1,"258","11","Security Force Equipment and Training Upgrade","The equipment and training of navy, coastguard and air force should be upgraded.",""],[1,"267","3","Comprehensive Defence and Security Policy","A comprehensive Defence and Security Policy should be in place by 2025, drafted through a participatory mechanism with input from think tanks, the parliament and other relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"307","6","National Security Policy Development","Establish a National Security Policy through a participatory mechanism that reflects the multiple security domains that the country is engaged in and the roles of different actors that safeguard our security (i.e. the state, the tri-forces and the new dimension of the citizenry guaranteeing its own security).",""],[1,"307","7","Maritime Domain Monitoring Enhancement","Comprehensively implement effective monitoring of Sri Lanka's maritime domain.",""],[1,"307","8","Stricter Immigration and Border Security Policy","Implement a more stringent immigration policy and a more robust border security policy in order to combat transnational organized crime.",""],[1,"307","9","Security Review Provision for Large-Scale Foreign Projects","Establish a Security Review Provision on large scale foreign projects under Sri Lankan law.",""],[1,"309","3","Pre-emptive National Security Institutional Design","The institutional structure should be designed to pre-emptively combat such threats.",""],[1,"309","5","Comprehensive Defense and Security Policy","A comprehensive Defense and Security Policy should be in place by 2025, drafted through a participatory mechanism with input from think tanks, the Parliament and other relevant stakeholders.",""]],"6":[[1,"39","4","Constitutional Reform and Political Accommodation Process","Articulate constitutional reforms acceptable to all communities or an alternative political accommodation equally acceptable to all.",""],[1,"57","2","Constitutional Reform Process","There is an ongoing reform process, to further strengthen and improve the constitution.",""],[1,"96","4","Constitutional Devolution of Governance Responsibilities","Constitutional reforms are needed to devolve governance responsibilities to provincial and local authorities in order to reduce centralized control in many fields.",""],[1,"96","7","Fundamental Rights and Economic and Social Rights Reform","Strengthen the chapter on fundamental rights in conformity with international treaty obligations and SDG's.",""],[1,"224","4","Constitutional Reform for Inclusive Governance","Constitutional reform that would respond to the negative aspects of the Constitution of 1978 which had emerged in over 30 years of experience since its enactment, resolving the national question by ensuring inclusive development and progress, balancing majority and minority community claims and interests in Sri Lanka's plural society.",""],[1,"224","6","Governance Institution Reform to Strengthen Professional Capacity","Reforms to the institutions of governance so as to eliminate political interference and develop professional capacity, in a manner that would restore the confidence of the people in public administration and the judiciary.",""],[1,"224","8","Legislative Institution Strengthening and Electoral Reform","Strengthening the legislative institutions and accountable use of national resources and finances, through electoral reform, effective power sharing between the Central government and provincial and local authorities.",""],[1,"224","9","Strengthening of the Bill of Fundamental Rights","Adopting a stronger Bill of Fundamental Rights of the people that would create obligations on state and non-state actors in conformity with Sri Lankans' obligations as a state that has ratified international treaties, and is also bound, like other nations by international law.",""],[1,"226","2","Constitutional Reform and Public Referendum Process","Reform of the Constitution that not merely tinkers with it, including more than the current 19 amendments, and with an active public campaign highlighting its key features, so that the people can decide at a Referendum whether to accept or reject it.",""],[1,"226","3","Constitutional Reform for Peace and Reconciliation","The constitutional reform process is also closely linked to another key aspect of good governance for the future - striving to heal the wounds of those who suffered most in the previous decades of violence.",""],[1,"227","1","Constitutional and Administrative Governance Reform","Constitutional and administrative reforms need to address these issues in order to create a conducive environment for sustainable development.",""],[1,"230","2","Constitutional Reform Process","The Constitutional reform process will help ensure peace, harmony and sustainable development.",""],[1,"266","3","Constitutional Reform for Provincial Development and Inclusion","Constitutional reform should contribute to greater investment and accelerated development in the provinces as well as acceptance of all communities of their full and equal place in a unified and democratic Sri Lanka, removing long-existing tensions and encouraging economic growth, security and stability.",""],[1,"303","8","Constitutional Reform Process","The constitutional reform process will help ensure peace and sustainable development.",""],[1,"307","2","Constitutional Reform and Political Accommodation Process","Articulate constitutional reforms acceptable to all communities or an alternative political accommodation equally acceptable to all.",""],[1,"308","4","Constitutional Reform for Provincial Development and Inclusion","Constitutional reform should contribute to greater investment and accelerated development in the provinces, as well as acceptance of all communities and their full and equal place in a unified and democratic Sri Lanka, removing long-existing tensions and encouraging economic growth, security and stability.",""]],"7":[[1,"152","1","International Environmental and Maritime Cooperation","Enhance collaboration and obtain cooperation from SAARC, SACEP, IMO, GLOBALLAST, etc.",""],[1,"152","6","Central Marine Affairs Governing Body","Therefore, it is imperative that the government establishes a central governing body for marine affairs and study the existing policies related to marine and coastal ecosystems and their management.",""],[1,"153","2","New Regulations for Key Marine Ecosystems and Threatened Species","Sri Lanka needs to update or develop new regulations for key marine ecosystems and threatened species.",""],[1,"153","10","National Level Coordination Committee for Marine and Coastal Ecosystem Management","Formulate a National Level Coordination Committee for marine and coastal ecosystem management.",""],[1,"154","1","National Marine and Coastal Ecosystem Management Policy Review and Reform","Conduct a national level policy review and reform on marine and coastal ecosystem management.",""],[1,"154","2","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Policy Implementation","Strengthen the capacity of relevant institutions to implement existing rules and regulations and future plans.",""],[1,"154","3","EEZ Zoning and Land Use Planning","Prepare zoning and land use plans for Sri Lankan EEZ with the participation of all stakeholders.",""],[1,"154","15","Marine Wildlife and Sensitive Marine Environment Regulation Reform","Revise regulations for marine mammal observation and introduce new regulations for privately owned turtle hatcheries, snorkelling, diving and boating in sensitive marine environments.",""],[1,"155","6","National Marine Ecosystem Services Awareness Programme","Formulate and implement national level awareness programmes targeting key stakeholders and the general public on the status of marine ecosystem services.",""],[1,"155","10","Alternative Land and Resource Provision to Prevent Encroachment","Provide alternative land and resources to counter encroachment and illegal land acquisition.",""],[1,"155","11","Effective Implementation of Existing National Legislation","Provide for effective implementation of existing national legislation.",""],[1,"155","12","Patrolling and Law Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity for patrolling and law enforcement.",""]],"8":[[1,"214","3","Public Communication Strategy for Accountability and Good Governance","This also means publicizing, critiquing and reacting publicly to acts of abuse of power, lawlessness, and corruption from any source.",""],[1,"215","7","Workshops for Women Bloggers","therefore, arranging workshops for women bloggers would be immensely useful for them to familiarise themselves with",""],[1,"216","4","Anti-Corruption Public Accountability Promotion","Publicizing, critiquing and not accepting without public reaction acts of abuse of power, lawlessness and corruption from any source will be promoted.",""],[1,"216","4","Right to Information and Media Freedom Strengthening","The right to information and media freedom will be strengthened.",""],[1,"226","2","Public Communication Strategy for Constitutional Reform","An effective communication strategy that will keep the public informed must be given maximum priority by the government and by all those who recognize the critical importance of constitutional reform for accountable governance and people-centric progress and development.",""],[1,"226","3","Community Awareness on Conflict Causes and Recurrence Prevention","This requires broadly based community awareness recognition and understanding of the root cause of our armed conflicts, and the need to prevent a recurrence of these conflicts.",""],[1,"226","4","Public Debate on Investigative Mechanisms","These proposals must also be placed before the public for debate and discussion, since there are many misconceptions regarding what should be investigative mechanisms for ascertaining facts and holding perpetrators of grave violations of rights of personal security and property, culpable for these violations.",""],[1,"301","3","Youth and Religious Leader Civic Activism through New Communication Technology","New communication technology will be used to challenge all identified negative features of our society and institutions, especially through the activism of youth groups and the guidance of enlightened religious leaders.",""],[1,"301","3","Public Accountability Campaign against Abuse of Power and Corruption","Acts of abuse of power, lawlessness and corruption from any source will not be accepted by the public, and will be publicized and critiqued.",""],[1,"301","3","Right to Information and Media Freedom Strengthening","The right to information and media freedom will be strengthened.",""]],"9":[[1,"119","1","TVET Programme Quality and Relevance Mechanism","Develop a systematic mechanism for quality and relevance of TVET sector programmes.",""],[1,"119","2","TVET Sector Reform for Labour Market Alignment","Support systematic reforms in the TVET sector particularly to match training supply with demand by creating strong linkages between training supply end users and market demands.",""],[1,"119","3","Private Sector Involvement in TVET On-the-Job Training","Promote private sector involvements (OJT) in the TVET sector.",""]],"10":[[1,"21","1","Country-wide Pre-Primary Education Service Delivery Network","Ensure a country-wide network of quality pre-primary education service delivery mechanism while providing children from low income households with publicly funded ECCE services.",""],[1,"21","2","Outcome-Based Curriculum Reform","Establish a better-articulated outcome based curriculum integrating and embedding skills (cognitive and well as socio-emotional) focusing on the underlying objective that all children should be successful learners, confident individuals, responsible citizens and effective contributors.",""],[1,"21","3","Teacher Professionalism and Training Improvement","Improve teacher professionalism, standards and training to use modern teaching-learning methods.",""],[1,"21","4","TVET Sector Reform and Labour Market Linkage Strengthening","Support systematic reforms in the TVET sector particularly to match training supply with demand by creating strong linkages between training supply end users and market demands.",""],[1,"21","5","University Curriculum Diversification and Modernization","Diversify and modernize the curriculum of universities and other higher education institutions in order to address present and future demands for social development and local and international labour markets.",""],[1,"119","13","University Curriculum Diversification and Modernization","Diversify and modernize the curriculum of universities and other higher education institutions in order to address present and future demands in the local and international labour markets.",""],[1,"119","14","Expansion of Tertiary and Higher Education Opportunities in the State Sector","Expand tertiary and higher education opportunities in the state sector.",""],[1,"120","1","Public-Private Partnership Programmes for Higher Education Expansion","Promote public-private partnership (PPP) programmes to expand opportunities for higher education.",""],[1,"120","2","University Teaching and Learning Modernization","Modernize university teaching and learning needs in line with international practices.",""],[1,"120","5","Higher Education and English Language Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of higher education and English language proficiency.",""],[1,"120","9","University Autonomy and Decentralized Decision-Making Reform","Delegate more authority and decision-making powers to universities.",""],[1,"290","3","National Pre-Primary Education Service Delivery Network","Ensure a country-wide network of high quality pre-primary education service delivery mechanisms, while providing children from low income households with publicly funded Early Childhood Care and Education (ECCE) services.",""],[1,"290","4","Outcome-Based Curriculum Reform","Establish a better-articulated outcome based curriculum, integrating and embedding skills - cognitive as well as socio-emotional - which focus on the underlying objective that all children should be successful learners, confident individuals, responsible citizens and effective contributors.",""],[1,"290","5","Teacher Professionalism and Training Improvement","C. Improve teacher professionalism, standards and training in the use of modern teaching- learning methods.",""],[1,"290","6","TVET System Reform and Labour Market Linkage Strengthening","Support systematic reforms in the Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) sector, particularly to match training supply with demand, by creating strong linkages between training supply end users and market demands.",""],[1,"290","7","University Curriculum Diversification and Modernization","Diversify and modernize the curriculum of universities and other higher education institutions, in order to enhance social development and address present and future demands of local and international labour markets.",""]],"11":[[1,"113","4","National ECCE Policy Framework and Strategic Plan","A national policy framework and a comprehensive strategic plan for ECCE specifying a collaborative regulatory mechanism and a systematic service delivery mechanism for ECCE through the public and private sector must be developed.",""],[1,"113","4","ECCE Regulatory, Teacher Education, and Monitoring Mechanism","Regulatory mechanism should embed possible ECCE models, an effective ECCE teacher education model, resourcing strategy, possible public sector interventions to encourage private sector providers, and an efficient monitoring and evaluation mechanism along with regular data gathering practices.",""],[1,"113","4","Universal ECCE Enrolment and Publicly Funded Access for Low-Income Households","To enable the country to achieve universal enrolment in ECCE, the service delivery mechanism should ensure a country-wide network of ECCE while providing children from low income households with publicly funded ECCE services.",""]],"12":[[1,"116","14","Systematic School Career Guidance System","Establish a systematic career guidance system in the school system to help children understand their capabilities at an early stage and develop their aspirations to make informed learning and career choices as they progress through school.",""],[1,"119","4","Systematic Career Counselling System","Establish a systematic career counselling system to give sound careers advice to young people.",""],[1,"120","16","Education-Sector Linkage Mechanism","Establish linkages between education and relevant sectors.",""],[1,"273","1","School-Level Career Guidance and Labour Market Awareness","It is important that both parents and youth be made aware of the dynamics and opportunities of labour demand.",""],[1,"273","1","School-Based Career Guidance Services","Well thought out career guidance given at the school level is necessary.",""],[1,"273","2","School Curriculum Redesign for Practical and Vocational Skills","Curriculums in schools need to be redesigned to produce individuals with both practical and theoretical knowledge.",""],[1,"273","2","Advanced Level Curriculum Reform for Vocational Pathways","Advanced level curriculums can be redesigned to prepare students to select their vocation when they leave school.",""],[1,"273","2","School-to-Vocational Education Access Procedure","Despite existing vocational training institutes, there is no constituted procedure to get the students who leave school after their Advanced Level examination to access vocational education streams.",""]],"13":[[1,"14","8","Job Creation and Inclusive Skills Development Initiative","Create more job opportunities (especially for women and youth), to address inequality concerns and make growth more inclusive, coupled with increased skills development, and for women, cultural acceptance of their work outside the home/community and better child care facilities.",""],[1,"17","4","Informal Employment and Casualization Reduction Measures","Manage the increasing trend towards casualization of work and the expansion of the informal sector, through appropriate policy and program interventions in order ensure greater income and employment security.",""],[1,"26","5","Transport Employment Formalization and Decent Work Initiative","The GoSL will by 2030 take steps to formalize transport employment and to create decent work conditions.",""]],"14":[[1,"156","10","Strengthening Maritime Teaching and Training Institutes","Therefore, maritime teaching and training institutes need further strengthening.",""]],"15":[[1,"212","9","Participatory Education for Diversity and Inclusion","Education in this respect is fundamental; but it cannot be merely the transmission of ideas: it is required the active participation and practice is incentivized.",""],[1,"212","10","Inclusive Religious Education Reform","Religious teaching, which most young people attend, should be incentivized to reflect positive traits of other communities and faiths.",""],[1,"212","10","Interfaith Tolerance and Anti-Discrimination Religious Instruction","It should help students recognize the shared values that exist across religious identities, and it should teach basic elements of mutual respect and tolerance.",""],[1,"212","10","Reform of Segregated Religious Schooling","The current practice of the state supporting teaching of religion in separate religious schools for different religious groups does not seem to help inter-faith understanding or even tolerance.",""],[1,"213","4","Participatory Civics and Human Rights Education","Civics teaching should have as a cornerstone the understanding of the Bill of Rights in the Constitution, and the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.",""],[1,"214","6","Global Citizenship Education Programme","Programmes such as Global citizenship education (GCE) can inspire action, and build partnerships, dialogue and cooperation through formal and informal education.",""],[1,"215","5","Teacher Training Programme on Citizenship and Communication Skills","Initiate teacher training programmes to increase the knowledge and understanding pertaining to the issues and trends around citizenship among teachers, and improve interpersonal/communication skills50.",""],[1,"216","5","Global Citizenship Education Programme","Programmes such as Global citizenship education (GCE) can inspire action, build partnerships, dialogue and cooperation through formal and informal education.",""],[1,"216","5","Community-Based Learning Environment Initiative","Community based approaches will create learning environments that promotes links to communities and link learners to real-life experiences.",""],[1,"259","13","Compulsory Reconciliation Curriculum Integration","Integration of a compulsory reconciliation curriculum in the national curriculum.",""],[1,"267","2","National Identity and Anti-Radicalization Education","Working towards creating a common Sri Lankan national identity by 2020, is essential for the country, especially in curbing the radicalization of youth.",""],[1,"267","2","Education for Ethnic and Religious Respect","In this regard, dignity and respect for all ethnicities, cultures and religions must be taught on an educational level in Sri Lanka.",""]],"16":[[1,"23","6","Hierarchical Peripheral Hospital Primary Health Care System","Establish a hierarchical system that develops the Peripheral Hospitals (with mobile labs) to deliver Primary Health Care, leaving Secondary and Tertiary Care hospitals to deal with complex cases ..",""],[1,"23","7","Transparent Hospital Medical Supply Chain","Establish a supply chain with auditing, accountability and transparency in supplying medicines and equipment to hospitals.",""],[1,"23","8","Public Education on Sanitation, Healthcare Standards, and Accident Prevention","Educate the public on proper sanitation, healthcare standards, avoidance of traffic accidents",""],[1,"23","9","Health Workforce Expansion and Incentive Support for Remote Areas","Increase trained staff in MOH areas, with suitable remuneration for working in remote areas, to further reduce maternal and infant mortality, and minimize communicable diseases, and reduce the prevalence of NCDs.",""],[1,"23","9","Ambulance Crew Training for Patient Transfers","Provide well trained ambulance crews to deal with transfer of sick patients to specialized units",""],[1,"24","1","Electronic Medical Records Digital Platform","Set up a digital platform for Electronic Medical Records, develop Public Private Partnerships, initially through its Corporate Social Responsibility Programmes.",""],[1,"24","1","Health Sector Public-Private Partnership Development","Set up a digital platform for Electronic Medical Records, develop Public Private Partnerships, initially through its Corporate Social Responsibility Programmes.",""],[1,"146","2","Healthcare Facility Classification and Referral System Reform","healthcare units must be classified based on their facilities and expertise, and a standard package of services assigned to each category.",""],[1,"146","2","Patient Referral and Health Information Access System","It would also be necessary to introduce a referral system, easy access to patient records, training, community education, and IT systems to increase efficiency.",""],[1,"146","2","Equitable Access to Preventive and Curative Health and Nutrition Services","Furthermore, issues of equity and access to preventive and curative health and nutrition services should be addressed.",""],[1,"147","1","Healthcare Facility Reorganization for Referral Continuity","Reorganize the existing healthcare facilities in the curative system, to accommodate referrals and back referrals to ensure continuity of care.",""],[1,"147","2","Provincial Primary Care Supervision Tool","A supervision tool to be developed and pre-tested, and given to provincial health authorities to supervise primary care institutions as a circular.",""],[1,"147","3","Primary Care Competency-Oriented Education Reform","Request the UGC and medical faculties to focus on education reform to develop relevant competencies for primary care.",""],[1,"147","4","Medicine Availability Monitoring System for Primary Care Units","Establish monitoring systems to ensure availability of medicines at primary care units.",""],[1,"147","5","Primary Care Medical Officer Incentive Structure","Introduce an incentive structure for MOs in primary care.",""],[1,"147","6","Career Progression Pathways for Primary Care Medical Officers","Design pathways to career progression for MO's in primary care.",""],[1,"147","7","Apex Hospital Outreach Support Mechanism","Develop outreach support mechanisms - where specialists in apex hospital can provide clinical guidance to doctors in surrounding primary care hospitals - to build confidence - for better patient care.",""],[1,"147","11","Patient Registration with Board-Certified General Practitioners","All patients would be registered under a board certified general practitioner.",""]],"17":[[1,"88","7","Disease Prevention Promotion","Encourage and resort to disease prevention which is more successful than management.",""],[1,"88","8","Health Insurance Scheme for CKDu-Vulnerable People","Introduce a health insurance scheme, especially for people who are venerable to CKDu.",""],[1,"88","9","Community Health Checkup Promotion","Advocate communities to undertake regular health checkups to enable early detection.",""],[1,"88","10","Disease Prevention Infrastructure Investment","Invest in appropriate infrastructure for disease prevention.",""],[1,"88","11","Interdisciplinary Disease Prevention and Management Approach","Use an interdisciplinary approach in both disease prevention and management as there are multi stakeholders in the process.",""],[1,"88","13","Community Disease Prevention Education and Empowerment","Community education and empowerment to manage their own vicinities to prevent diseases like dengue.",""],[1,"100","16","National Nutritional and Food Safety Programme","Implement a national nutritional and food safety programme",""],[1,"147","8","Public Education on Sanitation, Health Standards, and Sustainable Lifestyles","Conduct public education on sanitation, healthcare standards, and sustainable lifestyles (diet, exercise, etc.).",""],[1,"147","9","Aged-Care and Age-Friendly Facilities Expansion","Increase aged-care facilities and age-friendly facilities in public areas.",""],[1,"147","10","Expansion of Inpatient, Outpatient, and Laboratory Services","Increase inpatient, outpatient and laboratory services.",""],[1,"150","9","Central Treatment Facilities Establishment","Establish central treatment facilities.",""],[1,"151","15","First Responder Capacity Development and Training","Develop capacity development and training of first respondents.",""],[1,"154","14","Implementation of Already Identified SAM Sites","Implement already identified SAM sites.",""]],"18":[[1,"44","1","Universal Primary Health Care Provision","Primary health care would be ensured for all, while high end medical services up to the best international standards would be provided in selected areas.",""],[1,"44","1","National Health Insurance Scheme","A countrywide National Health Insurance scheme would be established.",""],[1,"44","1","Public-Private Partnership Expansion","Public Private Partnerships would become more prevalent.",""],[1,"44","1","Transparent Health Procurement System","A transparent procurement system would be established, to deliver quality non-consumables and consumables.",""],[1,"44","1","Electronic Medical Record System","Electronic medical record keeping would be set up.",""],[1,"147","11","Transparent Public Procurement System for Health Supplies","By 2020, a transparent procurement system would be established, to deliver quality non- consumables and consumables.",""],[1,"147","11","Electronic Medical Record System","Electronic medical record keeping would be set up.",""],[1,"147","11","Hazardous Materials Control and Management System","The government would control and manage the issue and use of hazardous materials.",""],[1,"147","12","National Health Insurance Scheme","A countrywide national health insurance scheme would be established, and public private partnerships would become more prevalent.",""],[1,"147","12","Expansion of Public-Private Partnerships in Health Care","A countrywide national health insurance scheme would be established, and public private partnerships would become more prevalent.",""],[1,"147","12","Digital Patient Health Records System","By 2030 it will be possible for all Sri Lankans to experience an international standard of health care in any part of the country with facilities to obtain a patient's health records at any given time, making use of electronic technology.",""],[1,"147","12","National Health Financing Scheme","The public private partnership combined with a national health financing scheme will ensure affordable Health for all, including the uninterrupted availability of essential drugs and other consumables according to the grade of the institution, thereby making the SDG-Health vision come true by 2030.",""],[1,"293","1","Hierarchical Hospital System for Primary Health Care Delivery","Establish a hierarchical system that develops the peripheral hospitals (with mobile labs) to deliver Primary Health Care, leaving Secondary and Tertiary Care hospitals to deal with complex cases.",""],[1,"293","4","Health Workforce Expansion and Ambulance Crew Training","Increase trained staff in Ministry of Health (MOH) areas - with suitable remuneration for working in remote areas - to further reduce maternal and infant mortality and minimize communicable diseases, and provide well trained ambulance crews to deal with the transfer of sick patients to specialized units.","Ministry of Health (MOH)"],[1,"293","5","Health Public-Private Partnership Development","develop public-private partnerships",""],[1,"293","5","National Health Insurance Scheme","establish a National Health Insurance scheme to reduce the financial burden on the Government",""],[1,"293","6","Electronic Medical Record System","Electronic medical record keeping will also be set up.",""],[1,"293","6","Patient Registration with Board Certified General Practitioners","All patients will be registered under a Board Certified General Practitioner.",""],[1,"293","7","National Health Insurance Scheme","A countrywide National Health Insurance scheme will be established during this time frame, and public-private partnerships will become more prevalent.",""]],"19":[[1,"189","8","Reverse Osmosis Plant Installation for Renal Disease Mitigation","Install reverse osmosis plants to mitigate renal disease conditions.",""],[1,"194","12","Rainwater Use Promotion in CKDU-Affected Areas","Promote the use of Rainwater in CKDU affected areas.",""],[1,"194","14","Control of Toxic Weedicides and Pesticides","Control use of toxic weedicides and pesticides in agriculture and educate the formers.",""],[1,"194","15","Safe Pipe-Borne Water Supply for CKDU-Affected Areas","Ensure supply of pipe borne water from a safe water source to CKDU or health effected areas, by building small ponds.",""],[1,"279","7","National Programme for Chronic Kidney Disease Prevention","National Programme for Chronic Kidney Disease Prevention",""],[1,"286","2","Interdisciplinary CKDu Eradication Approach","The eradication of CKDu by having an effective interdisciplinary approach which takes on the perspectives of all the stakeholders in delivering a sound solution to the recipients, will ensure a safe and secure life for them.",""]],"20":[[1,"293","2","Transparent Hospital Medical Supply Chain","Establish a supply chain with appropriate auditing, accountability and transparency mechanisms, in supplying medicines and equipment to hospitals.",""],[1,"293","5","Electronic Medical Records Digital Platform","Set up a digital platform for Electronic Medical Records",""],[1,"293","6","Transparent Procurement System for Medical Supplies","Within this period, a transparent procurement system will be established to deliver quality non- consumables and consumables.",""],[1,"293","6","Electronic Medical Record System","Electronic medical record keeping will also be set up.",""],[1,"293","6","Hazardous Materials Control and Management","The Government will control and manage the issue and use of hazardous materials.",""]],"21":[[1,"35","3","National Innovation Ecosystem Development","The island will capitalize on its size, diversity and openness to new ideas to create a vibrant innovation eco-system where invention and scaling by local as well as foreign innovators will be encouraged.",""],[1,"35","3","Innovation Testing and User Acceptance Assessment Framework","This will be achieved by fostering an environment wherein user acceptance of product and process innovations can be systematically assessed using modalities such as sample surveys, data analytics, qualitative research and A/B testing conveniently, quickly, and at low cost.",""],[1,"35","3","Innovation-Friendly Regulatory Process","The government, by creating a process instead of picking winners, keeps the necessary risk taking where it belongs, in the hands of the innovators.",""],[1,"35","4","Regional Product and Process Innovation Test-Bed","Create the leading test-bed in the region for product and process innovation by incentivizing private firms and non-profit entities to put in place the necessary elements for an innovation test-bed.",""],[1,"35","5","Angel and Venture Capital Promotion and Innovation Incubator Support","Further encourage Sri Lanka's inchoate angel and venture capital financiers and promote provision of incubators and accelerators along with incentives for large companies to create space for innovation.",""],[1,"35","6","Innovation Incentives and Intellectual Property System Reform","Create conditions for cross-fertilization of ideas along with a reward system for successful innovators (including, but not limited to, an effective intellectual property system).",""],[1,"35","7","Innovation Mindset Promotion through Education and Media","Foster mindsets conducive to innovation and larger-than-Sri Lanka thinking through the educational system and media.",""],[1,"45","4","Innovation Cross-Fertilization and Reward System","Cross-fertilization of ideas along with a reward system for successful innovators, and successful implementation by 2025 will vault Sri Lanka to the forefront of innovation among lower-middle- income countries in South and South East Asia.",""],[1,"71","9","Market-Based Incentives for R&D and Green Innovation","Provide market based incentives such as tax credits for business investments in R&D and environment-friendly innovations for sustainable development",""],[1,"78","6","Patent Law and Intellectual Property Rights Strengthening","Adopt strategies to encourage the issuance and enforcement of patents, including enacting new patent laws and strengthening intellectual property rights (IPR) policies",""],[1,"82","12","Green Technology Entrepreneurship Support","Create a suitable environment for domestic entrepreneurship to explore \"green technology\" in order to reduce Sri Lanka's dependence on non-renewable energy sources and volatile consumer product markets such as oil",""]],"22":[[1,"236","4","Entrepreneurial Scaling and Broader Angel Finance Mobilization","Entrepreneurs must be encouraged to think bigger than Sri Lanka.",""],[1,"237","3","Private Innovation Investment Mobilization","Because the proposed initiative is not anchored on subsidies, it will necessarily have to mobilize innovation-relevant investments by private entities both foreign and domestic.",""],[1,"237","3","Innovation Communication and Investor Outreach","This necessarily requires a strong emphasis on communication, so that the actions taken to create an Experiment Nation are well understood by potential investors.",""],[1,"237","3","Innovation Incubator Reactivation and Startup Showcasing","Effective communication will require \"facts on the ground\" including successful innovation incubators such as the reactivation of Trace Expert City in Colombo and elsewhere and the showcasing of start-ups and innovation units within established companies.",""],[1,"237","6","Innovation Incubator Reactivation and Success Story Identification","Create \"facts on the ground\" including successful innovation incubators such as the reactivation of Trace Expert City in Colombo, and identify success stories such as start-ups and innovation units within established companies.",""],[1,"237","8","International Communication Campaign","Design and implement an international communication campaign under the aegis of the Board of Investment or the Export Development Board using the above.",""],[1,"237","11","Innovation Mindset Communication Campaign Task Team","Establish a task team to plan a multi-pronged communication campaign to change mind-sets that are hostile to innovation.",""],[1,"304","1","Regional Innovation Test-Bed Development Initiative","Create the leading test-bed in the region for product and process innovation by incentivizing private firms and non-profit entities to put in place the necessary elements for an innovation test-bed.",""],[1,"304","2","Angel and Venture Capital Promotion and Innovation Incubator Support","Further encourage Sri Lanka's inchoate angel and venture capital financiers and promote the provision of incubators and accelerators, along with incentives for large companies to create space for innovation.",""],[1,"304","3","Innovation Incentives and Intellectual Property System Reform","Create conditions for cross-fertilization of ideas along with a reward system for successful innovators (including, but not limited to, an effective intellectual property system).",""],[1,"304","4","Innovation Mindset Promotion through Education and Media","Foster mindsets conducive to innovation and larger-than-Sri Lanka thinking through the educational system and media.",""]],"23":[[1,"14","3","Economic Reform Programme to Improve Business Climate and Reduce Public Debt","If the government shows a strong commitment to address current challenges by implementing economic reforms to improve its Doing Business global rankings to a position below 70 from the current 110, while lowering its public debt from the current 79.3% of GDP to 70% within the same period",""],[1,"15","2","Doing Business Indicator Improvement Reform","Improve Doing Business indicators - specifically with regard to enforcing contracts, paying taxes, registering property, and getting credit - to improve economic efficiency",""],[1,"67","7","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction Initiative","Attract more FDI to bridge the savings - investment gap.",""],[1,"73","3","Provincial Investment Promotion Strategy","Investment promotion strategies targeting the less developed provinces will help to induce infrastructural developments and generate employment opportunities that will help address regional economic imbalances and inequities.",""],[1,"73","6","National Industrial Policy and BOI One-Stop Shop Enhancement","Formulate a national industrial policy to provide investors a credible and coherent indication of future policy direction, whilst enhancing the effectiveness of BOI as a 'one-stop shop' for foreign investors that offers a range of services",""],[1,"78","4","Doing Business Reform Programme","Improve Doing Business indicators, specifically with regard to enforcing contracts, paying taxes, registering property, and getting credit, which could contribute towards lowering the ICOR",""],[1,"92","4","Regulatory and Approval Procedure Strengthening","Public and private investments need to be preceded by comprehensive regulatory and approval procedures.",""],[1,"92","4","Strengthening Provincial and Local Regulatory Agencies","Strengthen regulatory and approving agencies where they are currently weak such as provincial and local authorities.",""],[1,"100","7","Business Regulatory and Operational Environment Reform","Improving business regulatory and operational environment by restructuring regulatory institutions",""],[1,"100","7","Simplified Low-Tax Business Administration","Moving towards a low tax and tariff business environment with simplified and transparent administrative procedures",""],[1,"100","7","Land Lease Access Streamlining","Identifying and removing delays and complexities in obtaining land leases",""]],"24":[[1,"65","2","Export Competitiveness and Supply-Side Reform","This requires reforms aimed to address supply-side rigidities to enhance Sri Lanka's export competitiveness in international markets.",""],[1,"66","7","Export Diversification Expansion","Expand export diversification of both goods and services exports.",""],[1,"70","8","Trade and Investment Policy Reforms to Raise Export Earnings","Export earnings need to be raised through trade and investment policy reforms to shore up Sri Lanka's official reserves and thereby strengthen exchange rate management",""],[1,"72","6","National Trade Policy Strategy","Formulate and implement a national trade policy strategy with due consultation with stakeholders.",""],[1,"72","7","Trade System Simplification and Transparency Reform","Simplify and make the trade system transparent and predictable by limiting the number of rates, exceptions, amalgamating the para-tariffs, streamlining the computation of taxes, passing of WTO consistent trade remedies like anti-dumping, counter-vailing, and safeguard measures",""],[1,"72","8","Strategic Trade Agreement Negotiation and Review","Adopt a more strategic approach in future trade agreements with India, China and Singapore, whilst addressing short-comings in existing agreements",""],[1,"72","9","Trade Facilitation Agreement Implementation","Implement the Trade Facilitation Agreement (TFA) including improving the publication and administration of trade related policies, streamline export/import procedures, increase the usage of ICT for trade, improve infrastructure facilities at both the port and airport; extend pre-arrival processing to more products.",""],[1,"76","11","Export Basket Diversification to Value-Added and High-End Markets","Diversify current primary product export basket to value added/processed products and existing destinations to more high end markets",""],[1,"78","3","Reduction of Para-Tariffs","Minimize the proliferation of a variety of para-tariffs which significantly raise the costs and complexity of trading",""],[1,"82","8","Export Basket Diversification Initiative","Diversify export basket both in terms of products and markets in order to reduce dependence on EU and US.",""],[1,"82","9","Economic Partnership Arrangements with Asian Economies and Groupings","Seek economic partnership arrangements with Asian economies and groupings to promote exports and attract FDI",""],[1,"100","4","Trade Facilitation and Market Diversification Measures","-Implementing trade facilitation commitments -Phase out various para-tariffs -Reviewing and renegotiating existing FTAs and entering into new FTAs with dynamic Asian economies",""],[1,"101","1","Trade Negotiations and Trade Adjustment Program","Ongoing trade negotiations with India, Singapore, and China will continue, along with a trade adjustment program - including the enforcement of anti-dumping laws -to lessen competition impacts on domestic firms.",""],[1,"101","2","Trade and Financial Integration Strengthening","It is also imperative that Sri Lanka integrates its economy closely with the global economy through strengthened trade and financial relations to maximize the chances of realizing the set targets.",""],[1,"240","5","Economic Diplomacy and Investment Promotion Initiative","Economic diplomacy initiatives were pursued by the Ministry to bolster the economy, enhance development activities and attract foreign investors and traders to the country with vigour, taking advantage of the positive international focus on Sri Lanka.","Ministry"],[1,"240","5","Free Trade Agreement Negotiation Support","The Ministry also supported trade and economic policy decisions taken by the Government particularly related to negotiating free trade agreements with identified well performing economies in Asia while assisting the exploration of similar arrangements with other emerging economies.","Ministry"],[1,"240","5","Foreign Direct Investment and Global Value Chain Promotion","Furthermore, the Ministry worked closely with respective line agencies to attract more Foreign Direct Investments (FDI) to the country, increase trade potential, establish links with the global value chains in main economic corridors, and further improve substantial growth in tourism so as to contribute towards the economic progress of the country.","Ministry"],[1,"242","3","EU GSP+ Compliance and Free Trade Transition Strategy","Implementation of 27 international conventions to which Sri Lanka is party, which include 07 core human rights conventions is key to secure this facility and to continue to receive benefits from the EU GSP+ arrangement.",""],[1,"281","2","Export Competitiveness Supply-Side Reforms","Increase export earnings and FDI flows to achieve external stability - through supply-side reforms that improve export competitiveness, and a strategic approach to trade agreements.",""],[1,"281","2","Strategic Trade Agreements Approach","Increase export earnings and FDI flows to achieve external stability - through supply-side reforms that improve export competitiveness, and a strategic approach to trade agreements.",""],[1,"282","10","Trade Facilitation and FTA Reform Agenda","Implementing trade facilitation commitments, phasing out various para-tariffs, and reviewing and renegotiating existing FTAs and entering into new FTAs with dynamic Asian economies",""],[1,"283","11","Ongoing Trade Negotiations and Trade Adjustment Program","Ongoing trade negotiations with India, Singapore, and China will continue, along with a trade adjustment program - including the enforcement of anti-dumping laws - to lessen competition impacts on domestic firms.",""],[1,"283","12","Trade and Financial Integration Strengthening","It is also imperative that Sri Lanka integrates its economy closely with the global economy through strengthened trade and financial relations to maximize the chances of realizing the set targets.",""],[1,"290","2","Awareness Raising on Technical Barriers to Trade and Free Trade Agreements","For the long-term sustainability of the sector, a heightened awareness of the potential impacts of technical barriers to trade as well as FTAs is required.",""]],"25":[[1,"232","5","Innovation Parks and Incubators Public-Private Partnership Support","the provision of land for innovation parks and incubators to be professionally managed by specialized firms may be undertaken through public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"232","5","University-Industry Partnership Strengthening","Fostering closer university-industry partnerships is another element of this strategy.",""],[1,"232","6","Innovation Barrier Removal and R&D Partnership Support","the identification and removal of barriers to innovation can take place in parallel with the establishment of public- private partnerships to proactively improve the conditions for R&D and related activities.",""],[1,"232","6","Government R&D Organization Efficiency and External Orientation Reform","Government R&D organizations will necessarily continue.",""],[1,"234","3","Innovation Ecosystem Development and Innovation Testing Framework","The island will capitalize on its size, diversity and openness to new ideas to create a vibrant innovation eco-system where invention and scaling by local as well as foreign innovators will be encouraged.",""],[1,"234","4","Innovation Culture Promotion through Education and Media","In parallel, mind-sets conducive to innovation will be fostered through education and media.",""],[1,"234","4","Cross-Fertilization of Ideas Promotion","Conditions for the cross-fertilization of ideas will be promoted.",""],[1,"234","4","Innovator Reward and Intellectual Property Support System","A reward system for successful innovators (including, but not limited to, an effective intellectual property system that does not stifle innovation) will be developed.",""],[1,"234","4","Startup Financing and Incubation Support","Angel and venture capital financing for start-ups and the provision of incubators and accelerators will be encouraged along with incentives for large companies to create space for innovation.",""],[1,"234","4","Investment and International Partnership Facilitation Policy","The government will implement policies conducive to domestic and foreign investment and mergers and acquisitions, and openness to international partnerships and sourcing of inputs.",""],[1,"234","5","Innovation-Friendly Policy Process","The government, by creating a process instead of picking winners, keeps the necessary risk taking where it belongs, in the hands of the innovators.",""],[1,"234","7","Innovation Test-Bed Incentive Initiative","This can be done by incentivizing private firms and non-profit entities to put in place the necessary elements for an innovation test-bed.",""],[1,"234","7","Innovation Test-Bed Promotion and Investment Attraction","The initiative will be marketed to local and foreign firms by entities such as the Board of Investment and the Export Development Board.",""],[1,"234","7","Skilled Personnel Mobility Facilitation","Enabling firms to move to Sri Lanka and to bring personnel in would be essential for success.",""],[1,"234","7","Cross-Border Skilled Personnel Mobility Flexibility","In general, greater flexibility in terms of cross-border movement of skilled personnel, including those from the diaspora would be required.",""],[1,"234","9","Experiment Nation Innovation Testing Initiative","Positioning of Sri Lanka as an \"experiment nation\" that welcomes innovative companies to market-test products will have collateral benefits for entire economy.",""],[1,"236","4","University-Industry Collaboration and Commercialization Initiative","The government will enable closer university-industry collaboration wherein multiple firms in the same industry would work with selected academic units.",""],[1,"236","4","Expansion of Entrepreneurial Learning Across Tertiary Institutions","Lessons from University of Moratuwa's experience in inculcating entrepreneurial attitudes should be extended across a range of tertiary educational institutes, not limited to universities.",""],[1,"236","4","Industry-Sponsored Magnet and Demonstration Schools","In addition, a small number of magnet/demonstration schools at the secondary level, sponsored by industry associations such as CCC and SLASSCOM that will demonstrate innovation-focused learning must be implemented.",""],[1,"236","4","Innovation Messaging in Local Teledramas","Embedding innovation-friendly messages in local teledramas would be helpful.",""]],"26":[[1,"17","2","Rural Industries Promotion Programme","Promotion of rural industries based on agricultural raw materials is an important step that can be taken to narrow the present rural-urban disparity in terms of employment and income.",""]],"27":[[1,"16","8","Degrowth, Bio-economy, and Circular Economy Implementation in Resource-Consuming Enterprises","Research and implement ideas about de-growth, bio-economy and circular economy, in all resource consuming enterprises to eliminate waste and encourage recovery of resources.",""]],"28":[[1,"41","5","Youth Retention Incentives in Agriculture","Provide incentives for retaining youth in the agricultural sector, including promotion of agriculture based entrepreneurship to increase Youth participation and develop the small-scale agricultural business areas.",""],[1,"310","5","Youth Retention Incentives in Agriculture","Provide incentives for retaining youth in the agricultural sector, including the promotion of agriculture based entrepreneurship to increase youth participation and develop small-scale agricultural business areas.",""]],"29":[[1,"109","4","Public Investment in Irrigation and Infrastructure","greater public investments will be required for irrigation and other infrastructure.",""],[1,"109","10","Incentives for Water-Saving Farming Practices","Incentivize farmers to adopt water saving cropping patterns and cultural practices.",""],[1,"110","2","Farmer Technical Solutions for Water-Saving Agriculture","Provide farmers with technical solutions which save water, labour and agro chemicals.",""],[1,"110","3","Farmer Water Conservation and Agricultural Technology Training","Educate farmers on the need to conserve water and the use of new technology for farming, value addition and marketing.",""],[1,"188","11","Crop Diversification and Climate Adaptation Programme","Introduce crop diversification programmes and climate change adaptive mechanisms",""],[1,"191","6","Drip Irrigation Support for Small Home Agriculture","Introduce drip irrigation technology for small home land agriculture with an overhead tank, solar pump and suitable tank to store rain water.",""],[1,"191","11","Agro Well Rehabilitation and Solar Pump Water Supply","Existing agro wells have to be desilted, renovated and fixed with solar pumps and low cost overhead tanks to supply water for highland crops during droughts when no irrigation water is possible.",""],[1,"191","11","Restricted Use of Deep Wells for Crop Water Supply","Use of deep wells (tube well) will have to be resorted to only when other options are not possible, as scholars suspect that water with high content of minerals may cause kidney disease issues.",""],[1,"192","1","Agro-Well Pilot Project for Drought Preparedness","Introduce a pilot project in selected areas to set up agro-wells to be used for future droughts.",""],[1,"192","10","Irrigation Water Use Efficiency Awareness Programmes","Introduce awareness programmes with Department of Agriculture, Mahaweli Authority, Irrigation Department etc., to improve water use efficiency in irrigation.","Department of Agriculture | Mahaweli Authority | Irrigation Department"],[1,"192","11","Drip Irrigation and Bulk Water Allocation Promotion","Encourage use of drip irrigation, bulk water allocation etc.",""],[1,"192","12","Drought-Resilient Crop Diversification","Encourage farmers to grow crops with \"short harvest life\" to save water during droughts.",""],[1,"192","13","Agricultural Research and Development for Climate-Resilient Crop Varieties","Encourage R&D for drought resistant and short month crop varieties development.",""],[1,"192","14","Measured Agricultural Water Allocation System","Provide measured water for agriculture to quantify and monitor the allocation.",""],[1,"197","7","Irrigation Water Supply Enhancement for NCP and NWP","Supply of Irrigation water to NCP and NWP will be enhanced, diverting 900 MCM/year to NCP and 100 MCM/year to NWP.",""],[1,"198","4","Agricultural Water Measurement, Pricing, and Subsidy Reform","Water supply for all agriculture will be measured and quantified by 2030, and will be priced and charged for commercial farming.",""],[1,"205","6","Water Harvesting and Retention Expansion","Increase water harvesting and retention for a longer period through mechanical means and more environment friendly ways like expanding the ancient \"ellanga\" system where chains of small tanks are built and connected together.",""],[1,"205","7","Agricultural Water Management Improvement","Improve water management in agriculture by using short term crops, introducing varieties that need less water, and introducing drip irrigation systems where appropriate and possible.",""],[1,"205","8","Agro Well Construction and Groundwater Management","Build agro wells providing that the amount of water to be extracted should be studied and managed so that the water table will not be damaged.",""],[1,"205","9","Groundwater Recharge Measures","Take steps to recharge ground water.",""],[1,"207","10","Climate-Resilient Irrigation and Water Management Planning","With the incorporation of the ancient wisdom of irrigation and water management such as clusters of cascading tanks of various sizes into the planning processes, the effects of drought conditions can be largely mitigated.",""],[1,"207","10","Short-Term Crop Variety and Drip Irrigation Support","By cultivating short term crop varieties and using drip irrigation, farmers could manage their finances as well as their nutrient intake.",""]],"30":[[1,"95","7","Development of Green Raw Materials and Food Production on Abandoned Land","The large extents of land that have been abandoned in all parts of the country can be made full use of to promote the production of green raw materials, medicinal plants and food.",""]],"31":[[1,"75","5","Public-Private-People Partnerships for Supply and Value Chain Improvement","Promote public, private and peoples sector partnerships to improve supply and value chains of products, crops and services that would promote domestic consumption as well as exports",""],[1,"76","13","Smallholder Linkages to Global Value Chains","Institutional arrangements such as establishing linkages to connect small-holders to the global value chains; encouraging FDI and PPP in agro-processing",""],[1,"76","13","FDI and PPP Promotion for Agro-processing","Institutional arrangements such as establishing linkages to connect small-holders to the global value chains; encouraging FDI and PPP in agro-processing",""],[1,"110","4","Farmer Organization and Commercial Value Chain Integration","Organise farmers to overcome the scale constraint so that less water using crops can be produced, stored, value added and marketed profitably.",""],[1,"110","7","Integrated Implementation of the Nine-Point Action Plan","What is required, however, is a firm commitment to implement all of them together in an integrated manner even though the potential benefits will be realized over short, medium and long term time horizons.",""]],"32":[[1,"28","4","National Water Storage Priority","An urgent national priority should be given to address water storage.",""],[1,"28","5","National Programme for Small Storage Ponds and Gravity-Driven Mini Schemes","Initiate a national wide programme to identify suitable areas for small storage ponds and gravity driven \"Mini Schemes\" with pipe borne water, with the support of Provincial Councils, Water Board and other authorities.",""],[1,"28","8","Small Irrigation Tank Restoration Programme","Commence a programme to restore small irrigations tanks scattered throughout the country.",""],[1,"29","1","Island-wide Basin Management Awareness Programme","Launch an island wide awareness programme with the support of respective local authorities to educate best practices in basin management, including excavation control, home garden landscaping, mini agriculture construction of roads etc.",""],[1,"30","9","Inter-Basin Water Transfer Project Development","Innovative projects need to be developed after careful research to take excess water from southwest to northeast of the country to overcome long term effects of drought.",""]],"33":[[1,"187","4","Real-Time Water Management System","a \"real time water management system\" should be introduced to manage the water allocation for stake holders.",""],[1,"187","5","Public-Private Participation Promotion in High-Return Sectors","Also, public - private participation should be encouraged in the areas with high return on investments like commercial agriculture agro/eco-tourism, mini hydro and inland fisheries etc.",""],[1,"187","6","Common Water Sector Secretariat","special attention should be paid to form a \"common secretariat\" representing all departments, to take decisions on water sector developments, water use, planning etc.",""],[1,"188","8","Tank Bund Restoration Support to Local Authorities","Allocate sufficient funds to local authorities to restore tank bunds with farmer participation.",""],[1,"188","9","Island-wide Tank Restoration Data Collection Programme","Commence an island wide programme to collect necessary data to restore tanks.",""],[1,"188","10","Farmer-Participatory Tank Maintenance Plan","Plan for future maintenance of tanks with farmer participation.",""],[1,"189","6","Small Pocket Tank Restoration Study","Examine possibility of restoring small pocket tanks (around 600) scattered throughout the Peninsula.",""],[1,"192","2","Authority Data Collection Awareness Programme","Implement a programme to create awareness among authorities on collection of data, and to launch few pilot projects in respective districts.",""],[1,"192","15","Local Water Storage Capacity Expansion","immediate action needs to be taken to increase the retention capacity (storage) at local level, in addition to national level water supply schemes.",""],[1,"193","2","Integrated Urban and Industrial Water Demand Planning","Equal priority to drinking and industrial requirement should be given in city planning and for industrial zones, harbours etc.",""],[1,"193","2","Long-Term Commercial Water Demand Quantification","Commercial level water demand for next 50 year should be quantified concurrently with city development plans for factories, hospitals etc.",""],[1,"193","2","Inter-Ministerial Water Planning Coordination","Therefore, a good dialogue should be maintained with the relevant Ministries and Departments.",""],[1,"194","7","National Small Storage Ponds and Mini Schemes Programme","Initiate a national wide programme to identify suitable areas for small storage ponds and \"mini schemes\", with the support of Provincial Councils and other authorities.",""],[1,"194","7","Village Small Pond Survey and Gravity-Driven Mini Schemes Support","The Water Board, with the help of Provincial Councils to survey for suitable locations to build small ponds in each village and support to implement gravity driven \"mini schemes \"with pipe borne water.",""],[1,"194","8","Technical Support for Location-Specific Water Design Development","Provide technical support from National Water Board to develop designs appropriate to specific locations.","National Water Board"],[1,"194","16","Provisional Survey of Water Sources and Local Demand","Start provisional level survey to collect statistics of possible water sources and respective local demands in health affected areas.",""],[1,"195","2","Water Supply Sector Planning Database","Promote water supply sector planning database.",""],[1,"195","7","Water Infrastructure Siting and Planning","Identify the location for water infrastructure, intake, WTP, reservoirs, and bridge crossings.",""],[1,"197","5","National Water Use Master Plan","It is also a priority to prepare a \"national water use master plan\" covering both 'surface' and 'ground' water, optimization of water use, and measures to maintain the quality of water.",""],[1,"197","6","National Water Management Secretariat","In 2025, a \"national secretariat for water management\" would be set up with the participation of all government agencies dealing with water, to form a single body for making policy decisions in the water sector.",""],[1,"198","2","Smart Water Allocation Decision Support System","\"Smart water allocation\" assisted with \"real time software modules\" will be the decision support mechanisms for the \"National Water Management Secretariat\" for most of the water allocation in irrigation, agriculture, drinking and hydro power in 2030.",""],[1,"198","3","In-basin Water Use Development Promotion","“in basin” water use developments will be promoted, with appropriate agriculture crops, drinking needs, and industrial use to be harmonized with water availability and rainfall.",""],[1,"198","5","Groundwater Aquifer Survey and Database Development","All the ground water aquifer reservoirs will be surveyed for a data base, giving the quality and quantity of water available as an alternative to surface water, if and when necessary.",""],[1,"296","7","Island-wide Basin Management Awareness Programme","Launch an island wide awareness programme with the support of respective local authorities to provide information on the best practices in basin management, including excavation control, home garden landscaping, mini agriculture, construction of roads etc.",""],[1,"297","3","National Water Use Master Plan","It is also a priority to prepare a \"National Water Use Master Plan\" covering both 'surface' and 'ground' water, optimization of water use, and measures to maintain the quality of water.",""],[1,"297","4","National Secretariat for Water Management","In 2025, a \"National Secretariat for Water Management\" would be set up with the participation of all Government agencies dealing with water, to form a single body for making policy decisions in the water sector.",""],[1,"297","7","Smart Water Allocation Decision Support System","\"Smart Water Allocation\" assisted by \"Real Time Software Modules\" will be the decision support mechanisms for the National Water Management Secretariat for most of the water allocation in irrigation, agriculture, drinking and hydro power in 2030.",""],[1,"297","9","Agricultural Water Measurement and Quantification System","Water supply for all agriculture will be measured and quantified by 2030, and will be",""],[1,"298","2","Groundwater Aquifer Survey and Database Development","All the ground water aquifer reservoirs will be surveyed for a data base, giving the quality and quantity of water available as an alternative to surface water, if and when necessary.",""]],"34":[[1,"191","7","Rural Rainwater Harvesting Pilot Projects","Promote rain water harvesting in rural areas with the support of local authorities as pilot projects.",""],[1,"191","8","Home Gardening Promotion","Promote home gardening.",""],[1,"191","9","Household Drinking Water Quality and Filtration Support","Maintain quality of drinking water and provide households with filters.",""],[1,"191","10","Solar Pump Installation with Overhead Tanks","Fix solar pumps with overhead tanks to reduce operations costs.",""],[1,"192","3","Technical Support for Rural Water Supply Technologies","Provide technical support for \"Dug Well, Solar Pump and Over Head Tank\", following appropriate technology to suit available resources in specific areas.",""],[1,"192","4","Renovation of Abandoned or Dilapidated Agro-Wells and Wells","Renovation of Abandoned or dilapidated Agro-Wells, Dug Wells and Deep Wells (Tube wells)",""],[1,"193","9","Rainwater Harvesting Subsidy Programme","The government immediately needs to support rainwater harvesting with a subsidiary programme, especially in rural CKDu areas.",""],[1,"195","20","Rainwater System Promotion and Marketing","The benefit of rain water systems to be marketed.",""],[1,"195","21","Pilot Projects in Public Sector Instruction and Household Units","Pilot projects are to be implemented in public sector instruction and identified house hold units.",""],[1,"195","22","Rainwater Harvesting System Promotion","Make use of available funds for rain water harvesting system promotion from the on-going foreign funded projects.",""],[1,"197","3","Rainwater Harvesting and Rural Water Infrastructure Programme","In the road map toward 2030, the first stretch from 2018 to 2020 would cover events to promote rain water harvesting in CKDu and other possible rural areas (with subsidized financing); rehabilitate minor tanks for drinking and agriculture; and improve recharge aquifers in Jaffna area.",""],[1,"197","3","Rural Wells and Sanitation Improvement Programme","Other steps would be to clean, rehabilitate and construct shallow wells for drinking and minor agriculture, and to improve sanitation in rural schools and the estate sector with the assistance of provincial authorities and respective government agencies.",""],[1,"197","3","Water Resources Survey and Budget Allocation","A survey should be started immediately to quantify the work and data, and a necessary budget should be allocated.",""],[1,"197","7","Drinking Water Coverage Expansion","drinking water coverage will increase up to 60 per cent from the present coverage of 45 per cent, with the support of NWSDB and local authorities.",""],[1,"198","4","Subsidized Rainwater Harvesting and Alternative Water Supply","Rain water harvesting in urban and rural areas will be utilized with subsidized financing as an alternative to pipe borne supply.",""]],"35":[[1,"196","5","National Sanitation Facility Improvement Policy","proper sanitary facilities should be provided as a \"nation policy\", with a reasonable toll as a maintenance fee.",""],[1,"196","6","Sanitary Needs Prioritization Policy","Hence a policy decision should be taken to prioritize sanitary needs in any development programs planned nationally or locally.",""],[1,"196","6","Integrated Urban-Rural Water and Sanitation Planning","Any urban development should not be planned in isolation from adjacent rural water supply and sanitary schemes, and should follow a holistic regional viewpoint.",""],[1,"196","6","Rural and Estate Sanitary Facility Improvement","Further, the improvement of sanitary facility in rural areas, and the estate sector has to be considered, after collecting the statistics from provisional authorities and other sources.",""],[1,"196","10","Common Sanitary Network and Drainage Planning for Major Cities","Common sanitary network lines, drainage and treatment plans should be planned with national priority in major cities, to handle the waste demands for the next 30/50 years and all sub sanitary facilities should be linked to new networks.",""],[1,"196","11","Urban Sanitary System Upgrading and Waste Treatment","Existing sanitary systems in urban areas should be upgraded to cater for the present and near future requirements, and the sanitary waste should properly be treated before discharge to natural streams.",""],[1,"197","1","Sanitary Waste Discharge Control and Fines","People should be advised to make sure not to discharge the sanitary waste to natural streams without treatment, and polluters should be fined.",""],[1,"197","6","Drinking Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement Programme","Goals would include, supplying drinking water to 65 per cent of the population, improving the pipe borne network, organizing methods like RO plant, rain water harvesting, reserving necessary funding, procurement planning, planning for improving sewerage networks in the metropolis, and planning to improve sanitation in the rural and estate sector.",""],[1,"198","6","Metropolitan Sewerage Plant Upgrading and New City Sewerage System Development","Sewerage plants in most of the metropolis will be upgraded, and high priority will be given for renovating or constructing a sewerage system in new city development plans as a \"Government Policy\", beyond 2030, with proper access to acceptable sanitary facilities.",""]],"36":[[1,"17","2","Public Transport Service Improvement","Other effective measures that are necessary to reduce income inequalities include progressive income taxation, improvement of public educational services to cut down private tuition, introduction of a contributory health insurance scheme to minimize out of pocket medical expenses, adequate income support to the poor and vulnerable groups on the basis of a reliable and fair means test and the improvement of public transport services.",""],[1,"26","1","National Mobility Assessment and Inclusive Transport Access Improvement","Complete a mobility assessment to fill service gaps by 2030.",""],[1,"160","1","Bus Priority Lane Implementation","Recent policy initiatives have included bus priority lanes and the reform of the bus sector through the Sahasara pilot project.",""],[1,"160","1","Bus Sector Reform Pilot Project","Recent policy initiatives have included bus priority lanes and the reform of the bus sector through the Sahasara pilot project.",""],[1,"166","4","Urban Transport and Traffic Planning for Liveable Cities","By 2025, each city with over a 100,000 day time population will have a transport and traffic plan that will ensure adequate walkability, cycling and access by public transport modes including a multi-modal transport terminal, while controlling traffic volumes and on-street and even off-street parking to levels that are sustainable for the physical and cultural character of the city.",""],[1,"166","4","Public Transport-Based Urban Liveability Improvement","Public transport will be considered the means of improving liveability in urban areas from 2020 onwards.",""],[1,"168","3","Bus Transport Service Improvement","Improving bus transport services is considered the most cost effective and strategic approach in a densely-populated country where residences are scattered, to arrest the rapidly worsening traffic conditions by its more efficient use of road space.",""],[1,"168","4","Bus Sector Transformation Strategic Plan","the government will review such findings, and within a period of 3 months, formulate a strategic plan to transform the bus sector to enable it to achieve the desired objectives.",""],[1,"168","4","Bus Operations Regulation and Sector Consolidation Policy","This will include a policy to (a) regulate excessive on-road competition, (b) improved bus operations management of both SLTB and by consolidating the private sector operators,",""],[1,"168","4","Bus Fleet and Transport Infrastructure Modernization","modernize buses, terminals, ticketing systems, information systems and other supporting infrastructure,",""],[1,"168","4","Bus Transport Regulatory Institution Strengthening","creating strong regulatory institutions that can ensure the continuous delivery of high quality bus transport services by 2020.",""]],"37":[[1,"78","11","Railway Electrification and Network Development","in the transport sector, electrification and development of railway networks should be promoted with the involvement of the private sector",""],[1,"89","10","Transport Management Action Plan","Implement transport management action plan with modern dedicated bus lanes, mono rail or uni rails, expressways, carpooling, using alternative working hours or home based work schedules etc.",""],[1,"100","8","Efficient National Transport Network Development","Creating an efficient transport network connecting large and emerging cities, townships, economic centers and rural hubs",""],[1,"169","2","Multimodal Transport Network Development","As such, a multi modal transport network with seamless integration between them is considered as being the most sustainable to be developed across the country, regionally and within urban areas by 2030.",""],[1,"169","3","Multimodal Transport Infrastructure Development","Develop transport infrastructure within the context of multi modal transport development and its application nationally, regionally and within cities.",""],[1,"169","4","National Transport and Logistics Development Plan","The inefficiency should be eliminated by a series of interventions starting in 2020 with relation to a National Transport & Logistics Development plan.",""],[1,"169","5","Rural Product Supply Chain Management Study","Special emphasis to be given to (a) study of the supply chain management of different rural products including agriculture, fisheries and small industries",""],[1,"169","5","Rural Logistics and Storage Facility Development","facilitate the development of logistics centres, storage locations, value adding facilities, packing and handling etc., that would reduce waste and damage, and enable high quality products to reach markets reliably for a higher price",""],[1,"169","5","Supply Chain Information Flow Systems","supply chain information flow systems for producers and buyers",""],[1,"169","5","Private Partnership Facility Development","private partnerships for setting up such facilities",""],[1,"169","5","National Logistics Corridor Development","development of a logistics corridor that would connect the international gateways for maritime and air transport using both road and railway networks within the country specifically between Colombo and Trincomalee, as well as Colombo and Hambantota",""],[1,"170","1","Transhipment Port Value Addition and Trade Facilitation Reform","should be exploited for value addition as transhipment ports by attracting more shipping lines, improving flow of information and realignment of regulatory procedures and trade facilitation.",""],[1,"170","2","National Multimodal Transport Strategic Plan","government should collate all available transport sector plans and studies into a 10 year national multimodal transport strategic plan which will include development strategies for different transport networks including highways, railways, bus transport and air transport.",""],[1,"170","2","Transport Investment Alignment Policy","It will be the policy of the government that the public investment on transport sector infrastructure and services in each budget, be allocated on the basis of alignment to policy actions set out herein.",""]],"38":[[1,"166","4","Traffic Impact Assessment and Urban Traffic Audit Requirement","The government will make traffic impact assessment reports compulsory on new constructions and traffic audits in all municipal urban areas and national roads before the end of 2020.",""],[1,"166","5","Expanded Environmental Assessment for Transport Infrastructure","The environmental assessment process which by legislation provides for study and mitigation of the impacts will continue.",""],[1,"167","6","Urban Traffic and Motorization Management Measures","Intervene in managing future motorization and in particular the traffic levels in urban areas.",""],[1,"168","1","Electronic Road User Charging Reform","Convert vehicle taxes at importation gradually to road user taxes and levied on the basis of charging for road space used and its competing economic value through road user charges levied electronically in urban areas where traffic levels need to be controlled.",""]],"39":[[1,"26","4","Multi-Modal Transport and Logistics Network Development","Multi-modal transport & logistics networks to be developed by 2018 with strategic plans to (a) develop domestic aviation, (b) improve international air travel and (c) improve export facilitation and port development.",""],[1,"36","3","Transshipment, Logistics, and Commercial Hub Development","Maximise Sri Lanka's geostrategic potential to serve as an emerging transhipment and logistics hub as well as a commercial hub connecting different regions.",""],[1,"160","1","Private Port-Terminal and PPP Airport and Port Arrangements","Recent initiatives of allowing private port-terminals and consideration of PPP arrangements for airports and ports are observed as a policy change.",""],[1,"167","2","Integrated National Logistics Network Development","Such logistics networks have to be developed starting in 2020 by integrating multi modal transport networks in order to make the supply chain management efficient in terms of eliminating delays, wastage and lost economic opportunities.",""],[1,"167","2","Inter-Regional and Inter-City Transport Facility Development","Inter-regional and inter-city transport facilities will be developed to provide users with choices of modes as well as convenient inter-modal integration at multimodal transport terminals.",""],[1,"167","2","Domestic Air Transport Open Access Policy","In this respect domestic air transport will be provided open access by 2018.",""],[1,"167","2","Seaport and Airport Capacity Expansion and Modernization","The gateways for International transport such as the seaports and airports will be provided increased capacity to meet the demand and market conditions while ensuring that the highest level of technology and modernization is made available to make travel to and from Sri Lanka efficient and convenient, and fully integrated with the internal transport networks especially the railways.",""],[1,"167","2","Strategic Plans for Domestic Aviation, Air Travel, and Port Development","The government will before the end of 2018 develop strategic plans to (a) develop domestic aviation, (b) improve international air travel and (c) improve export facilitation and port development.",""]],"40":[[1,"26","2","Transport Safety Improvement Allocation","To provide an allocation of 5% of capital investment in the sector for transport safety improvements.",""],[1,"26","3","Transport Infrastructure and Services Environmental Assessment Framework","Assess transport infrastructure and services from 2020 based on: a) use of physical resources, b) number of beneficiaries, c) use of renewable energy d) environmental impacts and e) vehicle-km and fuel consumption.",""],[1,"26","6","Stakeholder Consultation Requirement for Major Projects","Such projects will proceed only after consultations with all stakeholder communities likely to be impacted.",""],[1,"166","2","Vision Zero Transport Safety Improvement Measures","Every accident, especially those that cause death and injury has to be investigated to ensure they would not re-occur by taking steps to improve standards in design of vehicles and infrastructure, operation, training, regulations, monitoring and enforcement aimed at Vision Zero or the pursuit of the complete elimination of transport fatalities by 2030.",""],[1,"166","3","Transport Safety Institutional Mechanism","The government, before the end of 2018, must set up a strong and independent institutional mechanism where possible with private sector partnerships to ensure justice for those affected by travel accidents and take leadership in ensuring the compliance of this policy across multiple agencies in the transport sector.",""],[1,"166","3","Transport Safety Investment Allocation","An allocation of 5 per cent of all transport sector capital investment should be allocated for transport safety improvements from 2020.",""]],"41":[[1,"168","12","Road Network Utilization and Management Improvement","Such a plan will give special emphasis on (a) improving the utilization and management of the existing road network,",""],[1,"168","12","Multimodal New Roads Planning Initiative","planning of new roads as part of multi modal transport network",""],[1,"169","1","Metro Region Connectivity Improvement","development in providing speedy connections between metro regions",""],[1,"169","1","Bus Priority and Multimodal Road Access Measures","prioritizing space for bus transport services on roads and ensuring space for multimodal access",""],[1,"169","1","Road Safety Improvement and Vision Zero Measures","prioritizing steps to improve road safety and achieve the vision zero goal by 2030",""],[1,"169","1","Urban On-Street Parking Regulation Reform","bring regulations for the removal or restriction of on-street parking on national roads in urban areas",""],[1,"169","1","Environmental Impact Mitigation for Road Projects","complete mitigation of environmental impacts of road construction and operation",""],[1,"169","1","National Road Environmental Quality Management","maintenance of quality of life and physical environment around national roads",""],[1,"169","1","Mandatory Pre-Investment Feasibility Study Requirement","ensuring that professionally acceptable feasibility studies are completed together with comparison of alternatives before investments are made",""],[1,"169","1","Road Infrastructure Disaster Resilience Measures","resilience to disasters",""],[1,"169","1","Urban Space Protection in Road Planning","ensuring no negative impacts on the quality of urban spaces within cities",""],[1,"169","1","Stakeholder Consultation for New Road Planning","including measures for consultation with stakeholder communities whenever new roads are planned",""]],"42":[[1,"16","3","Air Pollution Prevention and Sustainable Urban Transport Systems","Take early action to prevent air pollution due to heavy traffic congestion in major cities and introduce smart and sustainable transportation systems including non-motorized transport, electric vehicles and electrically operated public transport systems.",""],[1,"30","4","Electric and Hybrid Vehicle Import and Tax Incentive Policy","Strong policy decisions on importation of vehicles, tax reductions for electric and hybrid vehicles especially on public transport is a necessity.",""],[1,"89","12","Electric Vehicle Import Incentives and Fossil Fuel Vehicle Taxation","Provide duty free facilities to import electric vehicles and introduce enhanced taxes to petrol/diesel vehicles.",""],[1,"89","13","Solar Vehicle Battery Charging Station Network","Facilitate setting up of solar operated vehicle battery charging stations all over the country.",""],[1,"103","2","Long-Term Pollution-Free Transport Planning","Planning for pollution free transport in the long term with long range transport systems can reduce vehicle congestion and air pollution.",""],[1,"103","2","Dedicated Bus Lanes and Rapid Bus Transit Systems","The short-term plans for dedicated lanes for buses, rapid bus transit systems, and building flyovers at key junctions will ease our traffic problem and reduce air pollution.",""],[1,"103","2","Electric Vehicle and Solar Charging Incentive Scheme","Encouraging people to switch to electric cars and setting up of solar charging stations through providing tax concessions and incentives to private sector will eliminate the air pollution.",""],[1,"103","2","Fossil Fuel Discouragement Measures for Transport, Industry, and Power","Government strategies to discourage fossil fuel use for transport, industry and power generation through various financial and non-financial measures will further improve our air quality.",""],[1,"203","3","City Vehicle Entry Reduction Measures","Explore methods to limit vehicles entering the city.",""],[1,"203","4","Environment-Friendly Urban Transport System","Organize an environment friendly transport system within the city (Bicycles, LPG or electrically powered public transport).",""],[1,"203","5","Low-Emission Vehicle Access Restriction in City Limits","Allow low emitting vehicles (eg. electric and hybrid vehicles) only within the city limits.",""],[1,"203","6","Electric Vehicle Concessions and Renewable Charging Infrastructure","Provide concessions for electric vehicle users and providers, and arrange for charging stations operated with renewable energy like solar power.",""],[1,"203","7","Urban Traffic Re-routing Facilities","Provide facilities for vehicles that pass through the city to re-route and avoid converging to the centre of the city.",""],[1,"203","10","Dedicated Bus and Priority Lane Transport Measures","Provide dedicated lanes for buses and other large vehicles, and establish priority lanes to encourage carpooling.",""],[1,"203","11","Alternative Working Hours for Urban Traffic Management","Arrange for alternative working hours to reduce traffic congestion in cities.",""],[1,"207","7","Low-Emission Vehicle Access Control for Major Cities","if vehicles entering Kandy, Colombo and other major town and cities are controlled, and only zero or near zero emitting vehicles are allowed to enter, air pollution will reach near zero level in the city by 2020",""],[1,"284","5","Urban Air Pollution Prevention and Sustainable Transport Systems","Take early action to prevent air pollution due to heavy traffic congestion in major cities and introduce smart and sustainable transportation systems including non-motorized transport, electric vehicles and electrically operated public transport systems.",""],[1,"286","4","Long-Term Pollution-Free Transport Planning","Planning for pollution free transport in the long term with long range transport systems can reduce vehicle congestion and air pollution.","Ministry of Megapolis and Cities"],[1,"286","4","Dedicated Bus Lanes and Rapid Bus Transit Expansion","The short-term plans for dedicated lanes for buses, rapid bus transit systems, and building flyovers at key junctions will ease our traffic problem and reduce air pollution.",""],[1,"286","4","Electric Vehicle and Solar Charging Incentive Scheme","Encouraging people to switch to electric cars and setting up solar charging stations through the provision of tax concessions and incentives to the private sector, will eliminate air pollution.",""],[1,"286","4","Transport and Energy Fossil Fuel Discouragement Measures","Government strategies to discourage fossil fuel use for transport, industry and power generation through various financial and non-financial measures will further improve our air quality.",""],[1,"299","6","Low-Emission Vehicle Access Control in Major Cities","if vehicles entering Kandy, Colombo and other major towns and cities are controlled, and only zero or near zero emitting vehicles are allowed to enter, air pollution will reach a near zero level in the city by 2020",""],[1,"299","7","Urban Greening and Pedestrian Walkway Development","Forest patches and pedestrian walkways, will attract both foreign and local tourists, thereby stimulating economic growth.",""]],"43":[[1,"160","1","Rural Road Construction Programme","Rural road building figured prominently in providing access to basic services for many decades, while in recent years, expressway building in an attempt to improve inter-city travel has taken centre stage.",""],[1,"160","1","Expressway Expansion Programme","Rural road building figured prominently in providing access to basic services for many decades, while in recent years, expressway building in an attempt to improve inter-city travel has taken centre stage.",""],[1,"168","10","Future Road Building Program Alignment","Its future road building program should be aligned to developing a well-connected road network within a multi-modal transport network.",""],[1,"168","11","National Road Development Strategic Plan","Develop a 10-year national road development strategic plan before end of 2018 as part of the aforementioned national multi modal transport development strategy.",""],[1,"184","6","Expressway Construction and Highway Upgrading Programme","The presently available set of expressways and the ongoing set of projects connect Colombo to Matara and further extends to Hambantota.",""],[1,"184","6","Colombo-Dambulla Expressway Project","Others connecting Colombo to Dambulla via Kurunegala will positively contribute to the movements between the locations that falls within the development corridors.",""],[1,"184","6","Regional Highway Facilities Upgrading Programme","Fast improvements to rail service as indicated above and the upgrading of the existing regional highway facilities will adequately serve demands up to 2030.",""],[1,"184","7","Inter-Regional Highway Improvement and Maintenance","the existing highways that connect the proposed metro regions and the main cities must be improved and maintained on priority basis.",""]],"44":[[1,"160","1","Feasibility Studies for New Urban Transport Technologies","Feasibility studies have been initiated for new urban transport technologies such as light rapid transit, water transport and for railway electrification and modernization.",""],[1,"160","1","Railway Electrification and Modernization Studies","Feasibility studies have been initiated for new urban transport technologies such as light rapid transit, water transport and for railway electrification and modernization.",""],[1,"168","6","National Railway Network Modernization Programme","Pursue the systematic development of the national railway network to position it as a competitive modern-day transport option by the year 2030 for both passenger and freight transport.",""],[1,"168","7","Rail Transport Market Specialization Strategy","Strategically focus into competitive niche areas for rail transport such as (a) urban passenger, (b) long-distance express passenger and (c) bulk and long-distance freight transport markets.",""],[1,"168","8","National Railway Network Expansion","Allocate funds for 2020 with emphasis on (a) expanding railway network to cover the entire island as an alternate mode of transport to serve the long term mobility requirements including a new rail access to Kandy extendable to Uva and Eastern Province as well as to Sabaragamuwa",""],[1,"168","8","Rail Electrification and Infrastructure Upgrade","improving reliability and speed of travel through electrification and other infrastructure improvements",""],[1,"168","8","Rail Customer Service Modernization","modernize customer services through electronic ticketing, air conditioning, improved stations, integrated access by buses and three wheelers, park and ride facilities etc.",""]],"45":[[1,"184","4","Railway Electrification and Corridor Upgrade","Electrification of the rail between Aluthgama and Polgahawela is already proposed by the railway improvement master plan.",""],[1,"184","4","Kurunegala-Habarana Rail Link Development","In the Railway Improvement master plan, there is a proposal to link Kurunegala to Habarana, via Dambulla.",""],[1,"184","4","Habarana-Trincomalee Rail Electrification and Speed Upgrade","This length and the available rail line from Habarana to Trincomalee should be improved by 2030 into electrified, fast moving trains to enhance the linkage among locations within East-West corridor.",""],[1,"184","5","National Rail Service Electrification and Corridor Upgrading","there will be an electrified train service available from Aluthgama via Colombo to Trincomalee, via Kurunegala, Dambulla and Habarana by 2030.",""],[1,"184","5","Southern Rail Service Improvement and Extension","the existing rail services from Aluthgama to Matara needs to be improved.",""],[1,"184","5","Southern Rail Extension to Hambanthota","this service can be extended from Marata to Hambanthota.",""],[1,"184","5","Northern Urban Rail Service Intensification","In the northern urban corridor rail services should be intensified between Kilinochchi and Kankasanthurai by 2025.",""],[1,"184","5","Eastern Rail Service Improvement and Extension","rail services between Valachchenai and Baticalloa needs to be improved, while a potential extension of the same line up to Ampara via Kalmunai by 2025 is planned.",""],[1,"184","5","National Rail Network Upgrading for Inter-Regional Transport","The other available network and the services in them should also be improved in order to facilitate inter-regional transportation needs.",""],[1,"186","2","High-Priority Highway and Railway Development Projects","The initial planning and implementation of the high priority projects, such as the highway and railway development, would not take longer than and should be realized by 2025",""]],"46":[[1,"42","3","Social Safety Net Expansion for the Poor and Vulnerable","A simultaneous focus on providing adequate safety nets to safeguard the poor and vulnerable will help in ensuing that growth is inclusive, as recognized in Vision 2025.",""],[1,"69","8","Social Safety Net Efficiency and Disaster Readiness Enhancement","Improve the efficiency and effectiveness of social safety nets, and national readiness to respond to financial distress of the poor and vulnerable during natural disasters and other such events.",""],[1,"71","6","Rationalization of Transfer and Subsidy Programmes","Rationalize wasteful expenditures, including poorly targeted transfer and subsidy programmes for poor households.",""],[1,"71","10","Social Protection Framework Review and Welfare Benefit Board Strengthening","Re-examine social protection framework and ensure that the Welfare Benefit Board plays an active role in providing adequate social safety nets for the poor and vulnerable segments of society",""],[1,"75","12","Precise Targeting in Social Protection Programmes","Ensure precise targeting in social protection programmes",""],[1,"76","14","Precise Targeting in Social Welfare Programmes","Ensure precise targeting in social welfare programmes for the neediest",""],[1,"93","1","Well-Targeted Social Support Interventions","These could be addressed through well targeted interventions at national, provincial and local levels such as social housing for the poor, access to garden plots for food production, legal aid, etc.",""],[1,"93","3","Basic Needs Support Public Policy","Public policy to recognize the need to satisfy the basic needs of the people and support ventures that make a direct contribution to meeting the above needs",""],[1,"95","3","Evidence-Based Social Policy Financing","Adopt evidence based social policies backed by adequate funding to address issues of social insecurity and social exclusion.",""],[1,"97","5","Social Protection and Income Security Measures","Old age Pensions, employment and income security, disability support, child endowments, and national health insurance.",""],[1,"101","2","Social Safety Nets for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","A simultaneous focus on providing adequate safety nets to safeguard the poor and vulnerable will help in ensuing that growth is inclusive, as recognized in Vision 2025.",""]],"47":[[1,"18","2","Measures to Prevent Gender-Based Violence","Take special measures to arrest gender based violence.",""],[1,"33","8","Legal Reform and Enforcement Strengthening for Remedy and Relief","Reform the law in all relevant areas using experience based on past research and policy, strengthen law enforcement to prevent impunity, and provide access to remedy and relief, especially in the case of violence against women and sexual gender based violence.",""],[1,"33","9","Workplace Harassment Reporting and Prevention Policy","Introduce policies to encourage reporting of harassments.",""],[1,"33","9","Human Resource Training for Workplace Harassment Prevention","Provide human resource training by professionals including health professionals to halt its prevalence at the workplace.",""],[1,"97","5","Measures to Address Violence Against Women and Children","Effective measures by law enforcement and national and criminal justice system to address violence against women and children need to be taken to ensure justice and opportunity to them.",""]],"48":[[1,"33","6","Retirement Benefits and Post-Retirement Labour Protection Policy","Develop policies that provide adequate retirement benefits for the elderly and protection against post-retirement labour exploitation in the informal sector.",""],[1,"45","2","Integrated Retirement Benefits and Older Women's Reskilling Plan","An integrated plan strengthens retirement benefits, re-skills 60+ year old women for better jobs.",""],[1,"99","5","Universal Workers' Pension Scheme","developing a pension scheme for all workers by amalgamating existing schemes",""]],"49":[[1,"253","2","Inclusive Program Space Mobilization for Poverty Reduction","Mobilize government, private sector and other non-government agencies to declare the space in their programs for the poor in response to the current national call on supporting the sustainable development process to reach the national goal of a poverty free Sri Lanka by 2030.",""],[1,"253","3","Disclosure of Sustainable Production Opportunities for the Poor","The government and the private sector organizations disclose opportunities available in their sustainable production programs for the poor to benefit.",""],[1,"253","5","Countrywide Citizen Engagement and Community Self-Managed Development Campaign","Launch and regularly refresh a countrywide campaign to increase effective citizen engagement in public affairs in rural as well as urban economies, mainstreaming a community self-managed development approach in all Grama Niladhari Divisions with targets for 2020, 2025 and 2030 giving priority to the poorer and disadvantaged areas and community groups.",""],[1,"253","8","Community Platform-Based Village Economic Institutions","Promote and scale up the use of community platforms with community self-managed, inclusive, and accountable economic institutions in the villages, with information, decision making power, and supplementary resources.",""],[1,"253","11","Community-Driven Development and Local Investment Management in Grama Niladhari Divisions","Inclusive, accountable and formally organized community institutions will be active in managing investments for the increasing income in 5,000 Grama Niladhari Divisions, adopting community driven development approaches addressing the priority needs of the bottom 40 per cent of the",""],[1,"254","4","Converged Government and Private Sector Development Interventions for Bottom 40 Percent Communities","Convergence of relevant government and private sector development interventions for providing basic and growing needs of the bottom 40 per cent of the population will be evidenced in the poorer and disadvantaged areas.",""],[1,"306","1","Local Microeconomic Interventions for Inclusive Growth","Ensure that macroeconomic adjustments favour micro economic interventions at the local level for inclusive growth, with gender and youth specific components.",""],[1,"306","2","Multi-level Production Sector Partnership and Value Chain Support","Mobilize partnerships among individuals and enterprises in production sectors ranging from divisional through provincial to national levels, improving the supply/value chains of growth potential products and services benefiting the poor, with supply side inputs on demand driven processes.",""],[1,"306","3","Agency Action Plan Declaration for Poverty-Free Sri Lanka","Request public, private and people's sector agencies responding to the national call to contribute towards the goal of ensuring a poverty free Sri Lanka by 2030, to declare their action plans.",""],[1,"306","4","Countrywide Citizen Engagement Campaign in Public Affairs","Launch and regularly refresh a countrywide campaign of citizen engagement in public affairs, giving priority to poorer communities and lagging areas, using a community self-managed development approach.",""],[1,"306","5","Inclusive and Accountable Community Institutions","Promote inclusive and accountable community institutions practicing principles of good governance and ethics, as platforms for the convergence of services from various programmes directly focusing on the poor and the disadvantaged, to overcome poverty and inequality.",""],[1,"306","6","Community-Driven Development for Local Investment Management","Inclusive, accountable and formally organized community institutions will be active in managing investments from increasing income in 5,000 Grama Niladhari Divisions (GNDs) by adopting a community driven development approach, thereby addressing the priority needs of the bottom 40 per cent of the population.",""],[1,"306","7","Countrywide Civic Education and Community-Managed Development Training Campaign","A countrywide civic education campaign mainly focused on training communities to undertake community managed development, will be carried out through specifically identified training institutions related to certain Local Governments by 2020, demonstrating scalability to cover the rest of the country by 2025 and 2030 progressively.",""],[1,"306","8","Divisional Secretariat Development Planning and Coordination","Divisional Secretariats will play a key role in the planning and coordination of development interventions, specifically integrating Samurdhi safety net interventions and other programs to facilitate the sustainable management of resources, thereby creating a more holistic approach to poverty alleviation.",""],[1,"306","9","Government and Private Sector Investment Partnerships for Bottom 40 Percent Areas","The convergence of relevant government and private sector development interventions for providing the basic and growing needs of the bottom 40 per cent of the population, will be evidenced by the poorer and disadvantaged areas of over 1,000 GNDs and communities being covered through government and private sector investments and partnerships on improved supply/value chains of crops, products and services, with growth potential for technology adoption on innovations, import reduction and/or increasing exports.",""]],"50":[[1,"222","6","National Transport Policy on Connectivity and Passenger Safety","Introduce a national transport policy that not only focuses on rural-urban connectivity but also ensures zero tolerance of women's sexual harassment in buses and trains.",""],[1,"222","7","Legal Reform for Enforcement Against VAW/SGBV","Introduce law reforms to ensure proper law enforcement against VAW/SGBV by the police.",""],[1,"222","8","Workplace Harassment Reporting and Prevention Policy","Introduce policies to encourage the reporting of harassments.",""],[1,"222","8","Professional Human Resource Training for Workplace Harassment Prevention","Provide human resource training by professionals including health professionals to halt its prevalence at the workplace.",""],[1,"222","9","Violence Against Women and Girls Attitudinal Change Programmes","Implement educational, community and media programmes to create an attitudinal change towards zero tolerance of VAW/IPV/SGBV.",""],[1,"222","11","Community-Based De-stigmatization and Social Acceptance Programmes for Women Victims of IPV/SGBV","Introduce community based programmes towards the de-stigmatizing and social acceptance of women victims of IPV/SGBV.",""],[1,"261","2","Anti-Discrimination Legislation","Introduce anti-discrimination legislation - such as that adopted in South Africa post-apartheid, to increase representation of women and minorities in national institutions.",""],[1,"262","8","School-Based Gender Stereotype and Discrimination Reduction Initiative","Challenge stereotypes and gender discrimination within the education system at a young age",""],[1,"262","9","Gender-Sensitive and Inclusive Workplace Policies","Initiate and implement policies that are gender sensitive and inclusive within the work place.",""],[1,"262","12","Strengthen Laws Protecting Women and Access to Justice","Refine and strengthen existing laws that protect women and provide access to justice, combined with effective implementation of such laws.",""],[1,"262","13","Women’s Economic Empowerment and Skills Development Support","Equip women to take on new and challenging responsibilities, especially in the face of dire economic situations, in areas worst-affected by the war.",""],[1,"266","2","Gender Mainstreaming Institutionalization","During the past two years, the Sri Lankan government has focused on developing policies and Action Plans, which, in addition to the National Reconciliation Policy, includes specific efforts to address issues such as violence against women, empowering female headed households, women's entrepreneurship development, and institutionalizing gender mainstreaming.",""],[1,"266","2","Violence Against Women Action Measures","During the past two years, the Sri Lankan government has focused on developing policies and Action Plans, which, in addition to the National Reconciliation Policy, includes specific efforts to address issues such as violence against women, empowering female headed households, women's entrepreneurship development, and institutionalizing gender mainstreaming.",""],[1,"266","2","Women's Economic Empowerment Measures","During the past two years, the Sri Lankan government has focused on developing policies and Action Plans, which, in addition to the National Reconciliation Policy, includes specific efforts to address issues such as violence against women, empowering female headed households, women's entrepreneurship development, and institutionalizing gender mainstreaming.",""],[1,"287","4","Measures to Reduce Social Inequality and Gender-Based Inequality","Take measures to arrest the trend towards greater social inequality in terms of income distribution and regional disparities, in particular rural urban disparities.",""],[1,"287","8","Rule of Law and Personal Safety Strengthening Measures","Strengthen the rule of law, ensure personal safety and reinforce the regulatory functions of governance at all levels, in order to stem the tendencies towards lawlessness, abuse of power and corruption.",""],[1,"301","8","National Transport Policy on Connectivity and Passenger Safety","Introduce a national transport policy that not only focuses on rural-urban connectivity, but also ensures zero tolerance of women's sexual harassment in buses and trains.",""],[1,"301","9","Legal Reform and Law Enforcement Strengthening for VAW and SGBV","Reform laws in all areas identified by a well-established evidence base of research and policy, and strengthen law enforcement to prevent impunity and provide access to remedy and relief, especially for Violence Against Women (VAW) and Sexual and Gender Based Violence (SGBV).",""],[1,"301","10","Workplace Harassment Reporting and HR Training Policy","Introduce policies to encourage the reporting of harassment.",""],[1,"302","3","Gender Wage Gap Monitoring and Workplace Safety Policy","Adopting policies to monitor and abolish gender wage gaps and ensure the accessibility, safety and security of women in relation to public transport and workplaces, as well as strengthening the prevention of domestic violence will further encourage women into the labour force, facilitate their wellbeing and increase their productivity.",""],[1,"307","5","Gender Equality Enhancement in Government Services","Implement immediate efforts to enhance gender equality in all Government services, particularly at the highest levels.",""],[1,"308","3","Gender Equality Policy and Action Plan Package","During the past two years, the Sri Lankan government has focused on developing policies and action plans, which, in addition to the National Reconciliation Policy, includes specific efforts to address issues such as VAW, empowering female headed households, women's entrepreneurship development, and institutionalizing gender mainstreaming.",""]],"51":[[1,"14","7","Targeted Social Welfare Programme Rationalization","Rationalize wasteful expenditure, particularly by ensuring the precise targeting of social welfare programmes for poor households",""],[1,"14","9","Senior Citizen Participation and Retirement Social Security Support","Provide better opportunities for the growing senior citizen population to contribute their experience for sustainable development and improve their retirement social security safety nets.",""],[1,"17","2","Income Support for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Other effective measures that are necessary to reduce income inequalities include progressive income taxation, improvement of public educational services to cut down private tuition, introduction of a contributory health insurance scheme to minimize out of pocket medical expenses, adequate income support to the poor and vulnerable groups on the basis of a reliable and fair means test and the improvement of public transport services.",""],[1,"17","3","Progressive Taxation and Social Investment for Minimum Household Income","Implement measures to reduce income inequality through a twin strategy of progressive taxation and enhanced social investments leading to a guaranteed minimum household income and social security for all.",""],[1,"17","6","Social Inequality Reduction Measures","Take measures to arrest the trend towards greater social inequality in terms of income distribution and regional disparities, in particular rural urban disparities.",""],[1,"17","6","Gender Inequality Reduction Measures","Reduce gender-based inequality.",""],[1,"17","8","Targeted Social Services Improvement and Outreach","Take measures to improve the professional quality and outreach of various targeted social services to empower marginalized and disadvantaged groups such as the poor, disabled, the elderly, mentally ill, etc.",""]],"52":[[1,"39","6","Military Occupied Land Restitution and Compensation Mechanism","Complete hand-over/restitution of military occupied lands in the North and East.",""]],"53":[[1,"21","8","Power Transmission and Distribution Infrastructure Upgrade","The reliability of power supply has to be ensured with regular upgrades of the transmission and distribution infrastructure.",""],[1,"21","8","Accountability for Distribution Losses","Distribution licensees should be made accountable for the losses and in their respective areas",""],[1,"21","8","Generation Licensee Efficiency Improvement Mandate","the generation licensees should also be mandated for constant upgrades and efficiency improvements when and where necessary.",""],[1,"22","6","Transmission and Distribution System Upgrade Programme","Regular upgrades of the transmission and distribution system should take place to ensure adequate power system reliability.",""],[1,"43","4","Smart Grid and Distributed Energy Management Initiatives","Implementation of \"smart\" and sustainable initiatives will complement the renewable energy initiatives in the electricity sector, to facilitate a wide range of distributed generation, smart grid, smart metering and demand management options that are planned.",""],[1,"126","6","Science-Based Renewable Integration Planning and System Review","Base the entire management of the system from the planning stage to implementation (timing and locations) and operation on well proven scientific studies and on high level research into handling intermittency issues related to the introduction of renewable sources for generation and also a thorough review of system technical parameters in the whole system.",""],[1,"131","4","Renewable Energy Transmission Infrastructure Investment","Improve the transmission infrastructure substantially to transmit the power generated from NRE sources to load centres.",""],[1,"131","4","Large-Scale NRE Project Development","Such development programmes can also launch large scale NRE projects, typically in the range of 100MW which will contribute in required measures towards the 20 per cent target.",""],[1,"140","6","Renewable Energy Share Optimization and Pumped Storage Power Plant Development","In LTGEP, other renewable energy share is optimized and maintained at more than 20 per cent by 2020 onwards and would result in reduction of emissions from power generation considerably.",""],[1,"142","3","Renewable Energy Share Protection and Expansion Policy","A paradigm shift of policy is envisaged to defend and improve the share of renewables in the primary energy supply from the 55 per cent level maintained during the last decade",""],[1,"142","4","Wind and Solar Power Expansion under LTGEP","414MW of Wind and 410MW of Solar by 2020 and 894MW of Wind and 1009MW of Solar are to be introduced by 2030 according to the 2018/2037 LTGEP.",""]],"54":[[1,"16","7","Renewable Energy Transition for Power, Industry, and Transport","Replace fossil fuel based power generation for national grid by using modern renewable energy and promote application of renewable energy in industrial and commercial applications.",""],[1,"16","7","Tax Reduction for Renewable Energy Vehicles and Machinery","Reduce taxes on vehicles and machinery run on renewable energy - such as electric cars.",""],[1,"22","1","Indigenous Renewable Energy Development","Hence steps should be taken to develop indigenous renewable energy sources such as wind, solar and biomass being aware of the economic burden of 153 MUS$",""],[1,"22","1","Techno-Economic Evaluation of Renewable Energy Targets","renewable energy targets should be introduced only after thorough techno-economic and sustainability evaluation.",""],[1,"89","8","Renewable Energy Technology Expansion and Fossil Fuel Phase-Out","Introduce more renewable energy technologies phasing out non-renewables which are more environment damaging.",""],[1,"89","15","Methane Technology Transfer for Household and Transport Use","Facilitate transfer of technologies to use methane instead of kerosene and LP gas for household activities and in transport.",""],[1,"90","1","Biogas Production Education and Promotion for Farmers","Encourage and educate dairy and other farmers on biogas production.",""],[1,"95","7","Transition to Greener Materials and Energy Sources","The need to phase out certain non-renewable raw materials and energy sources and their replacement with greener materials and energy offer opportunities to open up new lines of production and service provision.",""],[1,"284","9","Renewable Energy Transition for Grid and End-Use Applications","Replace fossil fuel based power generation for national grid by using modern renewable energy and promote application of renewable energy in industrial and commercial applications.",""],[1,"284","9","Tax Reduction for Renewable Energy Vehicles and Machinery","Reduce taxes on vehicles and machinery run on renewable energy - such as electric cars.",""],[1,"285","2","Organic Agriculture and Forest Cover Expansion Targets","The targets established through the initiatives by H.E. the President to make agriculture organic and increase the forest cover to 35 percent, and sectoral targets such as the use of renewable energy for generating 20 percent of electricity by 2020, the introduction of a campaign for solar based electricity supply for households and commercial buildings and net-metering, are key examples.",""],[1,"285","2","Solar Electricity Supply and Net-Metering Campaign","the introduction of a campaign for solar based electricity supply for households and commercial buildings and net-metering, are key examples.",""],[1,"291","3","Long-Term Generation Expansion Plan","Implement rational plans, especially the scientifically derived and robust Long-Term Generation Expansion Plan.",""],[1,"291","6","Indigenous Renewable Energy Development","Take prudent steps to develop indigenous renewable energy sources such as wind, solar and biomass, to significantly improve the security of supply, while reducing carbon emissions.",""],[1,"292","1","Renewable Energy Systems Development","Most of the renewable energy systems such as Solar PV, both small scale roof top and MW scale grid connected power plants, wind, and to a certain extent biomass, are being actively pursued by the private sector in particular and the Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB) in the case of wind.",""],[1,"292","3","Smart Metering Infrastructure Pilot Expansion","The CEB and LECO have already commenced pilot implementation of smart metering infrastructure, and will implement several more pilot projects in 2018 and 2019.",""],[1,"292","3","Customer-Requested Smart and Pre-Paid Meter Provision","Further, smart and pre-paid meters would be provided on request to any customer starting from 2018, to enable customers to manage and monitor their own consumption, with or without utility intervention.",""],[1,"292","4","Renewable Energy Share Protection Policy Shift","A paradigm shift of policy is envisaged to defend and improve the share of renewables in the primary energy supply from the 55 percent level maintained during the last decade.",""],[1,"292","4","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Commitment","Sri Lanka is committed to reducing Green House Gas (GHG) emissions by 20 percent (4 percent unconditional and 16 percent conditional) from the Business as Usual scenario.",""],[1,"292","5","Wind and Solar Power Expansion under the LTGEP","894MW of wind and 1,009MW of solar are to be introduced by 2030 according to the 2018/2037 Long-Term Generation Expansion Plan (LTGEP).",""],[1,"292","6","Smart and Sustainable Electricity Sector Initiatives","Implementation of \"smart\" and sustainable initiatives will complement the renewable energy initiatives in the electricity sector, to facilitate a wide range of distributed generation, smart grid, smart metering and demand management options that are planned.",""]],"55":[[1,"21","6","Long-Term Generation Expansion Plan Implementation","Hence it is of utmost importance to implement the plans -- especially the scientifically derived and robust Long Term Generation Expansion Plan that has already taken into account development of power plants using a mix of energy sources.",""],[1,"21","7","Energy Pricing Reform and Demand-Side Management Policy Interventions","Energy prices should reflect the true cost to the economy properly adjusted to ensure prudence in utility management and any policy objective like eliminating wasteful practices, safeguarding vulnerable groups, protecting the environment, and enhancing industrial and any other growth sectors of the economy that would yield high economic returns.",""],[1,"22","2","Tariff Policy and Financial Discipline for Utility Sector Investment","domestic borrowings to meet operational losses can only be minimized by proper tariff policies, while the external debt burden should be eased through external financing",""],[1,"22","4","Long-Term Generation Expansion Plan Implementation","Implement rational plans especially the scientifically derived and robust Long Term Generation Expansion Plan",""],[1,"22","5","Sustainable Energy Pricing and External Financing Mobilization","Mobilize funds for sector development through sustainable energy pricing policies and appropriate external financing.",""],[1,"23","1","Inclusive Consultation Requirement for Energy Projects","Government must ensure that all energy projects proceed only after inclusive and meaningful consultations with stakeholder communities potentially impacted by their development.",""],[1,"124","6","Least-Cost Power Generation Expansion Plan Implementation","Implement the long term least cost generation expansion plan of the CEB.",""],[1,"127","3","Long-Term Power System Planning and Implementation","Successive governments intervened when CEB followed legal procedures to plan the generating system for the longer term, and to implement the plan.",""],[1,"127","9","CEB Generation Project Planning and Accountability Reform","Allow the CEB to follow the procedures laid out in the Electricity Act 2009, to plan and implement generation projects, without government interference.",""],[1,"127","9","CEB Project Delivery Performance and Cost Accountability","Demand performance from the CEB to implement projects on-schedule, and make the CEB fully accountable to generation costs.",""],[1,"128","1","Transmission and Distribution Loss Reduction Programme","all licensees (CEB Transmission, CEB distribution and LECO) should be encouraged to work towards the target specified for each segment of their respective networks.",""],[1,"128","6","Financial Separation and Accountability Reform for CEB Entities","Introduce financial separation of each generation, transmission and distribution entity of CEB, making each unit accountable for its key performance indices (KPIs), including loss targets.",""],[1,"131","2","Balanced Power Generation Mix Maintenance","Maintain a good balance between renewables and conventional generation to ensure technical and economic stability of the grid supply.",""],[1,"131","3","NRE Resource and Electricity Demand Study","Conduct a careful study of the NRE resources and electricity demand that would yield a road map for integration of more renewable energy with definite capacities.",""],[1,"131","3","NRE Integration Plan Development","Such information can be used to develop an NRE integration plan which can be used to encourage public and private sector investments in the sector.",""],[1,"133","3","CEB Financial Ring-Fencing and Bulk Supply Account Establishment","financial ring fencing generation, transmission and distribution businesses of CEB and establishment of the bulk supply transaction account recommended by the tariff methodology, will result in recognition of the subsidy due from GOSL for providing electricity below the cost of supply to a majority of the household category.",""],[1,"136","7","Timely Implementation of Pre-determined Projects","Timely implementation of pre-determined projects and ensuring maximum benefit to the economy by each individual project.",""],[1,"291","4","Sustainable Energy Pricing and External Financing Mobilization","Mobilize funds for sector development through sustainable energy pricing policies and appropriate external financing.",""],[1,"291","5","Transmission and Distribution System Upgrade Programme","Carry out regular upgrades of the transmission and distribution system to ensure adequate power system reliability.",""],[1,"291","7","Offshore Gas Development in the Mannar Basin","Give priority to offshore gas development in the Mannar Basin and elsewhere, to increase independence from imported energy, reduce foreign exchange costs, and strengthen the creditworthiness of the national economy.",""],[1,"291","8","Inclusive Consultation Requirement for Energy Projects","Ensure that all energy projects proceed only after inclusive and meaningful consultations with stakeholder communities potentially impacted by their development.",""]],"56":[[1,"125","6","Time-of-Use Tariff Retention and Removal of Generator Incentive","Hence this may be removed, while retaining the TOU.",""],[1,"125","7","Electricity Tariff Reform and Cost-Reflective Pricing Roadmap","Allow the PUCSL and CEB together with LECO to re-negotiate and arrive at a proper tariff structure and road map for tariff reforms and rebalancing to achieve the government's policy guideline requiring all customers to be charged a cost-reflective price.",""],[1,"125","8","Tariff Design Incorporating DSM Initiatives","The tariff making should meaningfully incorporate DSM initiatives mapped by the SLSEA.",""],[1,"133","3","CEB Tariff Methodology Implementation","Full implementation of the tariff methodology will ensure recovery of the cost of supply providing sufficient cash flows to meet energy costs and service its debt.",""],[1,"136","6","Energy Efficiency and Demand-Side Management Measures","Promote energy efficiency and other DSM measures for the efficient utilization of the infrastructure.",""],[1,"139","4","Large-Scale Energy Efficiency and Conservation Programme","In order to deploy a large-scale EE&C effort, these barriers have to be systematically removed.",""],[1,"139","5","Operation DSM","The programme will be led by a Presidential Task Force (PTF) and guided by a National Steering Committee (NSC) and implemented by a Programme Management Unit (PMU) within the SEA.",""],[1,"140","1","ODSM Monitoring, Reporting and Verification System","The ODSM will be a joint effort of several closely networked entities, whose relationships will be governed by a well-developed transaction processing system (TPS).",""],[1,"142","2","Smart Metering Infrastructure Pilot Expansion","CEB and LECO have already commenced pilot implementation of smart metering infrastructure, and will implement several more pilot projects in 2018 and 2019.",""],[1,"142","2","Customer-Requested Smart and Pre-Paid Meter Provision","Further, smart and pre-paid meters would be provided on request to any customer, starting in 2018, to enable customers to manage and monitor their own consumption, with or without utility intervention.",""],[1,"142","5","Smart and Sustainable Electricity Sector Initiatives","Implementation of \"smart\" and sustainable initiatives will complement the renewable energy initiatives in the electricity sector, to facilitate a wide range of distributed generation, smart grid, smart metering and demand management options that are planned.",""]],"57":[[1,"15","7","Solid Waste Disposal Site Development and Sanitary Landfill Programme","Solutions for solid waste includes finding suitable disposal sites, creating sanitary landfills, applying 3R practices, adopting effective policies and legislations for banning wasteful practices.",""],[1,"16","5","Environment-Friendly Waste Disposal Methods","Introduce environment friendly waste disposal methods.",""],[1,"87","6","National Waste Management Policy and Strategies Implementation","Implement the National Waste Management Policy and Strategies",""],[1,"87","7","Pilisaru Project Implementation","Take measures to realise the Pilisaru Project targets and objectives.",""],[1,"87","8","Municipal Waste Reduction and Recycling Programmes","Promote country wide programmes on recycling, reducing and rethinking of waste at municipality levels.",""],[1,"87","9","Urban Waste Sorting Centers","Establish waste sorting centers in large cities to increase economic value of recovered resources.",""],[1,"87","10","Private Sector Environmental Management and Recycling Support","Facilitate private sector in their efforts in environmental management including recycling.",""],[1,"87","11","Circular Economy Promotion","Encourage circular economy where waste becomes a resource.",""],[1,"87","12","Polythene and Plastic Use Reduction Measure","Discourage the use of polythene and plastics.",""],[1,"87","13","Biodegradable Packaging Materials Transition","Switch to biodegradable plastics for packaging materials wherever appropriate.",""],[1,"87","14","Hazardous Waste Collection and Disposal System","Introduce proper collection and disposal methods for hazardous waste.",""],[1,"87","15","Recyclable Material Collection Incentive Scheme","Introduce an incentive scheme- with a practical solution to collect reusable/recyclable material",""],[1,"87","16","Nationwide Industrial Waste Exchange","Using principle of industrial symbiosis, establish a nation-wide waste exchange where industries can buy segregated waste for their use.",""],[1,"87","17","Central Waste Recycling Park and Recycling Industry Development","Set Up a central waste recycling park and establish recycling industries for all major resource types (plastics, paper, textile pieces, glass, construction materials, wood wastes etc) and showcase proper recycling of different material and provide training to interested investors.",""],[1,"87","18","Ban Free Issue of Plastic Bags by Shops","Ban free issue of bags by shops - enable the law regarding this.",""],[1,"87","19","Private Sector Small Industry Recycling Incentive Programme","Incentivize small industries in private sector to commence recycling industries.",""],[1,"87","20","Community Waste Management Education and Awareness Pilot Programme","Using small scale pilot projects and programmes promote education and awareness of communities in waste management with special reference to 3Rs.",""],[1,"87","21","Community Engagement in Waste Management","Engage communities in the waste management by using them for key activities.",""],[1,"102","4","Community-Based Waste Segregation Support","The engagement of community through awareness, training and obtaining the support of community based organizations and non-governmental organizations for waste segregation at the point of origin is going to be one of the major strategies for effective solid waste management.",""],[1,"102","5","Private-Sector Resource Recovery from Segregated Waste","Use of technology to provide resource recovery from segregated waste can be done through the private sector.",""],[1,"102","5","SME Recycling Industry Incentives and Green Credit Support","Providing incentives and green credit to SMEs will encourage them to start many recycling industries or even expand existing recycling industries for plastic, paper, rubber, textile glass and metals.",""],[1,"102","5","Small-Scale Compost and Biogas Plant Development","SMEs can start up compost and bio gas plant at small scale which can support the replacement of chemical fertilizer by organic fertilizer.",""],[1,"102","5","Sanitary Landfill and Waste-to-Energy Development","The long term solutions such as sanitary landfills, waste to energy projects which need high investment and long lead times can be introduced later if necessary for other types of wastes.",""],[1,"141","7","Renewable Energy and Waste-to-Energy Project Development","Most of renewable energy systems such as Solar PV both small scale roof top and MW scale grid connected power plants, wind, and to a certain extent biomass are being actively pursued by the private sector in particular, and CEB in the case of wind.",""],[1,"141","7","Waste-to-Energy Project Development","There are also a few waste to energy projects being pursued.",""],[1,"151","4","Integrated Solid Waste Management Plan","Develop integrated plans to combat solid waste management issues, with reuse, recycling, waste to energy and incineration.",""],[1,"151","5","Plastic Recycling and Reuse Fund","Establish a fund for plastic recycle/reuse using \"polluter-pay strategy\".",""],[1,"151","6","Single-Use Plastic Reduction Regulations and Policies","Limit use and find alternatives for plastic material (packaging and wrappers).",""],[1,"151","6","Plastic-Free Government Office Initiative","Make office environments free from single use plastic material by developing new regulations.",""],[1,"151","6","Government Plastic Use Discouragement Policy","Introduce policies to discourage government institutions from using plastic for printing, decorating, etc.",""],[1,"272","6","Effective Implementation of Solid Waste Management Policies and Strategies","related policies and national strategies need to be implemented effectively and without delay.",""],[1,"272","6","Strengthening of the Central Environment Authority","The capacity of the Central Environment Authority needs to be increased in order to address, monitor, and regulate increasing sources of electronic and industrial waste.",""],[1,"284","7","Environment-Friendly Waste Disposal Methods","Introduce environment friendly waste disposal methods.",""],[1,"284","10","De-growth, Bio-economy, and Circular Economy Implementation","Research and implement ideas about de-growth, bio-economy and circular economy, in all resource consuming enterprises to eliminate waste and encourage recovery of resources.",""],[1,"285","5","Community-Based Solid Waste Segregation Engagement Strategy","The engagement of the community through awareness, training and obtaining the support of Community Based Organizations (CBOs) and Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs) for waste segregation at the point of origin, is going to be one of the major strategies for effective solid waste management.",""],[1,"285","6","Private-Sector Resource Recovery from Segregated Waste","Use of technology to provide resource recovery from segregated waste can be done through the private sector.",""],[1,"285","6","SME Recycling Incentives and Green Credit Support","Providing incentives and green credit to SMEs will encourage them to start many recycling industries or even expand existing recycling industries for plastic, paper, rubber, textile, glass and metals.",""],[1,"285","6","Small-Scale Compost and Biogas Plant Development","SMEs can start up compost and bio gas plants at a small scale, which can support the replacement of chemical fertilizer with organic fertilizer.",""],[1,"292","1","Waste-to-Energy Project Development","There are also a few waste to energy projects being pursued.",""]],"58":[[1,"30","4","Sustainable Land Use Enforcement Measures","Stringent measures should be taken to implement sustainable land use practices and prevent unsound ad hoc development programmes.",""],[1,"30","4","Weather Forecasting and Early Warning System Development","Research and development for weather forecasting, developing early warning systems and enhancing social capacity to cope with disasters, is a fundamental need.",""],[1,"30","5","Climate Change Adaptation Priority for Vulnerable Groups","Adaptation to climate change impacts must have priority, especially to protect the poor and vulnerable.",""],[1,"201","2","Climate and Weather Forecasting Capacity Enhancement","As such, prediction capabilities have to improve in order to have a reasonable and reliable forecast in the short term (up to 3 days) and medium term (3 to 10 days) to reduce the impacts of heavy rainfall, floods, landslides etc.",""],[1,"201","2","Subseasonal and Long-Range Climate Forecasting for Planning","Reliable sub seasonal to seasonal predictions (10 to 30 days) and long range forecasts (beyond 30 days) are needed to plan for agriculture, hydropower generation, and water supply.",""],[1,"201","2","Weather Observation and Radar Infrastructure Upgrade","Facilities such as RADAR, Doppler RADAR, high resolution cloud pictures, and monitoring of aerosols along with other weather data collected inland and off shore will be helpful for short term predictions.",""],[1,"201","2","Climate Forecasting Model Development","Good prediction models, especially prepared for islands like Sri Lanka, will be necessary for climate forecasts.",""],[1,"201","2","Climate Science Capacity Development","Most of all, developing a pool of scientists and researchers in areas such as meteorology, oceanography, geology and atmospheric physics is necessary to succeed in this task.",""],[1,"207","4","Sub-seasonal Weather Prediction and Early Warning System Enhancement","Improvement of sub seasonal weather prediction is essential to take important decisions for disaster preparedness.",""]],"59":[[1,"16","4","Participatory Forest Conservation and Land Restoration Measures","Implement participatory approaches to control deforestation and increase forest cover, and reduce soil erosion, land degradation and enhance soil fertility.",""],[1,"85","3","Natural Habitat Protection Policies for Wildlife","Bring in policies to ensure that the natural habitats of animals such as monkeys and elephants are not be disrupted.",""],[1,"85","4","Forest Estate Demarcation and Watershed Conservation","Demarcate forest estates and conserve critical watersheds.",""],[1,"85","5","Forestry Master Plan Implementation","Implement the proposals in the Forestry Master Plan which also promotes the multiple use forests with the participation of communities and private sector.",""],[1,"85","6","National Reforestation and Tree Cover Expansion Initiative","Reforest the country and increase the tree cover wherever appropriate including urban areas and rural areas.",""],[1,"85","9","Watershed Degradation and Soil Conservation Projects and Programmes","Effective projects and programmes to combat watershed degradation and promote soil conservation to be planned with an understanding of both social and institutional causes of land degradation.",""],[1,"284","6","Participatory Forest Conservation and Land Restoration Measures","Implement participatory approaches to control deforestation and increase forest cover, and reduce soil erosion, land degradation and enhance soil fertility.",""],[1,"294","2","Ecosystem and Habitat Restoration and Species Conservation","Restore severely degraded ecosystems and key habitats, and conserve important species.",""],[1,"299","7","Kandyan Home Garden Improvement Initiative","The improvement of the Kandyan home garden concept will help to prevent soil erosion.",""]],"60":[[1,"28","6","Micro Bund Construction for Soil and Water Conservation","Construct \"Micro Bunds\" on mountain slops along the contour to control surface erosion and improve water infiltration and absorption into sub soil strata.",""],[1,"84","9","Institutional Capacity Building for Land Resource Management","Increase the capabilities of institutions involved in land resource management to enable them to perform their roles effectively.",""],[1,"84","10","Institutional Mandate Rationalization and Redefinition","A rationalization and re-definition of mandates and responsibilities of institutions should be undertaken to avoid or minimize conflicts of interests.",""],[1,"84","11","Sub-national Environmental Management Support and Funding Oversight Mechanism","Provide assistance to Provincial Councils and Pradeshiya Sabhas to undertake environmental management and develop a mechanism to overcome improper use of funding by various funding sources.",""],[1,"84","11","Establishment of Sub-national Environmental Institutions","The need to establish appropriate sub-national level institutions to enable Provincial Councils to discharge environment related responsibilities placed on them should be explored.",""],[1,"84","12","Multi-Stakeholder Land Degradation Combat Initiative","Promote the greater participation of Pradeshiya Sabhas, NGOs and universities in combating land degradation.",""],[1,"84","13","Private Sector Land Degradation Response Framework","Develop the necessary policy, institutional and regulatory framework to accommodate the private sector in combating land degradation.",""],[1,"84","14","Land Use Planning Process Improvement","Enhance the land use planning process by improving the current system through usage of built capacity for deforestation and degradation of forests.",""],[1,"85","1","Implementation of Land Degradation and Forest Offence Laws","Implement existing laws and regulations pertaining to land degradation and forest offences.",""],[1,"85","2","Land Degradation Legislation Review and Reform","Review existing legislation pertaining to land degradation to rectify deficiencies and the laws to be made more effective and easier to coordinate.",""],[1,"86","3","Water Body Reservation Enforcement","Strictly maintain reservations in water bodies in line with the National Environmental Act, Mahaweli Authority Act and Irrigation Ordinance.",""]],"61":[[1,"14","2","Fiscal Consolidation and Tax Collection Improvement","Internal stabilization could be achieved by improving fiscal consolidation and tax collection efforts, and the adoption of prudent monetary and exchange rate policies.",""],[1,"14","2","Prudent Monetary and Exchange Rate Policy","Internal stabilization could be achieved by improving fiscal consolidation and tax collection efforts, and the adoption of prudent monetary and exchange rate policies.",""],[1,"14","2","Trade and Development Finance Engagement Strategy","A strategic approach to bilateral, regional and multilateral engagements with trading partners is also important in ensuring export growth momentum, access to FDI, and other forms of development finance to navigate turbulent global economic developments.",""],[1,"14","3","Economic Reform Programme to Improve Business Climate and Reduce Public Debt","If the government shows a strong commitment to address current challenges by implementing economic reforms to improve its Doing Business global rankings to a position below 70 from the current 110, while lowering its public debt from the current 79.3% of GDP to 70% within the same period",""],[1,"14","4","Fiscal Consolidation and Tax Collection Strengthening","Strengthen fiscal consolidation and improve tax collection efforts and adopt prudent monetary and exchange rate policies to achieve internal stability",""],[1,"14","5","Debt Management Measures","Urgent measures are also needed to manage high levels of debt.",""],[1,"42","3","Trade and Financial Integration Strengthening","Sri Lanka integrates its economy closely with the global economy through strengthened trade and financial relations to maximize the chances of realizing the set targets.",""],[1,"42","3","Fiscal, Trade, Investment, and Labour Market Reform Package","Also essential are reforms in fiscal, trade, investment and labour market policies - as discussed in previous sections - to remove existing impediments to achieving higher rates of economic growth.",""],[1,"43","1","Evidence-Based Public Policy Reform Package","Those issues that have been clearly identified in this document can be addressed effectively only through evidence based public policies relating to taxation, human resource development, in particular R and D, social security, social cohesion, etc.",""],[1,"65","2","Fiscal Consolidation and Prudent Macroeconomic Policy Reform","Internal stabilization could be achieved by fiscal consolidation efforts and adoption of prudent monetary and exchange rate policies to minimize price instability, high interest rates and rapid depreciation of the exchange rate.",""],[1,"66","2","Fiscal Deficit Reduction through Revenue Mobilization and Expenditure Rationalization","Lower fiscal deficits to more sustainable levels through strong revenue generation efforts and rationalization of expenditures.",""],[1,"66","4","Fiscal Consolidation to Reduce Borrowing Dependence","Progressively reduce fiscal dependence on borrowing to bridge deficit financing needs for debt sustainability.",""],[1,"66","5","Fiscal and Monetary Policy Coordination","Maintain proper coordination between fiscal and monetary policies to achieve price and exchange rate stability and a low interest rate environment",""],[1,"66","6","Conducive Macroeconomic Environment for Private Investment","Create a conducive macroeconomic environment to attract private investment, both local and foreign.",""],[1,"67","3","Domestic Resource Mobilization and Fiscal Consolidation","Improve domestic resource mobilization efforts, particularly government revenue generation through fiscal consolidation efforts to generate a primary surplus",""],[1,"67","4","Capital Market Development for Domestic Debt Financing","Shift the debt portfolio towards less risky domestic debt by developing Sri Lanka's capital market",""],[1,"67","5","Debt Management Strengthening and Public Investment Appraisal Reform","Enhance debt management practices through stronger institutional set ups and effective economic cost-benefit analysis of public investment projects",""],[1,"67","10","Debt-to-Equity Conversion Mechanism","Convert debt to equity where appropriate using transparent mechanisms such as listing in the Colombo Stock Exchange, or through negotiations with strategic partners, preferably via open and competitive processes.",""],[1,"67","11","Inflation Targeting Monetary Policy Framework","Initiatives by the monetary authorities to move towards an inflation targeting framework that will take cognizance of maintaining price stability within a targeted medium term growth trajectory for the country is expected to provide a consistent and predictable monetary policy framework in the future.",""],[1,"68","7","Monetary Authority Independence Measure","Monetary authorities must have a measure of independence to set appropriate policy responses to retain price stability",""],[1,"69","4","Prudent Monetary Policy Framework","Adoption of a prudent monetary policy framework, supported by better fiscal and monetary policy coordination",""],[1,"70","6","Flexible Exchange Rate Policy Framework","Maintain a stable and competitive exchange rate within a flexible exchange rate policy framework",""],[1,"70","7","Foreign Exchange Market Volatility Smoothing","Foreign exchange market intervention by monetary authorities in pursuit of exchange rate policy setting should be limited to smoothing out undue volatility in currency",""],[1,"71","5","Tax Revenue Mobilization and Tax Administration Modernization","Take measures to generate adequate government revenues (like computerizing tax collection - RAMIS, and expanding the taxpayer base), while keeping issues of progressivity in taxation as a key principle.",""],[1,"101","1","Fiscal Consolidation and Liability Management Strategy","through fiscal consolidation efforts involving a forward-looking liability management strategy, it is hoped to bring the debt-to-GDP ratio down from the current 79% to 70% by 2020.",""],[1,"101","2","Trade and Financial Integration Strengthening","It is also imperative that Sri Lanka integrates its economy closely with the global economy through strengthened trade and financial relations to maximize the chances of realizing the set targets.",""],[1,"101","2","Fiscal, Trade, Investment and Labour Market Reforms","Also essential are reforms in fiscal, trade, investment and labour market policies - as discussed in previous sections - to remove existing impediments to achieving higher rates of economic growth that will eventually take the country to upper middle-income status.",""],[1,"281","1","Fiscal Consolidation and Tax Collection Strengthening","Strengthen fiscal consolidation and improve tax collection efforts and adopt prudent monetary and exchange rate policies to achieve internal stability",""],[1,"281","2","Debt Management Measures","Urgent measures are also needed to manage high levels of debt.",""],[1,"283","11","Fiscal Consolidation and Liability Management Strategy","Additionally, through fiscal consolidation efforts involving a forward-looking liability management strategy, it is hoped to bring the debt-to- GDP ratio down from the current 79 percent to 70 percent by 2020.",""]],"62":[[1,"14","2","Anti-Corruption Legislation Enforcement","The enactment and proper enforcement of necessary legislation is key in minimizing corruption.",""],[1,"15","2","Doing Business Indicator Improvement Reform","Improve Doing Business indicators - specifically with regard to enforcing contracts, paying taxes, registering property, and getting credit - to improve economic efficiency",""],[1,"15","3","Transparency and Accountability Legislation and Enforcement","Enact and enforce necessary legislation to promote transparency and accountability and thereby minimize corruption",""],[1,"18","2","Rule of Law and Governance Enforcement Measures","Strengthen the rule of law, ensure personal safety and reinforce the regulatory functions of governance at all levels, in order to stem the tendencies towards lawlessness, abuse of power and corruption.",""],[1,"25","12","Standing Committee for Policy Compliance","Creating a Standing Committee to ensure compliance with these policies from 2018.",""],[1,"25","14","Legislative Alignment Amendment Package","Amending legislation to align to revised policies and present to Parliament by end of 2018.",""],[1,"224","5","Anti-Corruption and Rule of Law Enforcement Programme","Responding to and eliminating the serious and debilitating impact of corruption in all areas of governance and in society, by consistent and effective interventions and programmes, focusing especially on effective law enforcement.",""],[1,"228","14","Public Sector Ethics and Integrity Culture","Public sector employees must operate independently with integrity and maintain high standards of ethical conduct to maintain sound decision making processes and ensure community confidence and trust in the public sector.",""],[1,"229","1","Transparent Government-Bureaucracy Relations Reform","Ensuring clear and transparent relationships between the elected government and the bureaucracy is critical to prevent any undue influence in the administration of public functions and to ensure swift and efficient implementation of government policies and strategies.",""],[1,"229","2","Good Governance Strategy and Cross-Level Public Administration Structure","A structure needs to be put in place that cuts across all levels (e.g. central, provincial and local) of public bodies/agencies, re-defines their scope and re-assigns specific roles, responsibilities and accountabilities, and empowers them with delegated authority independent of political intervention or influence.",""],[1,"229","3","Public Service Integrity and Accountability Culture Programme","Create a culture in which people will be naturally motivated to do the 'right thing, the right way' with utmost loyalty and commitment.",""],[1,"229","13","Competitive Public Sector Pay Reform","Competitive pay for the public sector - includes a performance based variable pay component.",""],[1,"229","15","Public Sector Good Governance Framework","A framework for good governance by the public sector will help overcome the above fundamental problems and ensure effective implementation.",""],[1,"261","3","Anti-Corruption Measures Strengthening","Continued strengthening of anti-corruption measures adopted since 2015.",""],[1,"281","9","Transparency and Accountability Legislation and Enforcement","Enact and enforce necessary legislation to promote transparency and accountability and thereby minimize corruption",""],[1,"282","8","Revenue Administration and Expenditure Rationalization Reforms","Reforms relating to coverage, compliance and tax administration to increase Government revenue, and rationalizing Government expenditure through reduction of waste and elimination of corruption",""]],"63":[[1,"117","2","Teacher Professionalism and Recruitment Reform","Improve teacher professionalism, standards and training as the quality of teaching is a key factor in improving children's learning and the outcomes they achieve.",""],[1,"117","3","Teacher Training Modernization and Curriculum Upgrade","Modernize training of new teachers with curriculum upgrades to make them enquiring professionals who are able to use technology and data to enhance learning and teaching.",""],[1,"117","4","Modern Teaching-Learning Methods Promotion","Promote use of modern teaching-learning methods which enhance students' practical engagements in learning (e.g. innovative, research-based, assignment-based methods).",""],[1,"117","5","Bilingual Education Policy and Teacher Training Support","Introduce a general policy of bilingual education and related policies to ensure that bilingual teachers have the required training both in-service and pre-service.",""],[1,"117","5","Teaching Resources Support for English and Bilingual Education","Provide better teaching resources to support teachers of English language and bilingual education.",""],[1,"117","6","Professional Council for Teachers","Establish a professional council for teachers to maintain quality and standards of teacher development.",""],[1,"117","7","Teacher Education Institutional Strengthening and CPD Network Expansion","Improve the existing institutional framework of teacher education by upgrading NCoEs up to degree awarding level, establishing links between NCoEs, NIE and local universities to produce graduate teachers, strengthening the network of Teacher Learning Centers to provide Continuing Professional Development (CPD) for teachers in each education zone.",""],[1,"117","8","Teacher Licensing and Performance System","Introduce a teacher license system and performance system to improve teacher effectiveness.",""],[1,"117","9","Teacher Transfer System Between National and Provincial Schools","Implement a teacher transfer system between national and provincial schools as an interim approach until such time a school-based teacher recruitment policy is in place.",""],[1,"117","10","Teacher Incentive System for Service in Difficult Areas","Establish a teacher incentive system for encouraging service in difficult areas.",""],[1,"118","3","SEN Curriculum Upgrade in National Colleges of Education","Upgrade the SEN curriculum in the National Colleges of Education (NCoEs) to improve pre- service training in SEN provision.",""],[1,"118","4","Gifted and Talented Children Training in NCoE SEN Curriculum","Include training on identifying and meeting the needs of gifted and talented children in the NCoE SEN curriculum",""]],"64":[[1,"273","4","Expanded Higher Education and Vocational Training Access","Higher education and vocational training opportunities must be provided for students that do not achieve the necessary marks to enter into Government sponsored higher education.",""],[1,"273","4","Special Loan and Scholarship Schemes for Higher Education","Special loan and scholarship schemes should be introduced to the less privileged to receive higher education.",""]],"65":[[1,"120","3","Academic Staff R&D Exposure and Training Programme","Supply qualified academic staff with exposure to R&D through foreign higher degrees and training.",""],[1,"120","4","Research and Development Culture Promotion Initiative","Promote R&D practices and establish an R&D culture in the system through formation of research cells and university-based consulting in each of the universities and development of strong links with industry.",""],[1,"120","6","University Staff Participation in R&D Programmes","Encourage all university staff members without exception to participate in R&D programmes.",""],[1,"120","7","University Research-Supportive Administrative Culture","Promote a university administrative culture supportive of research",""],[1,"120","8","University Research and Innovation Promotion","Promote research and innovation outcomes in all university faculties.",""]],"66":[[1,"73","8","Modernization and Enforcement of Wage and Labour Standards Regulations","Domestic wage and labour standard regulations must be modernized and sensibly enforced to ensure that workers are safeguarded even as the country attempts to raise inflows of FDI",""],[1,"78","2","Termination of Employment of Workmen Act Reform","Reform the Termination of Employment of Workmen Act (TEWA) of 1971, in which the current compensation formula for 'non-disciplinary' termination of employment is the third highest in the world (Employers' Federation of Ceylon, 2009).",""],[1,"98","3","Workplace Technology and Modern Equipment Upgrade","Introduce technology and modern work instruments and implements to reduce or eliminate adverse effects of such work on health, safety and well- being of workers.",""]],"67":[[1,"40","4","National Cyber Security Strategy","Introduce a national cyber security strategy with inter-agency cooperation and cyber operation command centres to build Sri Lanka's cyber defence infrastructure.",""],[1,"258","5","National Cyber Security Strategy","We need to strengthen our cyber defence infrastructure through the introduction of a national cyber security strategy with inter-agency cooperation and cyber operation command centres.",""],[1,"258","5","Inter-Agency Cyber Task Force","An inclusive inter-agency cyber task force comprising relevant government, private sector and civil society institutions should implement this cyber security strategy.",""],[1,"307","10","National Cyber Security Strategy","Introduce a national cyber security strategy with inter-agency cooperation and cyber operation command centres to build Sri Lanka's cyber defense infrastructure.",""],[1,"308","1","Cyber Security Strategy Implementation Task Force","cyber task force with relevant Government and private sector institutions should implement this cyber security strategy.",""]],"68":[[1,"92","4","Peripheral Social Infrastructure Development","Develop social infrastructure in peripheral areas to curb rural urban migration.",""]],"69":[[1,"42","4","Sustainable Development Agenda Implementation","In 2030 with the implementation of sustainable development agenda through SDGs and other national green policies Sri Lanka seeks to enjoy a pollution free, clean and green environment with high quality of life for its people and inclusive green growth.",""],[1,"42","4","2020 Vision Awareness and Mobilization Campaign","The 2020 Vision is to mobilize all groups, including the public sector, private sector and especially school children through awareness, training and motivation, and to initiate all actions as a step towards the 2030 vision.",""],[1,"49","4","Alignment of National, Sub-national, and Sectoral Plans with the BIGG Path","our key recommendations provide guidance on how other national, sub-national and sectoral plans may be brought into alignment within the BIGG path.",""],[1,"49","4","Revision of Detailed Plans and Policies for Vision 2030","Such detailed plans and policies will need to be updated and revised to help us achieve the 2030 vision, by transforming our values, mindsets, institutions, behaviours, processes, methods, tools, technologies, projects, and policies.",""],[1,"49","4","Inclusive Consultations on Government and Societal Transformation","The transformation processes required within the government bureaucracy, civil society, business and industry, also need to be worked out through inclusive consultations.",""],[1,"56","1","Systematic Sustainable Development Planning Integration","more systematic and detailed integration processes will be needed, when the key recommendations in this report are elaborated within other specific national, sub-national and sectoral plans that will be developed under the broad framework of the balanced inclusive green growth (BIGG) pathway.",""],[1,"56","1","Vertical Integration of Sustainable Development Planning","particular attention will need to be paid to vertical integration of sustainable development planning, linking the central (national), provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"63","2","SDG Coordination, Direction, and Monitoring Mechanism","Unless there is a very strong mechanism to coordinate, direct and monitor all activities related the SDGs, achieving SDGs by 2030 could be difficult, mainly due to the crosscutting issues between the goals.",""],[1,"90","3","National SDG Secretariat","The proposed secretariat for SDGs under Ministry of Sustainable Development and Wild life and the vision 2030, Sri Lanka Next, will form the nucleus for effective implementation of 17 SDGs and its 162 targets by 2030 making Sri Lanka one of the sustainably developed high middle income country.","Ministry of Sustainable Development and Wild life"],[1,"101","6","National Sustainable Development Strategy","the country is moving towards a National Sustainable Development Strategy.",""],[1,"101","6","Blue Green Development Strategy","the country through the Ministry of Mahaweli Development and Environment recently promoted the Blue Green Development Strategy for sustainable development.","Ministry of Mahaweli Development and Environment"],[1,"102","2","Inter-departmental and Inter-institutional Coordination Mechanism","Therefore the country has to develop a clear mechanism to improve the inter-departmental and inter-institutional coordination.",""],[1,"285","2","National Sustainable Development Strategy","the country is moving towards a National Sustainable Development Strategy.",""],[1,"285","2","Blue Green Development Strategy","the country through the Ministry of Mahaweli Development and Environment recently promoted the Blue Green Development Strategy for sustainable development.","Ministry of Mahaweli Development and Environment"],[1,"285","2","National and Subnational Policy Implementation Institutions","There are many departments and institutions established for sound implementation of the policies and regulations at the national, provincial and local level.",""],[1,"285","3","Inter-departmental and Inter-institutional Coordination Mechanism","Therefore, the country has to develop a clear mechanism to improve inter-departmental and inter-institutional coordination.",""],[1,"285","3","Stakeholder Mobilization for Green Policy Collaboration","Further, it is required to mobilize the stakeholders for greater collaborations and cooperation in the development and implementation of the green policies and plans.",""],[1,"285","4","National Programme Mobilization and Incentive Framework","The country needs to mobilize all the public sector institutions to achieve these targets and obtain the commitment from the private sector and civil society to actively engage in the national programmes, through financial and non-financial incentives.",""],[1,"286","7","National Awareness, Training, and Motivation Mobilization Campaign","The 2020 Vision is to mobilize all groups including the public sector, private sector and especially school children, through awareness, training and motivation, and to initiate all actions as a step towards the 2030 vision.",""]],"70":[[1,"18","1","Subsidiarity and Local Governance Empowerment","Strengthen the subsidiarity principle by empowering lower tiers of government, especially local bodies and take effective measures to facilitate citizen participation in governance and development.",""],[1,"27","1","National Physical Plan Update","the National Physical Planning Department, as per the mandate given by the Town & Country Planning (Amended) Act of 2000, is in the process of updating the National Physical Plan in order to facilitate the development objectives of the Government.",""],[1,"27","4","Settlement Development Siting Guidance","Direct the settlement developments into the areas with the highest livability",""],[1,"27","6","Conservation and Regulated Development Framework for Sensitive Landscapes","The strategic proposals in the Plan includes the conservation and the regulated development in the fragile central hills of the island, coastal zone and the other sensitive landscapes, along with the containment of future urban development with higher population concentration in four 'Urban Corridors': extending between Colombo and Trincomalee, Galle and Tissamaharama, Batticaloa and Ampara and Jaffna and Kilinochchi, two 'Metro Regions' in Kandy and Anuradhapura, and nine 'Major Cities'.",""],[1,"27","6","Infrastructure Planning Framework for Investment Optimization","The future infrastructure developments are expected to adhere to this framework in order to have the best returns on investments and to optimize the returns on current investments.",""],[1,"27","6","Stakeholder Consultation in Infrastructure Planning","In order to minimize the potential for community tensions arising from such infrastructure plans, consultation with stakeholder communities will be an integral part of the planning process.",""],[1,"27","7","State-Level Enforcement of the National Physical Planning Policy","Head of the State Level intervention to enforce the National Physical Planning Policy",""],[1,"27","8","Public Awareness Campaign on the National Physical Plan","Wider and frequent awareness building among general public of the National Physical Plan and the state of its implementation.",""],[1,"27","9","Strengthening Local Authority Planning and Implementation Divisions","Strengthening Planning and Implementation divisions of the Local Authorities with relevant expertise, technology and the institutional setting.",""],[1,"27","10","Project Compliance Checks for Local Development Plan Funding","Strict conformity checks of the compliance of projects to the Local Development Plan in the allocation of funds from national, provincial and local budgets.",""],[1,"27","11","Annual and Periodic Implementation Programme for the National Physical Plan","Setting up annual and periodic implementation programme within the National Physical Plan.",""],[1,"27","12","Stakeholder Community Consultation in Infrastructure Planning","Consultation with stakeholder communities will be an integral part of the planning process, in order to minimize the potential for community tensions arising from such infrastructure plans.",""],[1,"44","4","National Physical Plan Adoption as Policy Guidance","The National Physical Plan should be adopted as a Broad National Level Policy Guidance for the identification, selection and the implementation of Inter-regional, regional and local level development projects and programmes.",""],[1,"173","3","National Physical Plan Update","The national physical plan giving effect to this policy is being updated by the National Physical Planning Department in consultation with national and regional level authorities, government and non-government development agencies and other interest groups.",""],[1,"175","6","Stakeholder Consultation for Major Projects","Meaningful consultations with stakeholder communities prior to launching new major projects is one way to increase awareness and compliance and to increase a sense of public responsibility and shared citizenship.",""],[1,"176","4","Update the National Physical Plan","the existing national physical plan ... needs to be urgently updated to meet current and emerging situations.",""],[1,"176","5","National Physical Planning and Urban Containment Framework","The existing national physical plan should be regarded for its many progressive elements, such as the identification of 'central fragile area', 'coastal zone' and 'wildlife corridors' as crucial to be conserved for future generations; the proposal to contain future urban developments into five Metropolitans along with a hierarchy of urban centres; and addressing the need for greater accessibility to all locations across the island.",""],[1,"176","7","Update of the National Physical Planning Policy","The way out from the given situation is to update the existing National Physical Planning Policy with a range of background studies, a series of in-depth analysis and a wider range of consultative participation of expertise, development agencies and interest groups.",""],[1,"177","5","Opportunity and Resource Exploration Development Initiative","Developments that promote the exploration of new opportunities and untapped resources in land, ocean, location and in inhabitants.",""],[1,"178","5","Brownfield-First Urban Development and Settlement Densification","In this regard, the existing settlement locations have possibilities for intensification of development along with the augmentation of space, facilities and amenities.",""],[1,"178","5","Urban Sprawl Containment Policy","Future urban development should be contained into a manageable limited area and discouraged from sprawling into vast land extents.",""],[1,"179","6","Conservation Zoning and Regulatory Control Framework","The physical developments within these zones are proposed to be guided with stringent regulations and guidelines with the support of the existing legislative framework.",""],[1,"179","6","Depopulation and Settlement Redistribution Strategy","The conservation will be supported by a depopulation strategy.",""],[1,"185","5","National Physical Planning Policy Enforcement","Head of the State level intervention to enforce the National Physical Planning Policy",""],[1,"185","6","Public Awareness Promotion on the National Physical Plan","Promotion of wider and frequent awareness among general public of the national physical plan and the state of its implementation.",""],[1,"185","7","Strengthening Local Authority Planning and Implementation Divisions","Strengthening Planning and Implementation divisions of the local authorities with relevant expertise, technology and the institutional setting.",""],[1,"185","8","Project Compliance Checks for Local Development Plan Funding","Strict conformity checks of the compliance of projects to the local development plan in the allocation of funds from national, provincial and local budgets.",""],[1,"185","9","Annual and Periodic Implementation Programme for the National Physical Plan","Setting up annual and periodic implementation programme within the national physical plan.",""],[1,"185","10","Updated National Physical Plan Implementation","the updated national physical plan is proposed to be implemented under the directives of the National",""],[1,"186","1","National Physical Plan Policy Guidance","The national physical plan should be adopted as broad national level policy guidance for the identification, selection and the implementation of inter-regional, regional and local level development projects and programmes.",""],[1,"186","1","Review of Pipeline Development Projects","The government may also reconsider some of the projects which are presently in the pipeline, for their immediate requirement, and the unfavourable impact that they can have upon a planned, sustained and broad physical development in the island.",""],[1,"295","5","Enforcement of the National Physical Planning Policy","Enforce the National Physical Planning Policy through the intervention of the Head of the State.",""],[1,"295","6","National Physical Plan Public Awareness Campaign","Carry out wider and more frequent awareness building among the general public regarding the National Physical Plan and the state of its implementation.",""],[1,"295","7","Strengthening Local Authority Planning and Implementation Divisions","Strengthen the Planning and Implementation divisions of the local authorities with relevant expertise, technology and institutional settings.",""],[1,"295","8","Project Compliance Checks for Local Development Plan Funding","Perform strict conformity checks on the compliance of projects to the Local Development Plan in the allocation of funds from national, provincial and local budgets.",""],[1,"295","9","Annual and Periodic Implementation Programme for the National Physical Plan","Set up an annual and periodic implementation programme within the National Physical Plan.",""],[1,"295","11","Updated National Physical Plan Implementation","the updated National Physical Plan is proposed to be implemented under the directives of the National Physical Planning Council, headed by H.E. the President and represented by the relevant line ministries and institutions.",""],[1,"296","1","Project and Programme Prioritization Guidance","Guidance for the identification, selection and implementation of inter-regional, regional and local level development projects and programmes.",""],[1,"297","1","Immediate Survey and Budget Allocation for Work and Data Quantification","A survey should be started immediately to quantify the work and data, and a necessary budget should be allocated.",""]],"71":[[1,"31","4","Public Communication Strategy for Common Values and Citizenship","Instill a sense of common values, ethics and a sense of citizenship in a unitary SL through an effective public communication strategy.",""],[1,"31","5","Global Citizenship Education Programme","Programmes such as Global citizenship education (GCE) can inspire action, build partnerships, dialogue and cooperation through formal and informal education.",""],[1,"31","6","Community-Based Learning Environment Promotion","Promote community based approaches that create learning environments that promote links to communities and link learners to real-life experiences (such as exchange programmes, community-based activities, and foreign language studies).",""],[1,"32","2","Inter-Religious and Inter-Ethnic Appreciation Incentive Measures","Ensure celebration of diversity through State intervention to incentivize inter-religious and inter-ethnic appreciation.",""],[1,"32","3","State-Led Equal Rights and Human Rights Education","Ensure recognition of equal rights through State intervention to affirm through all means (including its basic norms like the Constitution), that human rights are a common set of values across all cultures and identities.",""],[1,"32","3","Participatory Civics and Human Rights Teaching","Civics teaching should have as a cornerstone the understanding of the Bill of Rights in the Constitution, the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, treaties we have ratified and signed on as a State, and customary norms of International law that bind all nations.",""],[1,"32","3","Participatory Civic Action for Peaceful Change","This should not be merely theoretical but participatory -- students must be able to identify in their daily reality what situations go against the realization of human rights, and should be able to volunteer and engage to obtain peaceful, cooperative, and smart change.",""],[1,"38","2","Countrywide Citizen Engagement Campaign in Public Affairs","Launch and regularly refresh a countrywide campaign of citizen engagement in public affairs with priority to poorer communities and lagging areas mainstreaming community self- managed development approach.",""],[1,"45","1","Public Communication and Civic Values Strategy","An effective public communication strategy will instill common values, ethics and a sense of citizenship in a unitary Sri Lanka.",""],[1,"45","1","Social and Historical Education for Youth","Social and historical education will create an independent and responsible mentality among young people and promote understanding of the traditions of other communities.",""],[1,"45","1","Equal Rights Recognition Initiative","Recognition of equal rights.",""],[1,"45","6","Countrywide Civic Education and Community Institution Capacity-Building Campaign","Countrywide civic education campaign mainly focused on the communities undertaking community managed development will have coverage completed through specifically identified training institutions involving local government.",""],[1,"254","2","Countrywide Civic Education Campaign","A countrywide civic education campaign mainly focused on the communities undertaking community managed development will have coverage completed through specifically identified training institutions involving the local government by 2020, demonstrating scalability to cover the rest of the country by 2025 and 2030 progressively.",""],[1,"299","4","Education and Awareness Creation Initiative","Prioritize education and awareness creation among all citizens, especially at the school level.",""],[1,"300","2","Public Communication Strategy for Common Values and Citizenship","Instill common values, ethics and a sense of citizenship in a unitary SL through an effective public communication strategy.",""],[1,"300","3","Global Citizenship Education Programme","Programmes such as Global Citizenship Education (GCE) can inspire action and build partnerships, dialogue and cooperation, through formal and informal education.",""],[1,"300","4","Community-Based Learning Environment Promotion","Promote community based approaches which create learning environments that promote links to communities, as well as linking learners to real-life experiences (such as exchange programmes, community-based activities and foreign language studies).",""],[1,"300","5","Inter-Religious and Inter-Ethnic Appreciation Incentives","Encourage the celebration of diversity through state interventions to incentivize inter-religious and inter-ethnic appreciation.",""],[1,"300","5","Social and Historical Education for Shared Values","Social and historical education should strive to instill a critical, independent and responsible mentality among young people and promote understanding of the traditions of other communities (by learning each other's language, getting to know each other's festivities, exchanging cultural, musical, literary, culinary knowledge, etc.).",""],[1,"300","5","Inclusive Religious Education Reform","Religious education - which most young people receive - should be incentivized to reflect positive traits of other communities and faiths.",""],[1,"300","6","Equal Rights and Human Rights Civic Education","Ensure recognition of equal rights through state intervention to affirm through all means, including its basic norms like the Constitution, that human rights are a common set of values across all cultures and identities.",""],[1,"301","2","Values-Based Citizenship and Ethics Promotion","A common sense of morality, citizenship values and ethics should be instilled in people by using religion as a vehicle.",""],[1,"309","4","Education for National Identity and Intercultural Respect","In this regard, dignity and respect for all ethnicities, cultures and religions must be taught on an educational level in Sri Lanka.",""]],"72":[[1,"33","5","Women’s Upper Secondary, STEM, and Leadership Skills Development Policy","Develop policies to enable women access upper secondary and higher education including in STEM subjects, and train women in technical, innovation and leadership skills to bring them into the formal economy at better rates of pay.",""],[1,"38","4","Gender-Specific Skills Training and Employment Programme for Poor Women","Develop and implement gender specific programmes targeting poor women in particular for skills training leading to employment.",""],[1,"41","8","Equal Participation and Compensation Measures for Young Women","Ensure that specific measures are adopted to promote the equal participation and compensation of young women in the both the private and public sector economy.",""],[1,"45","2","Technical and Leadership Skills Training for Younger Women","Programs to train younger women in technical and leadership skills will enable them to enter the formal economy at better rates of pay.",""],[1,"75","6","Youth and Women Decent Employment Promotion","Create more decent employment opportunities for youth in all regions, especially for rural youth and women in general, especially to low income segments.",""],[1,"78","1","Female Labour Force Participation Promotion Measures","Adopt strategies to encourage more female labour force participation, such as the generation of part-time and flexible job opportunities, creation of jobs in rural areas, and changing cultural norms regarding the division of household work.",""],[1,"220","1","Unpaid Care and Domestic Work Formalization Policy","Recognize and value unpaid care and domestic work by adopting policies to formalize, diversify and develop household care across state, private and public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"220","1","Shared Responsibility Curriculum Mainstreaming","programmes on shared responsibility between men and women within the household should be mainstreamed into the educational curriculum.",""],[1,"220","2","Informal Economy Labour Regulation Enforcement","Enforce better regulation of the informal economy in relation to rates of pay, contracts and work hours to avoid profit maximization and exploitation of female and ageing female labour.",""],[1,"220","3","Women’s Technical, Innovation, and Leadership Skills Training Policy","Policies need to be developed to train women in technical, innovation and leadership skills to bring them into the formal economy at better rates of pay.",""],[1,"220","4","Elderly Pension and Social Protection Scheme Improvement","Improve pension and social protection schemes for the elderly to diminish their reliance on informal protection mechanisms such as loans/ financial support from children and family members, and/or participation in an ageing, exhausted workforce in low paid jobs.",""],[1,"220","5","Informal Economy Regulation for Fair Labour Conditions","Provide for better regulation of informal economy in relation to rates of pay, contracts and work hours to avoid profit maximization and exploitation of female / ageing female labour.",""],[1,"220","6","Attitudinal Change Programmes on Women's Gender Roles","Conduct programmes towards attitudinal changes to women and their gendered roles in society.",""],[1,"222","10","National Studies on Women's Economic Participation and Vulnerability","Conduct national studies on women's participation in the informal economy, the prevalence of SGBV, and the impact on women of climate change and environmental degradation.",""],[1,"223","2","Integrated Women's Economic Empowerment and Care Support Plan","An integrated plan that strengthens retirement benefits, re-skills 60+ year old women for better jobs, formally recognizes unpaid care and domestic work, brings in public-private partnerships for household care, and mainstreams joint responsibilities of men and women in parenting and household care into educational curricular and workplace norms will alleviate the disproportionate burden on women in the informal and unpaid care economy.",""],[1,"223","2","Women's Technical and Leadership Skills Training Programme","Programs to train younger women in technical and leadership skills that will enable them to enter the formal economy at better rates of pay, policies to monitor and abolish gender wage gaps, ensure the accessibility, safety and security of women in relation to public transport and workplaces, and strengthen the prevention of domestic violence will also encourage women into the labour force, facilitate their wellbeing and increase their productivity.",""],[1,"301","4","Unpaid Care and Domestic Work Formalization Policy","Recognize and value unpaid care and domestic work by adopting policies to formalize, diversify and develop household care across state, private and public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"301","4","Shared Responsibility Curriculum Mainstreaming","programmes on shared responsibility between men and women within the household should be mainstreamed into the educational curriculum.",""],[1,"301","6","Women’s Upper Secondary, Higher Education, and Skills Development Policy","Develop policies to enable women to access upper secondary and higher education, particularly in STEM subjects, and train women in technical, innovation and leadership skills to bring them into the formal economy at better rates of pay.",""],[1,"301","7","Retirement Benefits and Post-Retirement Labour Protection Policy","Develop policies that provide adequate retirement benefits for the elderly and protection against post-retirement labour exploitation in the informal sector.",""],[1,"302","3","Integrated Women's Economic Empowerment and Care Support Plan","An integrated plan that strengthens retirement benefits, re-skills 60+ year old women for better jobs, formally recognizes unpaid care and domestic work, brings in public-private partnerships for household care, and mainstreams joint responsibilities of men and women in parenting and household care into educational curricular and workplace norms, will alleviate the disproportionate burden on women in the informal and unpaid care economy.",""],[1,"302","3","Women's Technical and Leadership Skills Training Programme","Programmes to train younger women in technical and leadership skills will enable them to enter the formal economy at better rates of pay.",""]],"73":[[1,"41","3","Quality Education for Youth Curriculum and System Reform","Provide quality education to youth that leads to learning and skills that is relevant to their lives, and gives them the capacity required for the country's changing labour market.",""],[1,"41","6","Private Sector Innovation and Youth Technology Promotion","Encourage the private sector to actively play a role in promoting innovation and in identifying and promoting new technology for youth participation in labour force.",""],[1,"72","11","Productive Job Opportunity Training Support","Provide training and other opportunities to facilitate productive job opportunities in expanding sectors",""],[1,"308","2","Youth Employment Expansion through Mega Projects and SME Investment","The high unemployment rate of youth should be mitigated due to the increase in public and private mega projects, such as the Megapolis project and Cinnamon Life project, combined with community based initiatives and investment in Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs).",""],[1,"310","3","Quality Education for Youth and Curriculum Reform","Provide quality education to youth that leads to learning and skills that are relevant to their lives, and give them the capacity required for the country's changing labour market.",""],[1,"310","6","Private Sector Innovation and Youth Labour Force Participation Promotion","Encourage the private sector to actively play a role in encouraging innovation and in identifying and promoting new technology for youth participation in the labour force.",""],[1,"310","7","Youth Engagement for Sustainable Development Plan Implementation","Use the potential of youth to catalyse the implementation of the sustainable development plans of the Government.",""]],"74":[[1,"43","3","Education System Quality and Advanced Learning Upgrade","the education system should be providing not only a basic standard of quality education for everyone (including adult education), but also high-end educational opportunities for the most gifted students using the latest technology, curricula and teaching methods available in advanced countries.",""],[1,"76","15","Increased Investment in Education and Health Services","Increased investments in education and health services focusing on improving the quality and effectiveness in building up the human capital of the poor in the long term.",""]],"75":[[1,"79","1","Project Preparation and Evaluation Strengthening","The preparation and evaluation of such projects are critical on two fronts: first, that they pass economic feasibility assessments given the heavy financial costs involved and repayment of loans, especially foreign currency denominated loans on non-concessional terms; second, that environment impact assessments are carried out to safeguard the country's natural resources and ensure sustainable development outcomes.",""],[1,"79","1","Improved Project Selection and Implementation System","Learning from past experiences and improving the criteria for selection of projects, systematic evaluation and efficient implementation of them are critically important.",""],[1,"79","1","Cross-Agency Project Coordination Improvement","Coordinated action across multiple agencies and ministries remains weak in project planning and implementation.",""],[1,"80","1","National Project Identification Criterion","Establish a national project identification criterion on a decision making hierarchy that takes the National Physical Planning Policy (NPPP), Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and National Economic Policy (NEP) as the primary guidelines.",""],[1,"80","2","Strategic Screening of Major Public Sector Projects","All major public sector projects should be identified on the guidelines that originate from strategic needs of the NPPP, SDGs and the NEP.",""],[1,"80","4","Private Sector Project Promotion for Strategic National Priorities","Private sector projects that address strategic needs of NPPP, SDGs and NEP should also be encouraged after aligning them with the broad national criterion.",""],[1,"80","5","Strategic Environmental and Social Assessment Programme","Carry out strategic environmental and social assessments (SESA) for selected spatial areas and broad economic sectors that help to identify strategic projects.",""],[1,"80","6","Post-Implementation Project Monitoring","Strengthen post-implementation monitoring of projects according to project approving documents",""],[1,"80","7","Strengthening Institutional Mechanisms for Project Delivery","Institutional mechanisms must be strengthened in project planning and implementation, financial oversight and procurement.",""]],"76":[[1,"147","12","Alternative Medicine Facilities for Medical Tourism","This would encompass alternative medicine (ayurveda, homeopathy, yunani, siddha, etc.) facilities which would, along with International accreditation, enhance prospects for medical tourism.",""]],"77":[[1,"103","5","National Awareness, Training, and Motivation Mobilization Campaign","The 2020 Vision is to mobilize all groups, including the public sector, private sector and especially school children through awareness, training and motivation, and to initiate all actions as a step towards the 2030 vision.",""],[1,"103","7","National Multi-sectoral Social Action Plan","If a national, multi-sectoral action plan is developed and implemented, progress can be measured and monitored based on a set of indicators dealing with the social issues discussed in the report.",""],[1,"103","7","Multi-agency Social Monitoring and Follow-up Platform","Monitoring and measurement of progress can be greatly facilitated by a multi-agency platform that brings together all relevant agencies in order to share information and take follow up action.",""],[1,"275","3","Government Policy and Program Coordination for SDG Alignment","government policy and programs must be coordinated and aligned to ensure effective delivery and implementation, without redundancy and duplication of between ministries and authorities.",""],[1,"287","10","National Multi-sectoral Social Action Plan","If a national, multi-sectoral action plan is developed and implemented, progress can be measured and monitored based on a set of indicators dealing with the social issues discussed in the report.",""],[1,"287","10","Multi-agency Social Monitoring Platform","Monitoring and measurement of progress can be greatly facilitated by a multi-agency platform that brings together all relevant agencies in order to share information and take follow up action.",""]],"78":[[1,"112","6","Thirteen Years of Mandatory Education Reform","Under the new education reforms proposed in 2015, the government has taken a policy decision to implement 13 years of mandatory education.",""],[1,"113","5","Universal Free Education and Student Welfare Support","Sri Lanka provides free-education from the primary stage to the first degree level in university education.",""],[1,"116","7","Education Equity Gap Identification and Service Delivery Equity Action","Identify equity gaps within Sri Lanka's education system and address all service delivery inequities.",""],[1,"117","1","Special Support for Children from Poor Households","Identify and provide special support for children from poor households",""],[1,"117","1","Student Transport Subsidy Scheme","transport subsidies",""],[1,"117","1","School Health and Nutrition Programme Strengthening","a strengthened health and nutrition programme already implemented in schools",""],[1,"117","15","Special Education Legislation for Students with SEN","Formulate legislation specific to the education of students with SEN in order to provide a framework for policies, promote inclusion, empower students and parents, make the whole system of provision for SEN more accountable and contribute to better student learning outcomes.",""],[1,"117","16","National Special Education Needs Policy Document","Prepare a policy document that sets out the national policy on SEN including future strategies for SEN provision and practice.",""],[1,"117","17","Inclusive Education Improvement and Support Staffing","Improve the inclusive education concepts, teaching and learning processes and learning environments.",""],[1,"118","1","Special Education Resourcing Mechanism","Introduce new mechanism for resourcing special education institutions based on vertical equity principles and adequacy criteria.",""],[1,"118","2","Social Charter for Students with Special Educational Needs","Develop a social charter for students with SEN for ensuring their educational rights, provision of educational opportunities for them with national standards and ensure the social commitments for their education and well-being.",""],[1,"118","10","Gifted and Talented Students Policy and Programme Development","Develop a policy statement about gifted and talented students describing how they may be identified and their needs met.",""],[1,"118","10","New Programmes for Gifted and Talented Students","Introduce new programmes for gifted and talented students.",""],[1,"120","17","Systematic Education Resourcing Mechanism","Develop a systematic mechanism for resourcing education.",""],[1,"120","18","Increase Public Investment in Education","Increase significantly the proportion of public investment in education.",""]],"79":[[1,"25","1","Marine Research Institute Establishment and Coordination Hub","Establish a state of the art marine research institute with improved infrastructure and human resources to conduct marine research and to develop as a \"center of excellence in marine research\" which would serve as umbrella organization coordinating and facilitating marine research and sustainable utilization of ocean resources.",""],[1,"25","2","Environmentally Friendly Fishing Gear Promotion and Incentives","Promote environmental friendly fishing gear and provide incentives for environment friendly fishing gear operations.",""],[1,"25","3","Marine Protected Area Network Expansion and Management","Increase Marine Protected Area network and provide for effective management of these areas.",""],[1,"25","3","Marine Resource Management Institutional Coordination Reform","Improve the fragmentation of state institutions dealing with marine resource management.",""],[1,"25","6","Marine Sector Investment for Blue Economy Expansion","Invest more on marine sector in order to get the maximum return from blue economy, going beyond fisheries and expanding to develop ocean based resources for pharmaceuticals, minerals, responsible tourism, shipping, and renewable energy.",""],[1,"25","7","Ocean-Based Resource Diversification Initiative","Expand focus on ocean based resources beyond fisheries, to include pharmaceuticals, minerals, responsible tourism, shipping, and renewable energy.",""],[1,"293","8","Marine Research Institute Establishment","Establish a state of the art marine research institute with improved infrastructure and human resources, to conduct marine research and to develop as a \"center of excellence in marine research\".",""],[1,"293","9","Environmentally Friendly Fishing Gear Promotion and Incentives","Promote environmentally friendly fishing gear and provide incentives for environmentally friendly fishing gear operations.",""],[1,"293","10","Marine Protected Area Network Expansion and Management","Increase the Marine Protected Area network and provide for the effective management of these areas.",""],[1,"293","10","Marine Resource Management Institutional Coordination Reform","Improve the fragmentation of state institutions dealing with marine resource management.",""],[1,"294","2","Ecosystem and Habitat Restoration and Species Conservation","Restore severely degraded ecosystems and key habitats, and conserve important species.",""],[1,"294","3","Marine Sector Investment for Blue Economy Development","Invest more on the marine sector in order to get the maximum return from the blue economy, since the future resource base will be the ocean.",""],[1,"294","4","Ocean-Based Resource Diversification Initiative","Expand ocean based resources beyond fisheries to pharmaceuticals, minerals, responsible tourism, shipping, and renewable energy.",""],[1,"294","5","Marine Research and Technology Transfer for Ocean Health","Increased scientific knowledge, development of research, and transfer of marine technology, are essential in order to improve ocean health and to enhance the contribution of the ocean for the development of countries, small island developing states in particular.",""],[1,"294","6","Baseline Studies and Resource Surveys for Non-Living Marine Resources","It is imperative to carry out baseline studies, resource surveys and exploration of non-living resources.",""]],"80":[[1,"25","4","Fishery Harbour Infrastructure Development","Develop fishery harbour infrastructure.",""],[1,"25","4","Promotion of Underutilized Fishery Harbour Facilities","Promote underutilized facilities such as Dikkowita Fishery Harbour for economic development.",""],[1,"157","8","Advocacy for Greater Fishing Access in International Waters","Gain more opportunities to fish in international waters by requesting UN to reserve a larger proportion of the share to poor countries and small island nations.",""],[1,"157","14","Fishery Harbour Infrastructure Development","Develop fishery harbour infrastructure.",""],[1,"157","15","Underutilized Fisheries Facility Economic Development Initiative","Promote underutilized facilities such as Dikkowita Fishery Harbour for economic development.",""],[1,"157","16","Agricultural Harvest Freight Facility Support","Encourage local and foreign investors to obtain facilities and bring the harvest to the facility for quick freight by air or surface.",""],[1,"159","1","Green Harbour Development for Ports","If Sri Lanka is to benefit from the blue economy along with development of existing and new ports, development has to be based on the green harbour concept.",""],[1,"159","2","Baseline Studies and Resource Surveys for Non-Living Marine Resources","It is imperative to carry out baseline studies, resource surveys, and exploration of non-living resources.",""]],"81":[[1,"19","5","Seasonal Rainfall Forecasting and Early Warning System","Enhance the capacity and the ability to better forecast seasonal rainfall and provide early warnings on extreme weather events leveraging on modern technology and develop institutional arrangements to speedily respond to such early warnings.",""]],"82":[[1,"36","6","Improved and More Efficient Consular Services","Provide better and more efficient Consular Services for the protection and the advancement of the welfare of Sri Lankans abroad as well as to minimize document forgeries often committed in the past by human traffickers and people smugglers.",""],[1,"305","1","Improved and More Efficient Consular Services","Provide better and more efficient Consular Services for the protection and the advancement of the welfare of Sri Lankans abroad, as well as to minimize document forgeries often committed in the past by human traffickers and people smugglers.",""]],"83":[[1,"15","1","Strategic State-Owned Enterprise Restructuring","Continue with ongoing efforts to review and restructure strategic SOEs, by strengthening professional management and accountability, and minimising political interference - the focus should be on efficient performance of the SOE, rather than on ownership (i.e., public or private).",""],[1,"17","1","Governance Policy Development","Policies also need to be developed on governance related issues mentioned above.",""],[1,"66","3","Systematic Monitoring and Evaluation for Public Enterprises and Development Projects","Introduce systematic monitoring and evaluation mechanisms for all the public enterprises and development projects and curtail subsidies to public enterprises.",""],[1,"71","7","State-Owned Enterprise Restructuring Programme","Restructure loss making state owned enterprises to improve their financial performance and thereby lower pressures on central government finances.",""],[1,"78","7","SOE Restructuring and Privatization Programme","Continue with ongoing efforts to restructure and/or privatize heavy loss-making SOEs, and appoint managers and directors of SOEs based on merit rather than political patronage",""],[1,"78","10","E-Governance Enhancement in Public Enterprises","Enhance E-governance in public enterprises through resource mobilization and capacity building to increase the efficiency in service delivery and gain cost-efficient solutions for existing operational inefficiencies",""],[1,"78","12","Public Enterprise Recruitment Framework and Capacity Building Mechanism","Develop a comprehensive and meaningful framework for recruitments to public enterprises and improve the human resource productivity through an effective capacity building mechanism",""],[1,"281","7","Strategic State-Owned Enterprise Restructuring and Governance Reform","Continue with ongoing efforts to review and restructure strategic SOEs, by strengthening professional management and accountability, and minimising political interference - the focus should be on efficient performance of the SOE, rather than on ownership (i.e., public or private).",""],[1,"281","8","Doing Business Indicator Improvement Reform","Improve Doing Business indicators - specifically with regard to enforcing contracts, paying taxes, registering property, and getting credit - to improve economic efficiency",""],[1,"282","13","Business Regulatory and Administrative Simplification Reform","Improving the business regulatory and operational environment by restructuring regulatory institutions, moving towards a low tax and tariff business environment with simplified and transparent administrative procedures, identifying and removing delays",""],[1,"283","12","Fiscal, Trade, Investment, and Labour Market Reforms","Also essential are reforms in fiscal, trade, investment and labour market policies (as discussed in previous sections) - to",""],[1,"290","2","Guided Economic Transformation","A guided transformation is required.",""]],"84":[[1,"258","7","Dengue Health Security Preparedness Initiative","Health would be a component of upgrading national preparedness to meet emerging health security threats, starting with a focus on dengue.",""],[1,"258","7","Local Medical Research and Development Funding","Initiatives should be taken to fund local research and development of medication to fight diseases.",""],[1,"258","7","University and Medical Research Organization Support for Patents and Research","Encouraging universities and other medical research organizations and assisting them in areas such a securing patents and promoting research would be beneficial.",""]],"85":[[1,"14","2","Sustainable Agriculture Productivity Enhancement","Given that a majority of Sri Lanka's poor are in the rural sector, which primarily relies on agriculture, promoting sustainable agriculture through productivity improvements - such as new technology and farming techniques, improved extension services and setting up of agro based industries - should be a priority.",""],[1,"14","2","Agricultural Extension Services Improvement","Given that a majority of Sri Lanka's poor are in the rural sector, which primarily relies on agriculture, promoting sustainable agriculture through productivity improvements - such as new technology and farming techniques, improved extension services and setting up of agro based industries - should be a priority.",""],[1,"14","2","Agro-Based Industry Development","Given that a majority of Sri Lanka's poor are in the rural sector, which primarily relies on agriculture, promoting sustainable agriculture through productivity improvements - such as new technology and farming techniques, improved extension services and setting up of agro based industries - should be a priority.",""],[1,"14","6","Sustainable Agriculture Productivity Improvement Programme","Promote sustainable agriculture through productivity improvements to address persistent poverty in the rural sector",""],[1,"75","2","Agricultural Productivity Enhancement and Agro-based Rural Industry Support","Sufficient attention needs to be given to help farmers increase agricultural productivity by introducing new technology and farming techniques, providing necessary advice through improved extension services and assist rural communities to setup agro based industries, which could create new employment opportunities for rural youth",""],[1,"75","3","Agricultural Market Access Infrastructure and Marketing Facilities Improvement","Improve infrastructure and marketing facilities, so that the farmers could easily find markets for their produce",""],[1,"76","12","Reorientation of Agricultural Support Toward Extension, Finance, Irrigation, and R&D","Divert the investments from price and marketing interventions and input subsidies, towards provision of agricultural extension, agricultural finances, irrigation infrastructures, and R&D , and let the private sector play a bigger role rather than having the government try to manage the sector",""],[1,"100","12","National Food Production Programme","Investments in the National Food Production Programme",""],[1,"100","12","Agricultural Mega Zones Development","establishment of agricultural mega zones",""],[1,"100","12","Agricultural Value Chain Strengthening","strengthening of value chains development",""],[1,"100","12","Agricultural Marketing Authority Establishment","establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority",""],[1,"100","12","Agriculture Modernization Authority Establishment","establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority",""],[1,"100","12","Farmer-Centric Agro-Organization and Cooperative Formation","the formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives",""],[1,"100","12","Private Sector Participation and PPP Promotion for Agricultural Modernization","Promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"100","14","Crop Production Investment and Improved Varieties Promotion","Investments in crop production and improvement to promote new hybrid and high yielding varieties of crops",""],[1,"100","15","Seed Cultivation Farm Investment","Investments in seed and planting material to establish seed cultivation farms",""]],"86":[[1,"294","1","Fishery Harbour Infrastructure Development","Develop fishery harbour infrastructure.",""],[1,"294","1","Promotion of Underutilized Fishery Harbour Facilities","Promote underutilized facilities such as the Dikkowita Fishery Harbour to enhance economic development.",""],[1,"294","5","Marine Aquaculture and Ornamental Fish Trade Development","Since we are approaching the maximum limit from our coastal fish production, marine aquaculture (mariculture) as well as the marine ornamental fish trade targeting the export market will be substantially developed with the latest technology.",""],[1,"294","5","Seafood Export Value Addition Programme","Furthermore, the seafood export industry will be developed with value additions.",""],[1,"294","5","Green Harbour Development Programme","existing and new ports should be developed based on the green harbour concept.",""],[1,"294","6","Ocean-Based Ecotourism Promotion","Ocean based ecotourism including marine mammal observations, snorkeling, diving, sport fishing and other water sports, will be further promoted after setting up all the regulatory mechanisms.",""]],"87":[[1,"157","2","Establish Fisheries Reserves and Marine Protected Areas","Establish fisheries reserves and other forms of Marine Protected Areas (MPAs) with a sound scientific understanding.",""],[1,"158","4","Accession to the Memorandum of Understanding on Migratory Shark Conservation","Become a signatory to the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the Conservation of Migratory Sharks.",""]],"88":[[1,"157","1","Diversification of Fishermen into Non-Extractive Tourism Services","Divert fishermen more on to non-extractive (less impact on the resource) but more income generating areas such as charter boats for fishing tours for tourists.",""],[1,"158","5","Community-Based and Co-Management Pilot Projects","Promote, community-based and co-management practices.",""],[1,"158","6","Co-managed Fisheries Site Expansion","Increase the number of co-managed fisheries sites.",""],[1,"158","7","Alternative Livelihoods Support for Low-Income Fishermen","Develop alternative livelihoods for least income earning fishermen such as artisanal and lagoon fishermen.",""]],"89":[[1,"14","2","Export Competitiveness and Supply-Side Reform","Achieving external stability requires a progressive improvement in generating higher export earnings through reforms that address supply-side rigidities and enhance Sri Lanka's export competitiveness.",""],[1,"14","5","Export Competitiveness Supply-Side Reforms","Increase export earnings and FDI flows to achieve external stability - through supply-side reforms that improve export competitiveness, and a strategic approach to trade agreements.",""]],"90":[[1,"185","2","Pedestrian-Friendly Urban Planning and Regulation","As a priority measure, pedestrian friendliness should be considered as the main objective of future urban plans, instead of the present dominance given to vehicular movement.",""],[1,"185","3","Urban Public Open Space Provision","Yet, innovative approaches such as the opening of canal reservations, river banks, marshy areas and beach fronts along with reasonable facilities and maintenance of them will enable overcoming the difficulties in providing public open spaces.",""],[1,"185","3","Neighbourhood Play and Gathering Space Provision","Parallel to that, providing wider road spaces at neighbourhood levels to be used as makeshift children's play areas and gathering spaces will work as an alternative way of providing public open spaces and will also serve to strengthen 'neighbourhood' or 'lane' communities.",""]],"91":[[1,"19","4","Crop Diversification and Agricultural Mechanization Transition","A shift away from high water dependent agriculture to low water dependent / drought tolerant crops and varieties along with mechanization are required to address this threat.",""],[1,"19","4","Farmer Company Formation and Value Chain Linkage Initiative","At the same time the scale constraint of small farmers must be overcome via the formation of people's / farmer companies linked to longer value chains.",""],[1,"19","6","Drought-Tolerant Crop Variety and Cropping Pattern Development","Develop drought tolerant crop varieties and cropping patterns which consume less water, labour and agro chemicals, and incentivize their adoption.",""],[1,"19","7","Farmer Water Conservation and Agricultural Technology Training","Educate farmers on the need to conserve water and the use of new technology for farming, value addition and marketing.",""],[1,"19","8","Farmer Scale-Constraint Support for Water-Saving Crops","Enable farmers to overcome the scale constraint so that less water using crops can be produced, stored, value added and marketed profitably.",""],[1,"20","2","Consumer Nutrition Education Campaign","Educate consumers at large on better nutrition and appropriate changes in food habits.",""],[1,"272","3","Climate Change Adaptation Strategies for Agriculture","Remedial measures need to incorporate climate change adaptation strategies, incentives for retaining youth in the agricultural sector, national food security strategies, ecosystem based land use management strategies, and water resources management.",""],[1,"272","3","Youth Retention Incentives in Agriculture","Remedial measures need to incorporate climate change adaptation strategies, incentives for retaining youth in the agricultural sector, national food security strategies, ecosystem based land use management strategies, and water resources management.",""],[1,"272","3","National Food Security Strategy","Remedial measures need to incorporate climate change adaptation strategies, incentives for retaining youth in the agricultural sector, national food security strategies, ecosystem based land use management strategies, and water resources management.",""],[1,"272","3","Ecosystem-Based Land Use Management Strategy","Remedial measures need to incorporate climate change adaptation strategies, incentives for retaining youth in the agricultural sector, national food security strategies, ecosystem based land use management strategies, and water resources management.",""],[1,"272","3","Water Resources Management Measures","Remedial measures need to incorporate climate change adaptation strategies, incentives for retaining youth in the agricultural sector, national food security strategies, ecosystem based land use management strategies, and water resources management.",""],[1,"274","5","National Agricultural Research and Development Program","Improved national research and development programs should be carried out to identify seeds and clones for agricultural products that can generate higher yields, nutrition, and improved resistance to disease.",""],[1,"281","3","Sustainable Agriculture Productivity Improvement Initiative","Promote sustainable agriculture through productivity improvements to address persistent poverty in the rural sector",""],[1,"283","6","National Food Production Programme","Investments in the National Food Production Programme, establishment of agricultural mega zones, strengthening of value chain development, establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority, establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority, formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives, and promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"283","6","Agricultural Mega Zones Development","Investments in the National Food Production Programme, establishment of agricultural mega zones, strengthening of value chain development, establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority, establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority, formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives, and promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"283","6","Agricultural Value Chain Development Strengthening","Investments in the National Food Production Programme, establishment of agricultural mega zones, strengthening of value chain development, establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority, establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority, formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives, and promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"283","6","Agricultural Marketing Authority Establishment","Investments in the National Food Production Programme, establishment of agricultural mega zones, strengthening of value chain development, establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority, establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority, formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives, and promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"283","6","Agriculture Modernization Authority Establishment","Investments in the National Food Production Programme, establishment of agricultural mega zones, strengthening of value chain development, establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority, establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority, formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives, and promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"283","6","Farmer-Centric Agro Organizations and Cooperatives Formation","Investments in the National Food Production Programme, establishment of agricultural mega zones, strengthening of value chain development, establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority, establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority, formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives, and promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"283","6","Private Sector Participation and PPP Promotion for Agricultural Modernization","Investments in the National Food Production Programme, establishment of agricultural mega zones, strengthening of value chain development, establishment of an Agricultural Marketing Authority, establishment of the Agriculture Modernization Authority, formation of farmer centric large scale agro organizations and cooperatives, and promotion of private sector participation and PPPs to modernize the sector",""],[1,"283","8","Crop Production Investment and Improved Varieties Promotion","Investments in crop production and improvement to promote new hybrid and high yielding varieties of crops",""],[1,"283","9","Seed Cultivation Farm Establishment Investment","Investments in seed and planting material to establish seed cultivation farms",""],[1,"289","2","Drought-Tolerant Crop Variety and Cropping Pattern Development","Develop drought tolerant crop varieties and cropping patterns which consume less water, labour and agro chemicals, and incentivize their adoption.",""],[1,"289","3","Farmer Water Conservation and Agricultural Technology Education","Educate farmers on the need to conserve water and on the use of new technology for farming, value addition and marketing, with the aim of obtaining medium to long-term results.",""],[1,"289","4","Farmer Scale Constraint Support and Value Chain Services","Enable farmers to overcome the scale constraint so that less water using crops can be produced, stored, value added and marketed profitably.",""],[1,"299","8","Short-Term Crop Variety and Drip Irrigation Support","By cultivating short term crop varieties and using drip irrigation, farmers will be able to manage their finances as well as their nutrient intake.",""]],"92":[[1,"295","3","Stakeholder Consultation Requirement for Major Projects","Such projects will proceed only after consultations with all stakeholder communities likely to be impacted.",""],[1,"295","10","Stakeholder Community Consultation in Infrastructure Planning","Minimize the potential for community tensions to arise from such infrastructure plans by making consultations with stakeholder communities an integral part of the planning process.",""]],"93":[[1,"227","4","Decentralized Planning and Local Governance Empowerment","Decentralization of planning and plan implementation, adoption of the subsidiarity principle in devolution of power, people's participation in governance at national, provincial and local levels and the empowerment of local councils are measures that can change the present highly centralized decision making structure.",""],[1,"227","5","Strengthened Strategy Execution and Implementation Focus","It is therefore very critical to have equal emphasis being placed on execution/implementation to achieve the 2030 Vision.",""],[1,"229","15","Decentralized Planning and Local Governance Empowerment","Decentralization of planning and plan implementation, adoption of the subsidiarity principle in devolution of power, people's participation in governance at national, provincial and local levels and the empowerment of local councils will change the present highly centralized decision making structure.",""]],"94":[[1,"133","6","Petroleum Resource Development Area Tendering","In the petroleum sector, the PRDS is in the process of tendering the resource development areas for",""]],"95":[[1,"22","3","Gas Exploration in Mannar Basin and Other Promising Areas","High priority should be given to continue the gas explorations in the Mannar basin and other promising areas.",""],[1,"22","8","Offshore Gas Development in the Mannar Basin","Offshore gas development in the Mannar basin and elsewhere should have a high priority -- to increase independence from imported energy, reduce foreign exchange costs, and strengthen the creditworthiness of the national economy.",""]],"96":[[1,"85","7","Low Impact Urban Stormwater Management","Use low impact development in storm water management in urban areas.",""]],"97":[[1,"16","6","Water Pollution Reduction Enforcement and Pricing Policy","Preserve ecosystem services and improve ecosystem health, and minimize adverse impacts on human health (like CKDU and dengue), by reducing water pollution from all sectors, especially industry, agriculture, and waste disposal, through better enforcement of laws, regulation and pricing policy.",""],[1,"28","7","National Water Pollution Control Mechanism","Commence a national level mechanism with the support of Central Environmental Authority to control water pollution.",""],[1,"284","8","Water Pollution Reduction Enforcement and Pricing Policy","Preserve ecosystem services and improve ecosystem health, and minimize adverse impacts on human health (like CKDU and dengue), by reducing water pollution from all sectors, especially industry, agriculture, and waste disposal, through better enforcement of laws, regulation and pricing policy.",""],[1,"286","3","Wastewater Discharge Fee System","Introducing the wastewater discharge fee system - which has been delayed for the last fifteen years - will ensure that all business enterprises reduce the consumption of water and lead to a reduction of the discharged pollution load.",""],[1,"286","3","School-Level Water Conservation Awareness Campaign","Awareness creation at the school level on the preciousness of clean water and the need for the protection of it, will make all future generations act more responsibly.",""],[1,"286","3","Water Body Buffer Zone Protection","All water bodies need to be protected by having buffer zones, as prescribed by the relevant legislation.",""],[1,"296","5","National Water Pollution Control Mechanism","Commence a national level mechanism with the support of the Central Environmental Authority to control water pollution.","Central Environmental Authority"],[1,"297","6","Water Quality Improvement for Rivers and Water Bodies","The quality of water in rivers and water bodies will be maintained at World Health Organization (WHO) standards for drinking water sources and will be made suitable for agriculture.",""],[1,"300","1","Enforcement of Rules Against Unauthorized Riverbank and Waterway Development","Implementing existing rules and regulations without deviations, will reduce unauthorized developments and unauthorized structures in river banks, reservations, and near and around waterways and canals, and will prevent flooding and landslides to an extent, by 2020.",""],[1,"300","1","Control of Sand, Soil, Gravel, and Metal Extraction","Controlling and managing natural resource extraction such as sand, soil, gravel and metal will prevent many environmental problems including health hazards.",""]],"98":[[1,"16","2","Disaster Vulnerability Reduction and Climate Adaptation Measures","Implement urgent short, medium and long-term measures to reduce vulnerability to disasters (eg. droughts, floods, landslides) and adapt to climate change.",""],[1,"201","3","National Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Actions","Adaptation actions will be taken in agriculture, health, and water supply sectors.",""],[1,"207","5","Disaster Risk Management Capacity Enhancement","· Enhance social capacity to effectively cope with disasters, and manage disaster risks.",""],[1,"207","6","Community Disaster Prevention Committees and Plans","Establish community disaster prevention committees and develop community disaster prevention plans to enhance the disaster management capacity of communities.",""],[1,"284","4","Disaster Vulnerability Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation Measures","Implement urgent short, medium and long-term measures to reduce vulnerability to disasters (eg. droughts, floods, landslides) and adapt to climate change.",""],[1,"289","1","Seasonal Rainfall Forecasting and Early Warning System","Enhance the capacity and the ability to better forecast seasonal rainfall and provide early warnings on extreme weather events using modern technology, and develop institutional arrangements to speedily respond to such early warnings.",""],[1,"299","1","Climate Change Adaptation Prioritization","Prioritize adaptation to climate change impacts, especially to protect the poor and vulnerable.",""],[1,"299","3","Sustainable Land Use and Early Warning Systems","Recognize the urgent need for strong policy decisions, sustainable land use practices and the development of early warning systems.",""],[1,"299","7","Hillside Housing Development Restriction","The prevention of housing development on hilly slopes will help to reduce landslide type disasters.",""],[1,"299","8","Forest Cover Expansion and Soil Water Retention Measures","Increased forest cover will enhance water retention in the soil and improve infiltration.",""],[1,"299","8","Ancient Irrigation and Water Management Integration","Introducing some of the ancient wisdom of irrigation and water management - such as the cluster of cascading tanks of various sizes - into planning processes, will make it possible to live even with drought conditions.",""],[1,"300","1","Scientific Planning and Tree Cover Expansion for Disaster Risk Reduction","Proper scientific planning and increasing tree cover will reduce disasters such as flooding and landslides.",""]],"99":[[1,"16","9","Organic and Biodynamic Agriculture Promotion","Implement organic and biodynamic agricultural practices to reduce the use of chemical fertilizer and agrochemicals, to prevent long term health impacts and enhance soil properties.",""],[1,"272","7","Organic Fertilizer Promotion and Organic Agriculture Development","The implementation of the organic fertilizer promotion policy needs to be matched with more broad based application and development of organic agriculture techniques to prevent soil and water pollution as well as to rehabilitate degraded agricultural land.",""],[1,"284","11","Organic and Biodynamic Agriculture Promotion","Implement organic and biodynamic agricultural practices to reduce the use of chemical fertilizer and agrochemicals, to prevent long term health impacts and enhance soil properties.",""],[1,"286","2","Natural Fertilizer and Biodynamic Farming Promotion","Encouraging the replacement of agro chemicals and chemical fertilizers through the use of natural fertilizers and bio dynamic farming practices will permanently eradicate future catastrophes such as CKDu.",""]],"100":[[1,"17","1","Evidence-Based Policy Development for Human Resource and Social Protection Sectors","The development of evidence based policies in the area of education, skill development, research and innovation, employment, social security, protection of vulnerable groups, income distribution, food security etc. is an urgent step that needs to be taken.",""],[1,"267","1","Strategic Future Forecasting R&D Initiative","Sri Lanka should invest in R&D initiatives to forecast the strategic future of the country.",""],[1,"279","3","Strengthening National Statistical Capacity","The implementation of the 2030 Vision will also require substantive improvements in national statistical capacity, especially to strengthen disaggregated data gathering and analysis.",""]],"101":[[1,"99","5","Migrant Worker Skills Enhancement and Market Diversification","enhancing skills of migrant workers and exploring new markets",""]],"102":[[1,"104","1","Progressive Taxation and Social Investment Package","effective measures are taken to redistribute income through a progressive taxation regime, with corresponding increases in social investment in critically important sectors such as education, research and development, health and public transport.",""]],"103":[[1,"110","6","Consumer Nutrition Education Campaign","Educate consumers at large on better nutrition and appropriate changes in food habits.",""],[1,"289","5","Consumer Nutrition Education Campaign","Educate consumers at large, on better nutrition and appropriate changes in food habits.",""]],"104":[[1,"150","7","Coastal Pollution Monitoring and Blue Flag Beach Certification","Measure and monitor key pollutants along the coast.",""],[1,"150","11","Raw Sewage Discharge Prevention Measures","Urgently implement measures to stop raw sewage dumping in the sea and only after treatment.",""],[1,"151","3","International Cooperation for Debris Management Technology","Enhance cooperation with developed nations with better debris management technology such as Korea to address the issue.",""],[1,"151","7","Marine Debris Baseline Survey","Conduct baseline surveys to find out debris sources.",""],[1,"151","8","IAS Research, Monitoring, and Early Warning Measures","Increase understanding of IAS through primary research and constant long-term monitoring (eg. creating a blacklist).",""],[1,"151","9","Biofouling Control and Management Guidelines","Adopt guidelines for control and management of ships' biofouling to minimize the transfer of invasive aquatic species (Biofouling Guidelines) (IMO resolution MEPC 207(62).",""],[1,"151","10","Ratification of Maritime Environmental Conventions","Sign IMO ballast water convention and convention on Control of Harmful Anti-fouling Systems on Ships.",""],[1,"151","11","National Ship Hull Cleaning Regulations","Develop national regulations for ship hull cleaning based on IMO guidelines.",""],[1,"151","12","Port Waste Reception Infrastructure Development","Develop port infrastructure for waste reception based on international standards.",""],[1,"151","12","Fishery Harbour Waste Disposal Facilities","Fishery harbours should have facilities for dumping unusable nets and other fishing gear.",""],[1,"151","13","Waste Disposal Awareness for Fisher Communities and Sailors","Create awareness for fisher communities and sailors on proper disposal of waste.",""],[1,"155","16","Review and Adopt International Maritime Regulations","Review international regulations, conventions, treaties and guidelines and adopt them at national level, e.g. IMO Ballast Water Convention, IMO ship hull fouling guidelines.",""],[1,"155","17","Convention Review and Strengthening","Review and strengthen already signed conventions.",""]],"105":[[1,"148","5","Oceanic Sustainability Indicators Framework","The creation of a comprehensive underlying set of oceanic sustainability indicators would help assess the current status of marine systems, diagnose on-going trends, and provide information for forward-looking and sustainable ocean governance.",""],[1,"150","12","Coastal Ecosystem Carbon Sequestration Protection","Improve carbon sequestration by protecting mangroves, sea grass, corals, etc. as an immediate and continuous activity.",""],[1,"151","1","Carbon Emission Reduction Commitment","Reduce carbon emission in line with commitments to the Kyoto Protocol.",""],[1,"151","2","Coastal and Marine Ecosystem Protection and Restoration Programme","Implement programmes for the protection and restoration of key coastal and marine ecosystems which serve as carbon sinks.",""],[1,"154","4","Climate Change Vulnerability Assessment for Habitats and Species","Make an assessment of habitats and species for climate change vulnerabilities.",""],[1,"154","6","Ecosystem and Species Restoration and Conservation","Restore severely degraded ecosystems, key habitats and conserve important species.",""],[1,"154","7","Mangrove Sustainable Utilization and Conservation Policy","Implement a new policy or update existing policy for sustainable utilization and conservation of mangroves.",""],[1,"154","8","Marine Protected Area Network Expansion","Increase MPA network by identification and declaration of new MPAs within its EEZ and upgrading existing MPAs.",""],[1,"154","9","Marine Protected Area Coverage Expansion","Increase MPA coverage by 1000 km2.",""],[1,"154","10","Management Plans for Marine Protected Areas","Prepare management plans to manage new MPAs as well as existing MPAs.",""],[1,"154","11","Marine Protected Area Protection Upgrade","Strengthen resilience of MPAs by upgrading their present protection level.",""],[1,"154","12","Coastal Zoning-Based Strategic Management Frameworks and Plans","Prepare, adapt and implement strategic management frameworks and plans with multi stakeholder participation and based on coastal zoning.",""],[1,"154","13","Marine Ecosystem Strategic Management Frameworks","Prepare and implement strategic management frameworks for marine ecosystems.",""],[1,"155","13","Habitat Restoration and Species Conservation Action","Take immediate action to restore impacted habitats and conserve important species.",""],[1,"155","15","Enhanced Ecosystem Protection with Stakeholder Participation","Provide enhanced protection for impacted ecosystems with key stakeholder participation",""]],"106":[[1,"153","3","Marine Environmental Baseline Information Network (MEBIN)","there is, however, considerable progress underway to develop a Marine Environmental Baseline Information Network (MEBIN) initiated by the Petroleum Resources Development Secretariat.","Petroleum Resources Development Secretariat"],[1,"154","5","Ecosystem Monitoring and Scientific Research Programme","Closely monitor key ecosystems and identify the exact causative factors for less resilient and fragile ecosystems through scientific research.",""],[1,"154","16","Shark Data Collection Mechanisms","Introduce data collection mechanisms for the management and conservation of sharks.",""],[1,"154","17","State-of-the-Art Marine Research Institute","Establish a state of the art marine institute for research and innovations which can offer postgraduate qualifications (which could be named as the Sri Lanka Institute of Marine Science, SLIMS) with improved infrastructure and human resources to conduct marine research and to develop as a \"centre of excellence in marine research\" which would serve as an umbrella organization coordinating and facilitating marine research developing technologies.",""],[1,"154","18","Marine Environmental Baseline Database","Establish and maintain a marine environmental baseline database.",""],[1,"155","1","Marine Research and Development Funding Support","Ensure sufficient and continuous funding for marine research and development from the state sector.",""],[1,"155","2","Marine Sector Research and Development Priority Setting","Identify research and development priorities in the marine sector through relevant agencies.",""],[1,"155","3","Research Proposal Submission Support","Encourage submission of appropriate research proposals to national and international donors.",""],[1,"155","4","Cross-Country Research Partnership Expansion","Increase the number of cross country research partnerships and MoUs.",""],[1,"155","5","Technology and Knowledge Transfer Strategy","Develop strategies for quick transfer of novel technologies and new knowledge among national institutes.",""],[1,"155","7","Marine Science Curriculum Development","Develop school curricula to improve knowledge and right attitudes on marine ecosystem services.",""],[1,"155","8","Training Institution Infrastructure Improvement for Marine Ecosystem Skills","Improve the infrastructure in training institutions to enhance marine ecosystem-related knowledge and skills.",""],[1,"155","9","Ocean Resource Manager Training and Postgraduate Programme","Conduct training and postgraduate programmes for ocean resource managers.",""],[1,"155","14","Monitoring and Assessment of Vulnerable Marine Ecosystems","Conduct timely monitoring and assessment of vulnerable marine ecosystems.",""],[1,"158","12","Ocean Exploration, Research and Development Investment","if the country is to benefit from the blue economy, it is first necessary to invest in ocean exploration, research and development.",""],[1,"158","12","Marine Technology Transfer and Scientific Research Strengthening","Increased scientific knowledge and research and transfer marine technology are essential for improving ocean health and enhancing the contribution of the ocean to the development of countries, in particular small island developing states.",""]],"107":[[1,"44","2","Ocean-Based Ecotourism Promotion and Regulatory Framework","Ocean based ecotourism to be further promoted after setting up all the regulatory mechanisms.",""],[1,"91","5","Eco-Tourism and Special Tourism Promotion","Promote eco-tourism and other special forms of tourism to attract high caliber tourists.",""],[1,"156","11","Ocean-Based Tourism Promotion and Regulation Framework","Ocean-based tourism such as diving (in ship wrecks in particular), snorkeling, and other water sports should be promoted.",""],[1,"156","11","Tour Operator and Tour Guide Regulation and Training","In this regard, regulations need to be developed and guidelines developed for tour operators and tour guides who need to be well trained.",""],[1,"158","2","Ocean-Based Eco-Tourism and Responsible Tourism Development","Develop ocean-based eco-tourism and responsible tourism.",""],[1,"158","3","Shark- and Ray-Based Ecotourism Promotion","Promote ecotourism based on sharks and rays as an alternative to fishing which will provide more revenue to the local economy than fishing.",""],[1,"158","9","Eco-Tourism Use of Traditional Fishing Crafts and Methods","Use traditional fishing crafts and fishing methods for eco-tourism (particularly in lagoon fisheries).",""],[1,"159","2","Regulatory Framework for Ocean-Based Ecotourism","Ocean based ecotourism should be further promoted after setting up all the regulatory mechanisms including marine mammal observations, snorkelling, diving, sport fishing and other water sports.",""]],"108":[[1,"156","3","Comprehensive Fishery Resource Survey within the EEZ","there is a need to conduct a comprehensive resource survey within EEZ within a few years with the support from a nation with well-developed technology.",""],[1,"156","3","Acceleration of NARA Fish Catch Data and Resource Survey Initiatives","Although, there are some initiatives by NARA, this process has to be accelerated with international and national level cooperation and collaboration.",""],[1,"156","12","Ban on Illegal Fishing Gear Imports and Use","Ban all forms of illegal fishing gear, including a total ban of imports of illegal fishing gear and material.",""],[1,"156","13","Environment-Friendly Fishing Gear Promotion and Incentive Scheme","Promote more environment-friendly fishing gear and provide incentives for fishers who use environment- friendly fishing gear.",""],[1,"157","9","Resource Sustainability Survey","Conduct a resource survey to find out sustainable levels.",""],[1,"157","10","Standardized Fish Catch Data Collection Mechanism","Develop a standardized mechanism to collect actual fish catch data by making it compulsory for each fisher boat to provide fish catch data to obtain a license for the following year.",""],[1,"157","11","Scientific Studies on Sustainable Fishing Gear and Methods","Carry out scientific studies to identify most environmental promising and best fishing gear /methods for different types of fisheries.",""],[1,"157","12","Incentives and Restrictions for Sustainable Fishing Gear","Promote such gear by giving incentives (such as reduced fishing license fee) and discourage other fishing methods and ban the least environmental friendly fishing gear.",""],[1,"157","13","Illegal Fishing Legal Framework and Enforcement","Provide for a stringent legal framework and enforcement for illegal fishing methods such as poison, dynamite, monofilament nets and bottom trawling.",""],[1,"158","10","Environment-Friendly Fishing Awareness and Training Programme","Create awareness and conduct training for fishing to be more environment-friendly and minimize post-harvest losses.",""]],"109":[[1,"195","24","Rural School Domestic Water Supply Improvement","Domestic water usage in rural schools needs to be enhanced immediately.",""],[1,"196","4","School Water Supply Schemes","Implement proper water supply schemes in schools to avoid serious hygiene problems from spreading among school children.",""]],"110":[[1,"208","1","Early-Life Environmental Education and Awareness Strengthening","education and awareness needs to be strengthened from a young age order to provide better living conditions for future generations.",""],[1,"209","2","Values and Ethics Measures","measures will be proposed to address two critical issues: (1) values and ethics; and (2) Sri Lankan citizenship and identity.",""],[1,"209","2","Sri Lankan Citizenship and Identity Measures","measures will be proposed to address two critical issues: (1) values and ethics; and (2) Sri Lankan citizenship and identity.",""],[1,"211","2","Religious Values Mobilization for Civic Ethics","It is necessary to identify a set of moral and ethical values shared and sharable by all religions, and mobilize religious recourses in order to establish these values in people.",""],[1,"211","5","Religious Teaching Reinterpretation Initiative","Teaching/reinterpreting the religious teachings and concepts to suit the current social problems and issues: It is necessary that religious teachings which are age-old but immensely insightful be interpreted to suit current personal and social issues.",""],[1,"211","7","Religious-Based Environmental and Civic Behaviour Programmes","Religious programmes conducted by religious organizations, monasteries, kovils, churches, and mosques may be made to serve as means to inculcate good attitudes and behaviour in participants on 'mundane' matters such as how not to soil one's surroundings, how to dispose ones garbage properly, how to not produce too much garbage by adopting more environmentally friendly ways of living with 'mindful consumption', how to show compassion to others, how to be humane before being religious and the like.",""],[1,"211","8","Public Behaviour Norms and Compliance Measures","It is necessary to identify a set of 'do's and 'don'ts in public behaviour and attribute to those things a law-like character and take measures by the government to make sure that people adhere to such norms and practices.",""],[1,"216","3","Religious Values and Citizenship Education Initiative","A set of moral and ethical values shared and sharable by all religions, and mobilization of religious recourses in order to ingrain these values in the people will be established.",""]],"111":[[1,"33","3","Unpaid Care and Domestic Work Formalization Policy","Recognize and value unpaid care and domestic work by adopting policies to formalize, diversify and develop household care across state, private and public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"33","3","Shared Responsibility Curriculum Mainstreaming","programmes on shared responsibility between men and women within the household should be mainstreamed into educational curriculum.",""],[1,"75","8","Enhancement of Social Security Benefits and Day-Care Centers","Enhancing social security benefits such as maternity and sick leave and establishment of suitable day-care centers, will also help in increasing female labour force participation",""],[1,"75","9","Paternity Leave Regulatory Framework","Encourage establishment of regulatory frameworks for paternity leave, so that men also have more chances of sharing household responsibilities and freeing women to enter the labour force",""]],"112":[[1,"33","7","National Transport Policy on Connectivity and Passenger Safety","Introduce a national transport policy that not only focuses on rural-urban connectivity but also ensures zero tolerance of women's sexual harassment in buses and trains.",""]],"113":[[1,"36","5","Indian Ocean Regional Cooperation Promotion","Promote Indian Ocean based regional cooperation as a priority in Sri Lanka Foreign Policy.",""],[1,"36","8","Climate Change Mitigation Foreign Policy Advocacy","Advocate for climate change mitigation and adherence to the Paris Climate Accord commitments as a cornerstone of foreign policy.",""],[1,"44","2","Marine Science and Technology Transfer Initiative","Increased scientific knowledge and transfer marine technology, is essential to improve ocean health and to enhance the contribution of the ocean for development.",""],[1,"44","2","Marine Baseline Studies and Resource Survey Programme","Baseline studies, resource surveys, and exploration of non-living resources are essential.",""]],"114":[[1,"37","5","Local Microeconomic Interventions for Inclusive Growth","Ensure macroeconomic adjustments favour micro economic interventions at local level for inclusive growth, with gender and youth specific components.",""],[1,"37","6","Multi-level Production Sector Partnership and Value Chain Mobilization","Mobilize partnerships among individuals and enterprise of production sectors from divisional through provincial to national levels, improving supply/value chains of growth potential products and services benefiting the poor with supply side inputs on demand driven processes.",""],[1,"37","7","Mainstream Poverty Reduction Across Public, Private, and People’s Sector Programs","Ensure public, private and peoples sector agencies responding to the national call to declare the space and modalities for poverty reduction in their programs to contribute towards the",""],[1,"38","5","Special Measures for Sustainable Livelihoods of Vulnerable Groups","Adopt special measures to empower the poorest and most vulnerable members of society to find sustainable livelihoods (Note the 2018 budget is already doing this), including female headed households affected by conflict and persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"69","5","Concessionary Micro-Credit Access and MSME Growth Programmes","Improve access to micro-credit on concessionary terms, and to launch programmes aimed at encouraging the growth of MSMEs.",""],[1,"69","6","Financial Literacy Improvement for Rural and Poor Populations","Improve the financial literacy of rural/poor populations",""],[1,"75","10","Financial Inclusion and SME Support Programme","Improve access to financial services for the poor, create self- employment opportunities, and support for SMES",""],[1,"92","4","Rural, Estate, and Urban Productive Employment Promotion","Increase productive employment in rural, estate and urban areas by promoting agricultural production, agro-based industries and manufacturing, particularly in strategically important areas.",""],[1,"99","5","Decent Job Creation and Labour Productivity Enhancement","Promotion of decent job creation, improving labour productivity through skills development, developing a pension scheme for all workers by amalgamating existing schemes, enhancing skills of migrant workers and exploring new markets",""],[1,"100","7","SME Formalization Initiative","Integrating SMEs into the formal sector",""]],"115":[[1,"38","3","Inclusive and Accountable Community Institutions for Service Convergence","Promote inclusive and accountable community institutions practicing principles of good governance and ethics .as platforms for convergence of services from various programs directly focusing on the poor and the disadvantaged to overcome poverty and inequality.",""],[1,"75","4","Community Institutional Strengthening for Inclusive and Accountable Governance","Strengthen inclusive and accountable institutions in communities in order to make full use of new technology and innovations",""],[1,"76","9","Stakeholder-Consulted Reform Initiatives","Reform initiatives must involve appropriate stakeholder consultations and address concerns of those population groups or employment groups likely to be adversely impacted, at least in the short-term",""]],"116":[[1,"39","7","Gender Equality Enhancement in Government Services","Implement immediate efforts to enhance gender equality in all Government services, particularly at the highest levels.",""]],"117":[[1,"42","4","Inclusive Green Growth and Equity Safeguards","Specific policies and efforts are needed to ensure that green growth is inclusive and that environmental sustainability is not achieved at the expense of greater equity and poverty alleviation.",""],[1,"42","4","Immediate Action on Health, Waste, Agriculture, and Transport","The key areas that need immediate addressing are health, solid waste management, agriculture and transport.",""],[1,"78","9","Public Awareness Campaigns and Externality Pricing Schemes","Conduct public awareness campaigns and implement proper pricing schemes for externalities (such as pollution, vehicle, and garbage taxes) to internalize the costs of negative externalities",""],[1,"90","3","Sustainable Consumption and Production Policy Support Programme","The EU funded Switch Asia project on Sustainable Consumption and Production policy support program, the only pilot project in South Asia is supporting the country to develop a major policy on Sustainable consumption and Production (SCP) which contribute to SDG goal No 12.",""],[1,"91","2","Environmental Education and Sustainable Consumption Curriculum Integration","Introduce environmental education and sustainable consumption and production as well as 3Rpractices from grade 1 up to university levels.",""],[1,"91","4","Sustainable Consumption and Production Policy","Introduce the Sustainable Consumption and Production Policy and supporting instruments and tools.",""],[1,"91","6","Organic Certification and Labeling Enforcement","Introduce and enforce labels, organic certification and similar market based tools to create responsible community groups.",""],[1,"91","7","Community-Based Sustainability Groups Empowerment Initiative","Establish and empower community based sustainability groups/societies to actively engage in inclusive green growth.",""]],"118":[[1,"79","1","Western Megapolis Development Project","The Western Megapolis Development Project is the flagship development initiative of the present government.",""]],"119":[[1,"81","4","Financial Oversight Strengthening","Strengthen financial oversight at all levels of administration, including at the legislature",""],[1,"81","5","Auditor General's Department Integrity and Independence Reform","Ensure integrity and independence of the Auditor General's Department",""],[1,"81","6","Transparency and Accountability Legislation Enforcement","Enact and enforce necessary legislation to promote transparency and accountability such as the Right to Information, Audit Act, declaration of assets, etc.",""],[1,"81","7","Government Procurement Procedure Strengthening","Strengthen procedures and strictly follow guidelines on government procurement",""],[1,"81","8","Rule of Law Enforcement for Corruption and Fraud Charges","Apply rule of law on charges of corruption and fraud",""],[1,"81","9","Strengthen Anti-Corruption and Fraud Investigation Bodies","Strengthen independence of established agencies and bodies tasked with investigating and tackling corruption and fraud",""],[1,"96","7","Independent Commissions and Institutional Accountability Strengthening","Strengthen democratic and accountable governance by ensuring independent Commissions to monitor government action, actions of non-state actors, while ensuring the independence of the judiciary and law enforcement agencies, including the AG's office and public administration.",""],[1,"96","7","Anti-Corruption Investigation and Prosecution Support","Corruption that has undermined the proper functioning of many institutions and reinforced inequities in society can be stamped out by providing adequate resources to relevant institutions to carry out independent, professional investigation and prosecution.",""],[1,"97","1","Ban on Public Office for Corruption Offenders","those who have been found guilty of corrupt practices should be barred from holding or seeking public office.",""],[1,"99","8","Tax Coverage, Compliance, and Administration Reform","Reforms relating to coverage, compliance and tax administration to increase government",""],[1,"100","2","Government Expenditure Rationalization and Anti-Corruption Reform","Rationalizing government expenditure through reduction of waste and elimination of corruption",""]],"120":[[1,"86","1","Polluter Pays Principle Adoption","Adopt Polluter Pay Principle.",""],[1,"86","4","Marine Environment Protection Law Enforcement","Strictly enforce the legislation on Marine Environment Protection Authority in terms of pollution of marine water bodies.",""],[1,"86","5","Natural Resource Damage Assessment and Liability Framework","Conduct full cost accounting of the damages, Natural Resource Damage Assessments and compulsory liability.",""],[1,"86","6","Zero Liquid Discharge Systems Incentive Programme","Encourage and incentivize the zero liquid discharge systems in industries.",""],[1,"88","6","Clean Environment Incentives, Penalties, and Standards","Encourage a clean environment by all - using incentives, penalties and standards.",""],[1,"89","9","Environmental Law Enforcement for Emitting Sites","Strictly enforce environmental laws to all emitting sites.",""],[1,"89","11","Low-Interest Credit for Pollution-Free Enterprise Investment","Facilitating enterprises with low interest/no interest credit to introduce pollution free plants and equipment.",""],[1,"91","3","Environmental Regulation Enforcement","Enforcement of environmental regulation without favour or bias where needed.",""]],"121":[[1,"88","12","Research Facilities Support for National Priority Areas","Provide facilities to research institutions for new research in nationally important areas.",""],[1,"89","14","Research Facilities for Renewable Energy Innovation","Provide facilities to research institute/universities for conducting research on bio fuels/hydrogen energy and other renewable energy sources",""]],"122":[[1,"102","6","Interdisciplinary CKDu Eradication Approach","The eradication of CKDu by having an effective interdisciplinary approach which takes on the perspectives of all the stakeholders in delivering a sound solution to the recipient, will ensure a safe and secure life for them.",""],[1,"102","6","Promotion of Natural Fertilizers and Biodynamic Farming","Encouraging the replacement of agro chemicals and chemical fertilizers through the use of natural fertilizers and bio dynamic farming practices and will permanently eradicate the future catastrophes such as CKDu.",""],[1,"102","7","Wastewater Discharge Fee System","Introducing wastewater discharge fee system which is delayed for the last fifteen years will ensure all business enterprises to reduce consumption of water as well as reduction of discharged pollution load.",""]],"123":[[1,"103","3","Zonal Land Use Arrangement Implementation","Implementation of zonal arrangements as per the UDA plan for siting industries, setting up housing schemes and condominiums commercial areas is going to be a key requirement in effective land use.",""],[1,"103","3","Green Building Guidelines for Public Sector Buildings","The implementation of green building guidelines for public sector buildings, proposed green public procurement plan and development of eco villages are going to contribute green economic growth with inclusive community engagement.",""],[1,"103","3","Eco Village Development Initiative","The implementation of green building guidelines for public sector buildings, proposed green public procurement plan and development of eco villages are going to contribute green economic growth with inclusive community engagement.",""]],"124":[[1,"108","3","Transfer of Full Land Ownership to Farmers on Temporary Permits","The present government has declared its intention to transfer full land ownership to those who farm on temporary permits.",""],[1,"108","3","Farmer Society and Farmer Company Land Consolidation","As an alternative to the free operation of market forces in relation to land, other means of effective / operational land consolidation have also been tried out.",""],[1,"108","3","Return of Military-Occupied Land to Civilian Owners","Both public and private lands occupied by the military, in the North and East in particular, are being returned to civilian owners.",""]],"125":[[1,"109","7","Seasonal Rainfall Forecasting and Early Warning Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capacity and the ability to better forecast seasonal rainfall and provide early warnings on extreme events.",""],[1,"109","8","Early Weather Warning Institutional Coordination and Real-Time Dissemination System","Develop institutional arrangements to speedily respond to early weather warning signals.",""],[1,"110","5","Real-Time Agricultural Information Service","Fully leverage the recent advances in information technology and increased mobile telephone penetration to provide real time weather, pest and disease, as well as market data to farmers and village level officials.",""]],"126":[[1,"109","9","Drought-Tolerant Crop Variety Development and Dissemination","Drought tolerant crop varieties and cropping patterns which consume less water must be developed and made available to farmers.",""],[1,"109","9","Public and Private Agricultural R&D Investment Expansion","Sustained high investments in R&D by the public sector as well as the private sector are required to achieve this together with effective agricultural extension.",""],[1,"109","9","Agricultural Investment Incentive Reform","Appropriate changes in the investment incentive structure must be considered.",""]],"127":[[1,"117","8","Quality Assurance System for Private Education Institutes","Further, introduce a system for quality assurance in private education institutes.",""],[1,"118","5","Education Governance Restructuring","Restructure the overall governance structure in the system of education.",""],[1,"118","6","Devolution of Decision-Making Powers to Implementation Levels","Devolve decision-making powers and authorities to implementation levels.",""],[1,"118","7","Evidence-Based Policy and Planning Culture","Establish an evidence-based policy and planning culture in the system.",""],[1,"118","8","Policy Research and Development Promotion","Promote research and development practices for policymaking.",""],[1,"118","9","Systematic Accountability Framework","Introduce systematic accountability framework.",""],[1,"120","15","Education Sub-Sector Linkage Mechanism","Establish linkages between the sub-sectors (school education, technical and vocational education, tertiary and higher education).",""]],"128":[[1,"130","3","Stakeholder Consultation for Renewable Energy Projects","Therefore, it is critical that stakeholder communities are informed through consultations regarding projects, to avoid conflict and opposition from those that might be adversely impacted.",""],[1,"133","5","Renewable Energy Investment Facilitation","Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority (SLSEA), which allocates renewable energy resources, acts as a facilitator for investment in the renewable subsector, especially in streamlining the authorization processes of various government Institutions.",""],[1,"133","5","Energy Sector Investment Facilitation Institutions","The Board of Investment, Petroleum Resources Development Secretariat (PRDS) and the recently established Public Private Partnership Unit of the Finance Ministry are the other key institutions that facilitate investment in the energy sector.","Finance Ministry"],[1,"134","2","Amend Power Plant Procurement Guidelines","Hence if private sector participation is expected in power projects, the procurement guidelines need to be amended to suit present context.",""],[1,"134","7","Procurement Guideline Reform to Attract Private Sector Participation","Amend procurement guidelines appropriately to attract private sector participation.",""]],"129":[[1,"140","5","Coal Power Plant Efficiency Upgrade","The CEB has taken steps to reduce emissions through efficient technologies for coal power plants by introducing high efficient super critical technology instead of subcritical technologies.",""],[1,"140","5","Major Hydropower Project Development","The CEB has initiated to develop remaining major hydro power projects although they involve higher capital cost.",""],[1,"141","3","Carbon Crediting Programme with the World Bank","Sri Lanka has initiated a carbon crediting programme with the World Bank where the emission reductions above the NDC targets will be transferred to the Carbon Partnership Facility (CPF) of the World Bank.",""],[1,"141","3","Carbon Revenue Support for Renewable Energy Development","Carbon revenue received in this manner may be used to overcome technical and financial barriers for renewable development.",""],[1,"141","5","Administrative Pricing and Auction-Based Price Setting","various techniques such as administrative pricing including incremental cost analysis, investment analysis, economic evaluation or auctions can be used.",""]],"130":[[1,"151","14","Large-Scale Oil Spill Response Capacity Development","Develop infrastructure, equipment and training to handle large scale oil spills.",""],[1,"151","16","National Oil Spill Contingency Plan Implementation","Strengthen and implement the National Oil Spill Contingency Plan (NOSCOP).",""]],"131":[[1,"151","17","Coastal Construction and Sand Mining Regulation Reform","Develop, strengthen and implement policies and introduce stringent laws and regulations for coastal construction and sand mining.",""]],"132":[[1,"157","3","Post-Harvest Loss Reduction Programme","Create awareness, conduct training and provide technological development to minimize post- harvest losses.",""],[1,"157","5","Fish Postharvest Loss Reduction and Export Quality Improvement","To reduce the postharvest losses, increase fish exportability, and maintain the highest possible standards for fish products which would provide the highest rates for our exports.",""],[1,"157","7","Eco-labeling Scheme Adoption","The adoption of eco-labeling schemes provides additional tools to move towards sustainability of capture fisheries and aquaculture and brings together elements of the market, industry, environmental interests and communities.",""],[1,"158","1","Post-Harvest Loss Reduction and Fisheries Value Addition Initiative","Increase the contribution to GDP by reducing post-harvest losses, targeting more offshore fisheries and value addition to fish products.",""],[1,"158","11","Separate Market for Artisanal Fishers","Establish a separate market for artisanal fishers who use more environmental friendly fishing gear to sell their products at a higher rate (processed, packaged).",""],[1,"159","1","Seafood Export Industry Development with Value Addition","Further, the seafood export industry needs to be developed with value addition.",""]],"133":[[1,"160","1","Public Transport Fare Control and Subsidy Scheme","The government has also sought equitable access to public transport by control of bus and train fares with an index in operation since 2005.",""],[1,"160","1","Student, Public Employee, and Rural Bus Fare Subsidies","Discounted travel for students, state employees, and subsidizing rural bus services is also a long-standing policy which was followed by the Sisu Saeriya, Gami Saeriya and Nisi Saeriya programmes since 2004.",""],[1,"166","1","Mobility Assessment and Inclusive Public Transport Support Scheme","The government through the Ministry of Transport and the Provincial Councils, will before the end of 2019, complete a mobility assessment to ensure that no social groups are disadvantaged due to inadequate access.","Ministry of Transport | Provincial Councils"]],"134":[[1,"167","3","Transport Sector Employment Formalization and Decent Work Measures","The government has to take steps to formalize such employment and to create decent work conditions including automation of unsafe and risky activities to ensure occupational safety for all employees in the transport sector by 2030.",""],[1,"167","3","Transport Sector Domestic Value Addition Strategy","Steps should also be taken by 2020 to develop the transport sector as a driver of the economy pursued through strategies encouraging transport-related domestic value addition instead of being heavily import intensive.",""]],"135":[[1,"168","2","Fuel Pricing Reform","Discontinue differential pricing of fuel between different fuel types to better manage transport pricing, while maintaining affordability.",""]],"136":[[1,"170","3","Independent Transport Project Feasibility and Competitive Procurement Framework","The Department of National Planning will ascertain from 2018 that feasibility studies for transport projects are independently assessed, the cost benefit ensured, the financial implications well understood, its external impacts fully mitigated, local value addition and technology development maximized, and award of contracts are through the calling of competitive bids.","Department of National Planning | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"170","3","Transport Alternative Screening and Proposal Review Mechanism","The proposal for such funding from concept stage will require the identification of other transport alternatives and relevant institutions will also be invited to submit alternate proposals.","Department of National Planning"],[1,"170","3","Private Sector Financing Promotion for Transport","Private sector financing will be encouraged in all transport sectors.",""],[1,"170","3","Transport Project Economic Viability and Public Commitment Review","However each such proposal requiring government approval should be carefully studied for economic viability and long term public commitments and guarantees.",""],[1,"170","3","Transport Planning Circulars, Staffing, and Funding Arrangements","The Ministry of Finance will issue the relevant circulars, assign suitable staff and funding to initiate this from Jan 2018.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"170","4","Statutory Alignment and Powers Amendment Reform","the respective ministries and agencies will make necessary statutory amendments to ensure that the functions assigned under such legislation are aligned to this policy, and the powers required for the same are vested as necessary.",""],[1,"170","5","Transport Enterprise Governance Reform","Steps would be taken to improve management of transport enterprises by preventing interference in non-policy matters and in annual assessment of performances of top managers from the end of 2018.",""],[1,"170","5","Annual Legislative Alignment Proposals for Transport Functions","The relevant ministries will also submit to the Ministry of Policy Implementation annual proposals for continuing amendment of legislation, to further align the functions and powers to achieve the wider objectives of the UN sustainable development goals and the remedies set out within this policy.","the Ministry of Policy Implementation"],[1,"170","5","Transport Legislation Amendment and Parliamentary Submission","The ministries handling the function of transport will be required to amend the relevant legislation and present to Parliament before the end of 2018.",""],[1,"170","6","Transport Sector Human Resource Standards and Specialization Requirements","The government is to stipulate the educational and skill requirements for different grades of human resources required for such functions.",""],[1,"170","6","Transport Sector Professional Input and Modern Operations Framework","It will also take into consideration the professional inputs for high end planning and modern operational features.",""],[1,"170","6","Transport Sector Board Specialization Requirements","Requirements for higher management positions including positions on Boards to possess suitable sector specializations will also be introduced.",""],[1,"170","6","Transport Sector Human Resource Development and R&D Budget Allocation","The Government will also assign the transport sector budget for human resource development and research & development initiatives starting from 2020.",""]],"137":[[1,"179","6","Economic Development Zones and Livelihood Attraction Initiative","It is proposed to attract a larger share from the next two generations (2020-2050) of the populations in these areas into the proposed economic development zones by means of more attractive employment opportunities, affordable housing and more beneficial and vibrant living environments.",""],[1,"179","7","Urban Economic Corridor Development Strategy","The major economic development activities are expected to be concentrated into four urban corridors, two metro regions and nine main cities, which have been identified as the most effective locations in conformity with the three principles mentioned elsewhere in this report.",""],[1,"179","7","Port-Led Trade and Investment Promotion","The economic corridors will be sharing the largest contribution to the national economy, mainly by means of value addition to both local commodities as well as import-export based global supply chains, capitalizing upon the three international ports in Colombo, Trincomalee, and Hambanthota, and the small ports in Oluvil and Jaffna.",""],[1,"182","3","Colombo-Trincomalee Corridor Settlement Development","a reasonable share of the future population (approximately 30-35 per cent) in Sri Lanka should be settled within a corridor between Colombo and Trincomalee.",""],[1,"182","8","Development of Nine Strategic Main Cities","nine main cities are proposed at Mannar, Mullaitivu, Vauniya, Puttlam, Polonnaruwa, Nuwara Eliya, Mahiyangana, Wellawaya, and Rathnapura.",""]],"138":[[1,"189","10","Lagoon Freshwater Storage and Seawater Intrusion Control","Isolate major lagoons to store freshwater and curb sea water infusion to lagoon body.",""],[1,"189","11","Revision of the Arumugam River for Jaffna Proposal","Revisit the Arumugam proposal \"River for Jaffna\" and modify it to suit present demands.",""],[1,"189","13","Aquifer Recharge Study","Study suitable areas to recharge aquifers in the rainy season using runoff",""]],"139":[[1,"189","19","National Water Pollution Control Mechanism","Commence a national level mechanism with the support of the Central Environmental Authority to control water pollution.",""],[1,"189","20","Provincial Polluter Identification and Enforcement Action","Identify main polluters in each province and issue stern warnings and take legal action.",""],[1,"190","1","Special Task Force for River and Reservoir Pollution Inspection","Appoint a \"Special Task Force\" with relevant authorities and with the support of Army, to inspect and identify polluters of rivers and reservoirs that discharge solid and liquid waste in specific areas.",""],[1,"190","2","Illegal Reservation Encroachment Enforcement","Take action against illegal encroachment in reservations.",""],[1,"190","3","Periodic Comprehensive Water Quality Testing","Conduct comprehensive water quality testing of water bodies periodically.",""],[1,"190","9","Micro Bund Construction for Soil and Water Conservation","Construct \"micro bunds\" on mountain slops along the contour to control surface erosion and improve water infiltration and absorption into sub soil strata.",""],[1,"190","10","Regulatory Enforcement Strengthening","Effective enforcement of regulations by all relevant regulatory institutions.",""],[1,"190","11","Environmental Regulation Review and Update","Review and update existing regulations to effectively control damage to the environment.",""],[1,"190","12","Island-wide Basin Management Awareness Programme","Launch an island wide awareness programme with the support of the respective local authorities to educate best practices in basin management, including excavation control, home garden landscaping, mini agriculture construction of roads etc.",""],[1,"190","13","Reforestation with Environmental Safeguards","Commence reforestation where possible with proper drainage, controlled use of pesticides, weedicides etc.",""],[1,"193","4","Major River Water Quality Monitoring System","Water quality measurement and monitoring should be introduced to all major rivers.",""]],"140":[[1,"194","10","Potable Water Supply Efficiency and Tariff Collection Improvement","Improve technical efficiency of potable water supply and improve billing and collection of tariffs.",""],[1,"194","17","Manufacturer Prequalification Based on Product Standards and End-User Performance","Prequalification of manufacturer's with country origin (Factory location) based on product standards and end user performance.",""],[1,"194","18","Long-Term Partnership Development for Goods and Services Providers","Develop long term partnership for goods and services providers such as local manufacturers, fabricators, agents (SIERA for telecom service and Lanka Transformer for CEB),",""],[1,"194","19","Prequalified Manufacturer Procurement Requirement","Insist on prequalified manufacturer's with factory location for key items in all procurement activities including unsoiled packages funded by EXIM Bank of China, India, and South Korea.",""],[1,"195","11","Water Meter Procurement Quality Control","It is a procurement issue, and endurance test certificate is to be imposed.",""],[1,"195","13","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Remedial Measures","Remedial measures for NRW Reduction.",""],[1,"195","15","Pipe Laying Practice Improvement","Improve pipe laying practice.",""],[1,"195","18","Regulatory Measures for Water Fittings and Equipment","Introduce regulatory measures for water fittings and equipment in order to promote the availability of quality goods.",""]],"141":[[1,"203","13","Urban and Kandyan Home Gardens Promotion","Improve urban gardens and promote Kandyan home gardens to support biodiversity conservation, provide cooler temperatures, and prevent soil erosion.",""],[1,"203","14","Hill Slope Deforestation Prevention and Relocation to Stable Condominium Housing","Prevent deforestation and housing on hill slopes and provide more stable condominium housing in suitable places.",""],[1,"205","3","Urban Forest Patch Creation and Watershed Conservation","Increase green cover by creating forest patches even in urban areas.",""],[1,"205","4","Riverine Deforestation and Reservation Zone Construction Control","Enforce stringent laws preventing deforestation of riverine areas and not permitting construction of hotels in reservation zones.",""],[1,"205","5","Green Construction Standards for Roads, Housing, and Industry","Ensure that building of roads, houses and industries follow more environment friendly green applications/green growth.",""],[1,"207","3","Sustainable Natural Resource Extraction Enforcement","All natural resource extraction must be done in a sustainable manner giving due respect to environmental aspects.",""],[1,"207","3","Illegal Construction Halt and Enforcement","Unauthorized buildings, and illegal construction must be halted.",""],[1,"207","3","Green Pavement and Grassy Area Promotion","Construction of pavements with interlocking stones must be discouraged while promoting grassy areas.",""],[1,"207","10","Forest Cover Expansion for Water Retention and Drought Mitigation","Increased forest cover will enhance water retention in the soil and improve infiltration.",""],[1,"208","1","Enforcement Against Unauthorized Development and Structures","enforcement will reduce unauthorized developments, and unauthorized structures in river banks, reservations, near and around waterways and canals will prevent flooding and landslides considerably.",""],[1,"208","1","Control of Natural Resource Extraction","Controlling and managing natural resource extraction such as sand, soil, gravel and metal will prevent a host of environmental problems including most health hazards.",""]],"142":[[1,"235","5","R&D Tax Incentive Reform","The under-utilized tax incentives that were put in place a few years ago to promote R&D should be re-examined and modified to support the above actions.",""],[1,"235","5","Angel and Venture Financing Promotion","Domestic high net-worth individuals and firms should be encouraged to enter into angel and venture financing.",""],[1,"235","5","Crowdfunding Enabling Legislation","Legislation to permit a company to have more than 50 shareholders would enable the creation of effective crowd-funding platforms similar to Kickstarter and Indiegogo.",""],[1,"235","5","Research and Innovation Hub Development","Plans to make Trace Expert City a space for research and innovation should be reactivated.",""],[1,"235","5","Regional Innovation Facility Expansion","Similar facilities should be promoted/enabled in Jaffna, Matara, Kandy and Kurunegala.",""],[1,"235","5","Innovation Infrastructure Support","Infrastructure assistance in the form of land and utility services must be provided.",""],[1,"235","7","Frameworks for Financiers, Incubators, and Accelerators","Creation of frameworks for the activities of financiers, incubators and accelerators will bound official discretion and contribute to good governance.",""],[1,"236","1","Innovation Reward System Development","This requires mobilization of the best brains in the world to critically assess the status quo and experience on the subject and develop a cutting- edge reward system that includes prizes and similar rewards, in addition to conventional patents.",""],[1,"236","1","Fast-Track Legal Channel for Reward System Disputes","A \"fast track\" legal channel to handle contract disputes and matters related to the reward system is desirable.",""]],"143":[[1,"179","2","Planned Promotion of Inland Tourist Destinations","The inland locations which have high potentials to attract tourists need to be promoted in a planned manner.",""],[1,"207","8","Forest Patch and Workway Tourism Enhancement","With forest patches and work ways, the level of tourist attraction both foreign and local will be high, with increased economic growth.",""]],"144":[[1,"203","12","Hospital Facilities Improvement in Surrounding Districts","Improve hospital facilities in surrounding districts to prevent a large number of people travelling to Kandy for medical treatment.",""],[1,"207","8","Government Health Bill Reduction","The government health bill will be lowered, with a healthier workforce and increased efficiency and output.",""]],"145":[[1,"195","17","Illegal Electricity Tapping Detection Strategy","New strategies are required to identify illegal tapping using billing package, and public participation.",""]],"146":[[1,"203","9","Environment-Friendly Refrigerant Requirement","All air-conditioning and refrigeration systems, especially in hotels and restaurants, must use environment friendly gases.",""]],"147":[[1,"237","2","Experiment Nation Initiative","it will be necessary to establish a supra-ministerial task force supported by a lean management team to implement a focused \"Experiment Nation\" initiative.",""],[1,"237","5","Experiment Nation Initiative Task Force","Establish a supra-ministerial task force supported by a lean management team to implement a focused \"Experiment Nation\" initiative.",""],[1,"237","7","Review and Reform Constraints on the Experiment Nation","Study laws, regulations and procedures that hinder the \"Experiment Nation\" and engage in changing the highest priority constraints.",""],[1,"237","9","Domestic Study Group on Innovation Incentive Reform","Mandate a domestic study group to examine the efficacy of the tax and other government incentives used over the years to promote investment in innovation-intensive activities and to develop recommendations for reform.",""],[1,"237","10","International Legal Expert Panel on Innovation Incentives","Commission an international legal expert panel to study an optimal reward-and-risk environment for innovation and experimentation in Sri Lanka, with special reference to competitor countries.",""],[1,"274","2","Intellectual Property Law Reform for Innovation and Technology","Intellectual property laws must be reviewed and changed in a manner that supports and promotes innovation & technology in Sri Lanka.",""]],"148":[[1,"252","11","Divisional Secretariat Planning and Coordination for Sustainable Production and Conservation","Mobilize the divisional secretariat as the unit of planning and coordination of interventions for sustainable production, consumption and conservation in their area of authority in line with the provincial and national strategy, engaging stakeholders of public, private and peoples sector for development for investment.",""],[1,"252","12","Restructuring Divisional and Provincial Government Development and Administrative Structures","Divisional and provincial government development and administrative structure to be restructured taking up responsibility of coordinating economic and social interventions for effective improvement of the micro economy of their area of authority.",""],[1,"254","3","Divisional Secretariat Planning and Coordination for Development Interventions","The Divisional Secretariats will play a key role in planning and coordination on development interventions, specifically integrating Samurdi safety net interventions and other programs for sustainable management of resources complementing a more holistic approach for poverty alleviation.",""]],"149":[[1,"259","7","Youth Economic Participation and Employment Measures","Introduce pro-active measures to increase youth participation in the economy through full- time employment, (particularly when such efforts increase female participation in the work force and address underlying disparities in work-force participation between communities), to foster reconciliation and durable peace.",""],[1,"259","8","Accelerated Infrastructure Projects with Youth Participation","Conduct accelerated infrastructure projects with special emphasis on multi-cultural youth participation.",""],[1,"266","1","Public and Private Mega Projects for Youth Employment","The high unemployment rate of youth should be mitigated due to the increase in public and private mega projects.",""],[1,"266","1","Megapolis Project","For example, the Megapolis project and Cinnamon Life project, combined with community based initiatives and investment in small and medium enterprises (SMEs).",""],[1,"266","1","Cinnamon Life Project","For example, the Megapolis project and Cinnamon Life project, combined with community based initiatives and investment in small and medium enterprises (SMEs).",""]],"150":[[1,"259","9","Targeted Interventions for War-Affected Communities","Introduce targeted interventions addressing multiple critical issues at once.",""],[1,"259","9","Infrastructure Investment in War-Affected Communities","an acceleration of infrastructure investment in war affected communities",""],[1,"259","9","Integrated Youth Work Force Recruitment","the recruitment of integrated youth work forces to bring members of different communities, who rarely interact in their daily lives, together.",""]],"151":[[1,"259","10","Youth Engagement in Environmental Projects","Engagement of unemployed youth in integrated, multi-cultural environmental projects such as tree planting or coastal climate change mitigation.",""],[1,"259","11","Integrated Youth Skills Training for Environmental Projects","Conduct integrated skills training for youth, linked to real or projected demand in the labour market for Youth-led environmental projects.",""]],"152":[[1,"259","12","Bilingual and English Education Reform","Introduce educational reforms including lessons in both official languages and English.",""],[1,"265","10","Integrated Bilingual Skills Training","Provide integrated skills training for the communities to learn both languages.",""],[1,"265","11","Bilingual and English Education Reform","Introduce educational reforms including lessons in both official languages and English.",""],[1,"274","1","English Language Promotion in Education","Proactive promotion of the English language in the education sector where all youth have the opportunity of learning in English both as a link language and the language of choice in the private sector globally.",""]],"153":[[1,"260","10","Implementation of Language Rights and Bilingual Public Services","Effective implementation of language rights and policies so that government services from policing to health care, to Courts are accessible in both official languages.",""],[1,"265","1","Translator Service for Administrative and Basic Translation Support","the launch of the translator service by the Office of National Unity and Reconciliation focuses on providing translators for any situations varying from administrative assistance, to basic translation services.","Office of National Unity and Reconciliation"],[1,"265","3","Language Barrier Reduction for Environmental Policy Implementation","By bridging the language barriers faced in Sri Lanka, the execution of policies related to the protection of the environment can be implemented in a timely and effective manner.",""],[1,"265","12","Bilingual Public Services and Communications Provision","Ensure that public services and communications are available in both official languages.",""],[1,"265","13","Recruit Tamil Speakers in Government Services","Recruit Tamil speakers in all Government services, including the police, especially where Tamil speakers are a majority.",""],[1,"266","5","Tamil Language Equality and Accessibility Measures","The government has taken important steps to give equal representation to the Tamil language in national life.",""],[1,"266","5","Constitutional Reform to Strengthen Tamil Language Rights","Constitutional reforms are expected to further strengthen Tamil language rights contributing to greater inclusion and commitment to national goals.",""]],"154":[[1,"263","4","Military Land Return and Productive Reuse Initiative","The return of lands remedies issues pertaining to homelessness and poverty.",""],[1,"264","5","Devolution of Land Powers to Provincial Councils","Great authority must be vested in the hands of the Provincial Councils, so that a more context-specific and useful approach could be adopted with regards to the use of land.",""],[1,"264","6","Military Land Restitution in the North and East","Restitution of all land held by the military in the North and East.",""],[1,"266","4","Military Land Restitution and Business Withdrawal","The restitution of lands held by the military to civilians and the withdrawal of the military from business activities, will be close to completion by 2020.",""]],"155":[[1,"272","2","Urban Space and Connectivity Management","The quality of urban spaces, structures, and improved connectivity with and in between urban areas must be managed.",""],[1,"272","2","Affordable Housing Policy Reform","Land and housing policy reforms should ensure space for affordable housing while fostering innovative housing finance to allow better access to everyone.",""],[1,"272","2","Innovative Housing Finance Mechanism","Land and housing policy reforms should ensure space for affordable housing while fostering innovative housing finance to allow better access to everyone.",""]],"156":[[1,"281","4","Targeted Social Welfare Programme Rationalization","Rationalize wasteful expenditure, particularly by ensuring the precise targeting of social welfare programmes for poor households",""],[1,"282","6","Universal Pension Scheme Development","developing a pension scheme for all workers by amalgamating existing schemes, enhancing skills of migrant workers, and exploring new markets",""],[1,"283","12","Social Safety Nets for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","A simultaneous focus on providing adequate safety nets to safeguard the poor and vulnerable will help in ensuring that growth is inclusive, as recognized in Vision 2025.",""],[1,"287","1","Progressive Taxation and Social Investment for Minimum Household Income","Implement measures to reduce income inequality through a twin strategy of progressive taxation and enhanced social investments leading to a guaranteed minimum household income and social security for all.",""],[1,"287","6","Targeted Social Services Quality and Outreach Improvement","Take measures to improve the professional quality and outreach of various targeted social services to empower marginalized and disadvantaged groups such as the poor, disabled, the elderly, mentally ill, etc.",""]],"157":[[1,"266","1","Community-Based Initiatives and SME Investment Support","For example, the Megapolis project and Cinnamon Life project, combined with community based initiatives and investment in small and medium enterprises (SMEs).",""],[1,"281","5","Job Creation and Skills Development for Women and Youth","Create more job opportunities (especially for women and youth), to address inequality concerns and make growth more inclusive, coupled with increased skills development, and for women, cultural acceptance of their work outside the home/community and better child care facilities.",""]],"158":[[1,"282","7","Public Social and Economic Infrastructure Investment","A focus on public social and economic infrastructure projects, while creating space for local and foreign private investors to invest in directly productive and profit-oriented ventures",""],[1,"283","2","Efficient National Transport Network Development","Creating an efficient transport network connecting large and emerging cities, townships, economic centers and rural hubs",""],[1,"290","2","Megapolis and Urban Centre Infrastructure Development","The proposed development of megapolises and other urban centres, and the associated physical infrastructure development, will speed up the structural transformation of the economy.",""]],"159":[[1,"286","5","Zonal Industrial Siting and Mixed-Use Housing Arrangement","Implementation of zonal arrangements as per the UDA plan for siting industries, and setting up housing schemes and condominiums in commercial areas are going to be key requirements for effective land use.",""],[1,"286","5","Green Building Guidelines for Public Sector Buildings","The implementation of green building guidelines for public sector buildings, the proposed green public procurement plan, and the development of eco villages are going to contribute to green economic growth with inclusive community engagement.",""],[1,"286","5","Green Public Procurement Plan","The implementation of green building guidelines for public sector buildings, the proposed green public procurement plan, and the development of eco villages are going to contribute to green economic growth with inclusive community engagement.",""],[1,"286","5","Eco Village Development Initiative","The implementation of green building guidelines for public sector buildings, the proposed green public procurement plan, and the development of eco villages are going to contribute to green economic growth with inclusive community engagement.",""]],"160":[[1,"287","2","Informal Employment and Casualization Reduction Measures","Manage the increasing trend towards casualization of work and the expansion of the informal sector, through appropriate policy and program interventions in order ensure greater income and employment security.",""],[1,"295","2","Transport Employment Formalization and Decent Work Initiative","The GoSL will by 2030 take steps to formalize transport employment and to create decent work conditions.",""]],"161":[[1,"287","7","Subsidiarity and Local Governance Empowerment Measures","Strengthen the subsidiarity principle by empowering lower tiers of government, especially local bodies and take effective measures to facilitate citizen participation in governance and development.",""]],"162":[[1,"294","7","Mobility Assessment and Inclusive Urban Transport Access Improvement","Complete a mobility assessment to fill service gaps by 2030.",""],[1,"294","8","Transport Safety Improvement Investment Allocation","To provide an allocation of 5% of capital investment in the sector for transport safety improvements.",""],[1,"294","9","Transport Infrastructure and Services Environmental Assessment Framework","Assess transport infrastructure and services from 2020 based on: a) use of physical resources, b) number of beneficiaries, c) use of renewable energy d) environmental impacts and e) vehicle-km and fuel consumption.",""],[1,"294","10","Multi-Modal Transport and Logistics Network Development","Improve connections nationally and with the world: Multi-modal transport & logistics networks to be developed by 2018 with strategic plans to (a) develop domestic aviation, (b)",""],[1,"295","1","International Air Travel Improvement","improve international air travel",""],[1,"295","1","Export Facilitation and Port Development","improve export facilitation and port development.",""],[1,"295","2","Domestic Value Addition Strategy for the Transport Sector","Transport sector to be made a driver of the economy pursued through strategies encouraging related domestic value addition.",""],[1,"296","2","High-Priority Highway and Railway Development Projects","The initial planning and implantation of the high priority projects such as highway and railway development, should be realized by 2025, in order to lay the foundation for a future settlement development pattern and to capitalize upon the dividends of the demography and global opportunities.",""]],"163":[[1,"296","3","National Programme for Small Storage Ponds and Mini Water Schemes","Initiate a national wide programme to identify suitable areas for small storage ponds and gravity driven \"Mini Schemes\" with pipe borne water, with the support of Provincial Councils, Water Boards and other authorities.",""],[1,"296","4","Micro Bund Construction for Soil and Water Conservation","Construct \"Micro Bunds\" on mountain slops along the contour to control surface erosion and improve water infiltration and absorption into sub soil strata.",""],[1,"296","6","Small Irrigation Tank Restoration Programme","Commence a programme to restore small irrigation tanks scattered throughout the country.",""],[1,"296","9","Rainwater Harvesting and Rural Water Infrastructure Programme","In the road map toward 2030, the first stretch from 2018 to 2020 would cover events to promote rain water harvesting in CKDu and other possible rural areas (with subsidized financing), rehabilitate minor tanks for drinking and agriculture, and improve recharge aquifers in the Jaffna area.",""],[1,"296","9","Rural Wells and School Sanitation Improvement Programme","Other steps would be to clean, rehabilitate and construct shallow wells for drinking and minor agriculture and to improve sanitation in rural schools and the estate sector, with the assistance of provincial",""],[1,"297","4","Water Supply, Sewerage, and Sanitation Improvement Measures","Its goals would include supplying drinking water to 65 percent of the population, improving the pipe borne network, organizing methods like reverse osmosis (RO) Plants, harvesting rain water, reserving necessary funding, procurement planning, planning for improving sewerage networks in the metropolis, and planning to improve sanitation in the rural and estate sectors.",""],[1,"297","5","Drinking Water Coverage Expansion","In line with the major works planned, drinking water coverage will increase up to 60 percent from the present coverage of 45 percent, with the support of the National Water Supply and Drainage Board (NWSDB) and the local authority.",""],[1,"297","5","Irrigation Water Supply Enhancement for NCP and NWP","The supply of irrigation water to north central province (NCP) and north western province (NWP) will also be enhanced, diverting 900 MCM/year to NCP and 100 MCM/year to NWP.",""],[1,"297","6","Water Storage Rehabilitation and Drinking Water Access Expansion","At the end of the road map in the year 2030, more than 90 percent of the water retention storage in the country will be harnessed by developing and rehabilitating major, medium, and minor tanks, while conveyance losses will be minimized.",""],[1,"297","6","Universal Drinking Water Access Expansion","Access to drinking water for all citizens will be reached - 65 percent from pipe borne water and other organized resources like RO plants, and the balance 35 percent by rain water harvesting.",""],[1,"297","9","Rainwater Harvesting and Alternative Water Supply Support","Rain water harvesting in urban and rural areas will be utilized with subsidized financing, as an alternative to pipe borne supply.",""],[1,"297","9","CKDu-Affected Zone Drinking Water Support","In particular, the CKDu affected zones will be fully supported with quality drinking water by rain water and small tanks, and with RO plants when necessary as a last solution.",""],[1,"298","3","Metropolitan Sewerage Plant Upgrading and Sewerage System Development","Sewerage plants in most of the metropolis will be upgraded and high priority will be given to the renovation or construction of a sewerage system in the new city development plans, as a Government Policy beyond 2030, with proper access to acceptable sanitary facilities for all.",""],[1,"299","5","Inter-Basin Water Transfer Projects","Develop innovative projects through careful research to take excess water from the southwest to the northeast of the country, to overcome the long-term effects of droughts.",""]],"164":[[1,"304","9","Economic Diplomacy Initiative","Vigorously pursue economic diplomacy initiatives to bolster the economy, enhance development activities and attract foreign investors and traders to the country, taking advantage of the positive international focus on Sri Lanka.",""],[1,"305","7","EU Free Trade Relationship Development","we have the vision and initiative to transform the trade relationship with Europe into one of free trade, by the time the GSP+ facility ceases to exist in 2022/2025.",""]]}});